"""
Press Conference Questions
==========================
Post-game press conference question bank for Geeked-Out Basketball franchise mode.

Structure:
  PRESS_CONFERENCE_QUESTIONS — master list of all question dicts, filterable by
  category, subcategory, tier, and trigger conditions at runtime.

Question dict shape:
  {
    "id": str,                        # unique identifier
    "category": str,                  # top-level grouping
    "subcategory": str,               # sub-grouping within category
    "tier": int,                      # 1 = ready (box score derivable), 2 = needs tracking
    "requires_tracking": bool,        # True for all Tier 2 conditions
    "trigger": {
      "condition": str,               # primary condition key for selection logic
      "filters": dict                 # optional additional filters (thresholds, flags, etc.)
    },
    "weight": int,                    # selection weight; higher = more likely selected
    "player_slot": str | None,        # e.g. "high_scorer", "foul_out"; None if no injection
    "text": str,                      # question text shown to user
    "answers": [
      {
        "letter": str,                # A-E (shuffled per question, not archetype-ordered)
        "archetype": str,             # authoritarian | systems_coach | player_maximizer |
                                      # culture_builder | neutral
        "text": str,                  # answer text in coach's voice
        "effect_tags": list[str]      # gameplay effect tags; resolved by backend
      }
    ]
  }

Effect tag library (magnitudes tuned separately in effect_tag_resolver.py):
  prestige_minor_up / prestige_minor_down
  prestige_major_up / prestige_major_down
  team_chemistry_up / team_chemistry_down
  fight_up / fight_down
  discipline_up / discipline_down
  fan_interest_up / fan_interest_down
  player_em_up / player_em_down        (applies to player_slot player)
  player_mo_up / player_mo_down        (applies to player_slot player)
  team_mo_up / team_mo_down
  archetype_consistency_bonus
  red_herring                          (no effect; window dressing only)

Player slot placeholders in text: {player_name} — resolved at session creation.
Questions substitute the player's full display name (first + last when available);
answers use first name only when the question contained {player_name} and the
full name has multiple words (see press_conference_routes + pgpc_player_slot).
Jersey numbers are NOT injected (press convention: name only).

Archetype answer order is deliberately shuffled per question so no letter
is predictably associated with an archetype across questions.
"""

PRESS_CONFERENCE_QUESTIONS = [

    {'id': 'win_generic_01', 'category': 'game_result', 'subcategory': 'win_generic', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'win', 'filters': {'specificity': 'generic'}}, 'weight': 1, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'Coach, what do you think was the key to the win tonight?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "These guys compete for each other. That's what it comes down to every single night.", 'effect_tags': ['fight_up', 'team_chemistry_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': 'We executed the game plan. Nothing more to it than that.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "A lot of things went our way tonight. We'll enjoy this one and get back to work tomorrow.", 'effect_tags': ['red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': 'The system worked tonight. When everyone knows their role and trusts the scheme, good things happen.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'team_chemistry_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': 'Our guys were locked in individually. When each player is focused on maximizing what he does best, the wins take care of themselves.', 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_up', 'fan_interest_up']}]},
    {'id': 'win_generic_02', 'category': 'game_result', 'subcategory': 'win_generic', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'win', 'filters': {'specificity': 'generic'}}, 'weight': 1, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'How satisfied are you with the overall performance tonight?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': 'Satisfied with the result. There are execution details we need to clean up, but the scheme held together when it needed to.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "I'm proud of the individual performances. I saw guys doing things tonight that show real growth.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "It was a win. We have standards in this program and we didn't meet all of them tonight. We'll address that.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "A win is a win. We'll look at the film and figure out what to build on going forward.", 'effect_tags': ['red_herring']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "I'm proud of this group. They gave everything they had and the result reflects that commitment.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up']}]},
    {'id': 'win_generic_03', 'category': 'game_result', 'subcategory': 'win_generic', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'win', 'filters': {'specificity': 'generic'}}, 'weight': 1, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'What does this win mean for the program right now?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "It means we did our job. That's what this program expects. We move on.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': 'It means everything to these kids. This is what we build toward every single day in that gym.', 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fan_interest_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "It's good for our record and our confidence. We'll take it and keep moving.", 'effect_tags': ['red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "It's validation for the individual work these players have been putting in. They're seeing results and that matters.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'fan_interest_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "It means the system is working. We're building something here that gets harder to beat every week.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_up', 'discipline_up']}]},
    {'id': 'win_generic_04', 'category': 'game_result', 'subcategory': 'win_generic', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'win', 'filters': {'specificity': 'generic'}}, 'weight': 1, 'player_slot': None, 'text': "What's the message to the team heading into the next game?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Keep developing. Every game is an opportunity to show what you're capable of. Don't waste it.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "Stay focused. One game at a time. That's always the message.", 'effect_tags': ['red_herring']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': 'Enjoy tonight with each other. Then we come back tomorrow ready to work even harder for the next one.', 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "Same standards. Same expectations. A win doesn't change what we demand of ourselves in this program.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': 'We go back to the film, find where the system broke down, and fix it. The next opponent is already being scouted.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}]},
    {'id': 'loss_generic_01', 'category': 'game_result', 'subcategory': 'loss_generic', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'loss', 'filters': {'specificity': 'generic'}}, 'weight': 1, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'Coach, what happened out there tonight?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "We didn't execute the scheme at the level it requires. That's on us to fix. The answers are on film.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "They played well and we didn't play well enough. It's that simple. We'll move on.", 'effect_tags': ['red_herring']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "We didn't meet the standard. That's unacceptable and we'll address it directly.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "We fell short tonight, but I believe in this group. We'll come together and respond the right way.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': 'We have to look at what each individual needs to do better. Losses like this show us exactly where the development gaps are.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}]},
    {'id': 'loss_generic_02', 'category': 'game_result', 'subcategory': 'loss_generic', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'loss', 'filters': {'specificity': 'generic'}}, 'weight': 1, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'How do you bounce back from a performance like that?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "We lean on each other. That's what a close team does when things go wrong. We don't point fingers — we pull together.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "You get back in the gym. You work harder. There's no secret to it.", 'effect_tags': ['fight_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "We look at each individual's performance and find the specific things that need to change. Then we work on those things.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "We'll watch the film, figure out what went wrong, and be ready for the next one.", 'effect_tags': ['red_herring']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "We go back to the system. The fundamentals don't change after a loss. If anything, we run the scheme more, not less.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'team_chemistry_up']}]},
    {'id': 'loss_generic_03', 'category': 'game_result', 'subcategory': 'loss_generic', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'loss', 'filters': {'specificity': 'generic'}}, 'weight': 1, 'player_slot': None, 'text': "What's your message to the fan base after tonight?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "We didn't play well enough tonight. The fan base deserves better and we know that. We'll deliver.", 'effect_tags': ['fan_interest_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "Stay with us. Every program goes through tough nights. We'll be better.", 'effect_tags': ['fan_interest_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "Trust the process. We're building something here. One result doesn't define the program.", 'effect_tags': ['fan_interest_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': 'These players are working every day to get better. The fan base will see that work pay off.', 'effect_tags': ['fan_interest_up', 'player_em_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': 'We need them. The support in this building means everything to our guys. Keep believing in this program.', 'effect_tags': ['fan_interest_up', 'team_chemistry_up']}]},
    {'id': 'loss_generic_04', 'category': 'game_result', 'subcategory': 'loss_generic', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'loss', 'filters': {'specificity': 'generic'}}, 'weight': 1, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'Do you think this loss reveals something about where this team is right now?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "It reveals exactly where we need to grow individually. That's not a bad thing — it gives us a clear map.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "It reveals that we have more work to do as a unit. But the character in that locker room? That hasn't wavered.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "Every loss tells you something. We'll look at the film and figure out what that is.", 'effect_tags': ['red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "It reveals we're not where we need to be yet. And that's going to change starting tomorrow morning.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "It reveals execution gaps in the system. Those are fixable. We'll fix them.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}]},
    {'id': 'blowout_win_01', 'category': 'game_result', 'subcategory': 'blowout_win', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'win', 'filters': {'min_margin': 20}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'That was a dominant performance tonight. What was working so well?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "Everything we practiced this week. When players execute the game plan at a high level, that's the result.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "The energy was there from the opening tip. When this group locks in together, it's hard to stop them.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': 'We came out ready to play. Everything clicked tonight and we made the most of it.', 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Individual players were operating at their ceiling tonight. That's what it looks like when preparation meets opportunity.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'prestige_minor_up', 'fan_interest_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "The system created advantages at every level — offense, defense, transition. That's what a well-executed scheme looks like.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_up', 'discipline_up', 'fan_interest_up']}]},
    {'id': 'blowout_win_02', 'category': 'game_result', 'subcategory': 'blowout_win', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'win', 'filters': {'min_margin': 20}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'Is there a danger in winning by this kind of margin — complacency setting in?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': 'Not if we go back to the film and find the breakdowns. A blowout can hide flaws just as easily as a close win.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "We'll enjoy it tonight and come back to work tomorrow. This program doesn't take nights off.", 'effect_tags': ['red_herring']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "Complacency has no home in this program. We'll be in the gym tomorrow fixing the things that weren't good enough.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "This group doesn't have that problem. They hold each other accountable. That's who they are.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Each player knows his individual standard doesn't change based on the scoreboard. That's how we're built.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'player_em_up']}]},
    {'id': 'blowout_win_03', 'category': 'game_result', 'subcategory': 'blowout_win', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'win', 'filters': {'min_margin': 20}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': "Performances like this — what do they do for a program's confidence?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "They confirm for each player what he's capable of when he commits to the work. That's real confidence — earned confidence.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'prestige_minor_up', 'fan_interest_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': 'Confidence is earned in practice. Tonight just showed what that work looks like in a game.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "Nights like this build something in a locker room that you can't manufacture. It's shared belief and it's contagious.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "They're good for the record and good for morale. We'll take them when they come.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "They validate the system. When players trust the scheme completely, this is what's possible. That's a powerful thing to demonstrate.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_up', 'discipline_up', 'fan_interest_up']}]},
    {'id': 'blowout_win_04', 'category': 'game_result', 'subcategory': 'blowout_win', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'win', 'filters': {'min_margin': 20}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'Did you consider resting your starters once the game was in hand?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': 'Absolutely. These guys work hard and when we have the chance to get them some rest and let others step up, we take it.', 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': 'We managed minutes where we could. Player health is always on our mind.', 'effect_tags': ['red_herring']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': 'We play until the final buzzer at our standard. Every minute on that floor is an opportunity to do things right.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': 'We made substitutions according to plan. Every player who entered the game was executing a specific role.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'player_em_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Yes. And the guys who came in took full advantage. That's exactly what you want from your depth.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'team_chemistry_up']}]},
    {'id': 'blowout_loss_01', 'category': 'game_result', 'subcategory': 'blowout_loss', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'loss', 'filters': {'min_margin': 20}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'Coach, that was a tough night. What went wrong?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': 'Everything. And I mean that. We were not competitive tonight in any phase of the game. That is not acceptable.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': 'We broke down schematically in ways that compounded throughout the game. Every phase fed the next. We have to get back to the fundamentals of what we run.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': 'We lost our identity out there. We stopped playing for each other and it snowballed. We have to find our way back to who we are.', 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_down', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': 'They were the better team tonight. We have to look honestly at what happened and fix it.', 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_down', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Individual performances were well below what these players are capable of. We'll look at each player specifically and identify what needs to change.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_down', 'discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}]},
    {'id': 'blowout_loss_02', 'category': 'game_result', 'subcategory': 'blowout_loss', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'loss', 'filters': {'min_margin': 20}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'Is there any concern about how a loss like this affects the locker room?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "Any loss stings. We'll deal with it internally and come back ready to compete.", 'effect_tags': ['red_herring']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "This locker room doesn't get to feel sorry for itself. We address it, we fix it, we move forward. That's how this program works.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "I'm more concerned about what each player takes from this individually. That's where the real work happens — in how you respond personally.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "The locker room responds to clarity. We give them a clear picture of what went wrong and a clear plan to fix it. That's how you prevent a spiral.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'team_chemistry_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "Honestly, this is where you find out what a team is made of. I've seen this group respond before. I expect them to respond again.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up', 'player_em_up']}]},
    {'id': 'blowout_loss_03', 'category': 'game_result', 'subcategory': 'blowout_loss', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'loss', 'filters': {'min_margin': 20}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': "What responsibility do you as the head coach take for tonight's performance?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "Full responsibility. When this team doesn't perform, it starts with me and the culture we create every day in practice.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fan_interest_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "I take responsibility for putting each player in position to succeed. Tonight I didn't do that well enough for everyone.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'fan_interest_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "The coaching staff always shares in the result. We'll look at what we could have done differently.", 'effect_tags': ['red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "I take responsibility for the preparation and the scheme. If we're getting beat that badly, there's a preparation failure somewhere and that's on me.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fan_interest_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "All of it. The standard in this program comes from me and tonight we didn't meet it. That starts and ends with the head coach.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fan_interest_up', 'fight_up']}]},
    {'id': 'blowout_loss_04', 'category': 'game_result', 'subcategory': 'blowout_loss', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'loss', 'filters': {'min_margin': 20}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'Some coaches use a loss like this as a turning point. Do you see it that way?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "Every result is data. A loss this significant tells you exactly where the system is breaking down. In that sense — yes, it's useful.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "Turning points are made in practice, not press conferences. We'll see what this team is made of starting tomorrow morning.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "We'd like it to be. That's up to the players to decide. Coaches can't manufacture that for a team.", 'effect_tags': ['red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': 'I do. Adversity reveals character and it accelerates development. The players who respond well to this will be different players for it.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "It can be. But only if this group decides together that it will be. I believe they will. That's the kind of team we're building.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up', 'player_em_up']}]},
    {'id': 'close_win_01', 'category': 'game_result', 'subcategory': 'close_win', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'win', 'filters': {'max_margin': 3}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'It came down to the wire. What does a win like this do for a team?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "It proves the system works under pressure. That's actually more valuable than a blowout win — we found out the scheme holds in tight situations.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up', 'team_mo_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "A win is a win. Two points, twenty points — it counts the same. We'll take it and move on.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'team_mo_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': 'It shows these players they can compete when it matters most. Winning close games is a skill and they proved they have it.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'prestige_minor_up', 'team_mo_up']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': 'Wins like this build bonds. When you survive something together, it brings you closer. This team needed this.', 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up', 'team_mo_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': 'It gives you confidence. Knowing you can win close games is important for any team.', 'effect_tags': ['team_mo_up', 'red_herring']}]},
    {'id': 'close_win_02', 'category': 'game_result', 'subcategory': 'close_win', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'win', 'filters': {'max_margin': 3}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'There were a few moments tonight where it could have gone either way. What kept your team in it?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': 'The trust in that locker room. When things got tight, nobody panicked because they trust each other completely.', 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "We stayed composed. That's all you can ask for in a close game.", 'effect_tags': ['red_herring']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "Discipline. We didn't panic, we didn't abandon the game plan. We did what we practice.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Individual players stepped up in big moments. That's a reflection of the individual preparation we invest in every week.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'team_mo_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "The system gave us structure when the game got chaotic. Teams without a system tend to fall apart in close games. We didn't.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'team_mo_up']}]},
    {'id': 'close_win_03', 'category': 'game_result', 'subcategory': 'close_win', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'win', 'filters': {'max_margin': 3}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': "Close games like this — are they good for your team's development or do you prefer a more comfortable margin?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "I prefer to dominate. But there's value in being tested. Tonight tested us and we passed. Barely — but we passed.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "These are the games that develop players. There's no better education than having to make real decisions in real pressure moments.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': 'Every win helps. Comfortable ones build confidence, close ones build toughness. You need both.', 'effect_tags': ['red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': 'I love them. This is where you find out what your team is really about. And tonight we found out some good things.', 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up', 'player_em_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "Close games are a systems test. They reveal every crack in the scheme. I'd rather find those cracks in a win than a loss.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}]},
    {'id': 'close_win_04', 'category': 'game_result', 'subcategory': 'close_win', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'win', 'filters': {'max_margin': 3}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': "What's the feeling on the bench when a game gets that close at the end?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "Focused. You're tracking every possession against what the scheme calls for. There's no time to feel anything — you're problem-solving in real time.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "You're thinking about which players are in the best position to make the next play. Matchups, individual confidence, who's been sharp. It's constant evaluation.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': 'Tense. Same as for everyone watching, I imagine. You just try to stay calm and make good decisions.', 'effect_tags': ['red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "You're drawing energy from your players. Watching them compete for each other at that level — it's something special.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "The same as always. Calm. That's what I demand of myself and what I model for my staff and players.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}]},
    {'id': 'close_loss_01', 'category': 'game_result', 'subcategory': 'close_loss', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'loss', 'filters': {'max_margin': 3}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'A heartbreaker tonight. How do you process a loss that close?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "You don't process it — you fix it. Find the two or three possessions that were the difference and make sure they never happen again.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "It hurts. But we were right there. That tells me we're capable. We need to find a way to close it out next time.", 'effect_tags': ['team_mo_down', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "We feel it together. That's important. You can't skip the disappointment — you have to go through it as a team. Then you come out the other side stronger.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up', 'team_mo_down']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "Analytically. We lost by two or three possessions. Those possessions have names — they're plays we either executed or didn't. We'll find them.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'team_mo_down']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "I look at the individual moments where we needed someone to step up and either did or didn't. That's where this game was decided.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'team_mo_down']}]},
    {'id': 'close_loss_02', 'category': 'game_result', 'subcategory': 'close_loss', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'loss', 'filters': {'max_margin': 3}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'Your team was right there at the end. Is there a silver lining in a performance like that?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "The silver lining is who we showed we are. This team competed for forty minutes and didn't quit. That matters more than the final score.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up', 'player_em_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "Silver linings are for teams without standards. We lost. We'll fix it.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': 'The silver lining is that the system worked. We were competitive because of the scheme. Now we refine the execution.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Individual players showed they can compete at this level in pressure moments. That's real data about what this roster is capable of.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "We were competitive, and that's something to build on. It's a loss, but not the kind that should shake this team.", 'effect_tags': ['red_herring']}]},
    {'id': 'close_loss_03', 'category': 'game_result', 'subcategory': 'close_loss', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'loss', 'filters': {'max_margin': 3}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'What did you see in the final minutes that you wish had gone differently?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "A few possessions we'd like to have back. That's the nature of close games. You can't dwell on them.", 'effect_tags': ['red_herring']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "I wanted to see certain players trust their individual preparation when the moment came. Some did. Some didn't. We'll have that conversation privately.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "Decision-making. In close games, every decision is magnified. We made some that we can't afford to make in crunch time.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': 'I wanted to see more trust in each other. When it gets tight, you have to play for the guy next to you. We lost that for a few possessions and it cost us.', 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_down', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "Two specific sequences where we abandoned the scheme under pressure. That's a solvable problem. We'll solve it.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'team_mo_down']}]},
    {'id': 'close_loss_04', 'category': 'game_result', 'subcategory': 'close_loss', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'loss', 'filters': {'max_margin': 3}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'Does a close loss like this tell you anything about where this program stands competitively?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "It tells me we're schematically competitive with good teams. The gap isn't the system — it's the execution details. Those are correctable.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "It tells me we're close. And close isn't good enough. We'll close the gap.", 'effect_tags': ['fight_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': 'It tells me we belong. Now we need to start finishing.', 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': 'It tells me this roster has the talent to compete at this level. Now we have to develop the mental toughness to match.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'prestige_minor_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "It tells me this team has the character to compete in big moments. That's not a small thing. We'll build on it.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}]},
    {'id': 'overtime_win_01', 'category': 'game_result', 'subcategory': 'overtime_win', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'win', 'filters': {'overtime': True}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'You had to go to overtime to get this one. What does winning it say about your team?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "It says we're tough enough to handle adversity. We didn't get it done in regulation — we got it done when it mattered.", 'effect_tags': ['fight_up', 'discipline_up', 'team_mo_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "It says our players have the mental fortitude to compete in overtime situations. That's a specific kind of toughness and these guys have it.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "It says we found a way. That's all you can ask for. A win in overtime counts just as much as any other.", 'effect_tags': ['team_mo_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "It says this group has something special. You don't win overtime games without genuine trust and genuine fight. We have both.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_up', 'team_mo_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "It says the system is deep enough to sustain an extra period. We didn't panic, we didn't abandon the scheme. We executed.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up', 'team_mo_up']}]},
    {'id': 'overtime_win_02', 'category': 'game_result', 'subcategory': 'overtime_win', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'win', 'filters': {'overtime': True}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'What was your message to the team going into overtime?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "I told them to play for each other. Everything we've built as a program — it's all right here in the next four minutes.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': 'We made two or three specific adjustments and reminded them of the reads we wanted in overtime situations. Keep the scheme. Trust it.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'team_mo_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "Stay calm, execute, and compete for every possession. Same as it's been all night.", 'effect_tags': ['red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': 'That this is what we prepare for. That the harder team wins in overtime. That I expected them to be the harder team.', 'effect_tags': ['fight_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': 'I told them this is what their individual preparation has been building toward. Moments like this belong to players who are ready for them.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'fight_up']}]},
    {'id': 'overtime_win_03', 'category': 'game_result', 'subcategory': 'overtime_win', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'win', 'filters': {'overtime': True}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'Games like this — do you think they define programs?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "Programs are defined by how they execute under pressure. Tonight we executed in overtime. That's a meaningful data point.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': 'Every game that tests you shapes you. This one will stick with these players for a while.', 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': 'Programs are defined by the daily work. Tonight was just the result of that work showing up when it had to.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Individual players are defined by moments like this. And this team has players who rose to it. That's who they are now.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'prestige_minor_up', 'fan_interest_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "Absolutely. What this team showed in overtime is exactly the culture we've been building. Moments like this are why you do the work.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'prestige_minor_up', 'fan_interest_up']}]},
    {'id': 'overtime_win_04', 'category': 'game_result', 'subcategory': 'overtime_win', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'win', 'filters': {'overtime': True}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'The extra period took a physical toll. How do you manage recovery heading into the next game?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': 'We look at each player individually — who needs more rest, who recovers quickly. We manage minutes and load in practice accordingly.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': 'We take care of each other. The staff, the training room, the players — everyone has a role in getting this group ready for the next game.', 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "You recover. You prepare. You compete again. The schedule doesn't care how tired you are.", 'effect_tags': ['fight_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "We'll manage it. Rest and recovery are part of the process. These guys know how to prepare.", 'effect_tags': ['red_herring']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': 'We build recovery protocols into the week. Practice load adjusts, film sessions become more important, and we keep the scheme sharp mentally while the body recovers.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'team_chemistry_up']}]},
    {'id': 'overtime_loss_01', 'category': 'game_result', 'subcategory': 'overtime_loss', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'loss', 'filters': {'overtime': True}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'Losing in overtime has to sting. How do you make sense of a game like this?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "It hurts. We had chances and we didn't convert them. That's the game of basketball.", 'effect_tags': ['team_mo_down', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "We look at the overtime possessions specifically. Where did the scheme break down? That's where we lost the game and that's where we start tomorrow.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'team_mo_down']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "You let the team feel it. A loss in overtime means you gave everything you had. That's not nothing. We'll grieve it together and come back stronger.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up', 'team_mo_down']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "We were in a position to win this game and we didn't close it out. That's a failure of execution and it won't happen again.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'team_mo_down']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': 'You look at which players were in position to make plays in the extra period and whether they delivered. That tells you a lot about where the individual work needs to happen.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'team_mo_down']}]},
    {'id': 'overtime_loss_02', 'category': 'game_result', 'subcategory': 'overtime_loss', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'loss', 'filters': {'overtime': True}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'Your team battled for forty minutes and then some. Is there anything to take from that effort?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "Effort without results is just effort. We'll take the fight and direct it toward better execution next time.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "Everything. This team showed its character tonight. That doesn't disappear with a loss. It actually grows.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up', 'player_em_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "The individual performances in extended time showed me who is ready for pressure and who needs more work. That's valuable information.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': 'We showed we can compete for a full game and more. That matters as we look ahead.', 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': 'The effort confirms the system is holding up under extended pressure. The issue was specific execution moments, not endurance or scheme.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}]},
    {'id': 'overtime_loss_03', 'category': 'game_result', 'subcategory': 'overtime_loss', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'loss', 'filters': {'overtime': True}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'What was your message to the team in the locker room after?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': 'That we lost this game in three or four specific possessions. Those possessions are fixable. We will fix them. Everything else we did was enough to win.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'team_chemistry_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "Keep your heads up. We competed hard. We'll learn from this and get the next one.", 'effect_tags': ['red_herring']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': 'I told them that the character they showed tonight matters more than the result. And that tomorrow we figure out individually how to be better in those moments.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'team_chemistry_up']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "That we had a chance to win and we didn't take it. And that we'll be in the gym tomorrow making sure that doesn't happen again.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': 'I told them I was proud of them. Not of the result — but of who they were tonight. And that this team has too much in it to let one loss define us.', 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_up', 'fight_up']}]},
    {'id': 'overtime_loss_04', 'category': 'game_result', 'subcategory': 'overtime_loss', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'loss', 'filters': {'overtime': True}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'If you could replay one possession from tonight, what would it be?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "I'd rather not pick one possession. This game was a collective effort and the response will be too. We win and lose together.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "I'll let the film answer that. I know what I saw and the players involved know too. We'll handle it internally.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': 'There was a sequence in overtime where we deviated from the scheme on back-to-back possessions. Those two possessions were the margin.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'team_mo_down']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "There are a few, honestly. But you don't get replays in this game. You just get the next one.", 'effect_tags': ['red_herring']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "There's a specific moment in overtime where I'd have liked to see a player trust his preparation instead of second-guessing himself. We'll work on that.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}]},
    {'id': 'winning_streak_01', 'category': 'game_result', 'subcategory': 'winning_streak', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'winning_streak', 'filters': {'min_streak': 3, 'max_streak': 9}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': "You've won three or more in a row now. What's driving the momentum?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "The system is clicking. Command is high on the plays we've installed and the team is reading defenses faster. That's what a streak looks like when it comes from the right place.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up', 'team_mo_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "We're playing well and things are going our way. We're not going to overthink it — just keep competing.", 'effect_tags': ['team_mo_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "Consistency. We've held the standard every day in practice and it's showing up in games. That's what sustained winning looks like.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': 'Individual players are peaking at the right time. When everyone is operating near their ceiling simultaneously, you get results like this.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'prestige_minor_up', 'team_mo_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "The locker room energy is different right now. When a team gets rolling and starts winning for each other, it feeds itself. That's what you're seeing.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_up', 'team_mo_up']}]},
    {'id': 'winning_streak_02', 'category': 'game_result', 'subcategory': 'winning_streak', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'winning_streak', 'filters': {'min_streak': 3, 'max_streak': 9}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'How do you keep a team focused and hungry during a winning streak?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "You remind them what this is about. It's not about the streak — it's about each other. The moment it becomes about the streak, you're vulnerable.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "The standard doesn't change. Whether we've won three or thirty, I expect the same preparation and the same execution. Full stop.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "One game at a time. That's a cliche because it works. You can't let the streak become bigger than the next game.", 'effect_tags': ['red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': 'We go back to the film after every win and find the execution errors. A streak can hide problems just as easily as it reveals strengths. We stay honest.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'team_mo_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': 'You challenge each player to keep raising their individual bar. A streak is only as good as the individual growth happening inside it.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}]},
    {'id': 'winning_streak_03', 'category': 'game_result', 'subcategory': 'winning_streak', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'winning_streak', 'filters': {'min_streak': 3, 'max_streak': 9}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': "What does this stretch mean for the program's trajectory right now?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': 'It means the individual development work is paying off at the right time. These players are becoming who we believed they could be.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'prestige_minor_up', 'fan_interest_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "It's a good stretch. We'll see where it takes us. The schedule ahead will tell us a lot.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "It means we're becoming the program we set out to build. Winning streaks are a byproduct of the culture — and the culture is showing up right now.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'prestige_minor_up', 'fan_interest_up']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': 'It means the work is paying off. Nothing more. We keep our heads down and keep working.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "It means the system has reached a level of command where it's consistently producing wins. That's a significant milestone for any program.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_up', 'discipline_up', 'fan_interest_up']}]},
    {'id': 'winning_streak_04', 'category': 'game_result', 'subcategory': 'winning_streak', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'winning_streak', 'filters': {'min_streak': 3, 'max_streak': 9}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'Are you aware of the streak, or do you try to block that out?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "I'm aware of it. I'm also aware of every mistake we made in each of those wins. I don't let the streak do my evaluation for me.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "I'm aware of it as a data point. What it confirms is that the system is working consistently. That's what I focus on.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "I'm aware of it because the players feel it. And that energy is worth protecting. I want them to enjoy it while staying grounded.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_up']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "You can't ignore it completely. But you also can't let it become the story. We focus on the next game.", 'effect_tags': ['red_herring']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': 'I let the players be aware of it. Confidence is part of performance. But I make sure they know the streak is a product of their growth, not the other way around.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'team_mo_up']}]},
    {'id': 'winning_streak_historic_01', 'category': 'game_result', 'subcategory': 'winning_streak_historic', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'winning_streak', 'filters': {'min_streak': 10}}, 'weight': 3, 'player_slot': None, 'text': "Ten wins in a row — that's a remarkable run. How do you put that in context for your program?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "It's a testament to what this group has built together. Ten wins doesn't happen without ten games of trust, sacrifice, and compete. I'm incredibly proud of these young men.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'prestige_major_up', 'fan_interest_up', 'team_mo_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "It's significant and we acknowledge it. But the only one that matters right now is the next one.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_major_up', 'team_mo_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "It means the standard we've held every single day is showing up every single night. Ten wins is ten days of preparation paying off. Keep working.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_major_up']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "Ten consecutive wins means the system has reached a level of command that's very difficult to beat consistently. That's what sustained excellence looks like.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_major_up', 'discipline_up', 'fan_interest_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': 'It means every player on this roster is operating at or near his peak. When you get everyone peaking simultaneously over ten games, you get something historic.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'prestige_major_up', 'fan_interest_up']}]},
    {'id': 'winning_streak_historic_02', 'category': 'game_result', 'subcategory': 'winning_streak_historic', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'winning_streak', 'filters': {'min_streak': 10}}, 'weight': 3, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'At what point does a streak like this start to feel different — does the pressure change?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "Pressure is the same every night. You either hold the standard or you don't. The number next to the streak is irrelevant to how we prepare.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "For individual players it can. That's why we have constant conversations about trusting your preparation. The mental side of a long streak is real and we manage it.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "You'd be lying if you said nothing changes. But the goal is to keep the routine exactly the same. Routine is what beats pressure.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': 'The trust in the locker room actually takes the pressure off. When you know your teammates are going to give everything, the streak becomes fuel rather than weight.', 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up', 'team_mo_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': 'The system insulates us from that pressure. When players trust the scheme, they have something concrete to execute rather than something abstract to protect.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'team_mo_up']}]},
    {'id': 'winning_streak_historic_03', 'category': 'game_result', 'subcategory': 'winning_streak_historic', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'winning_streak', 'filters': {'min_streak': 10}}, 'weight': 3, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'What has surprised you most about this team during this stretch?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "The depth of the system's execution. I knew the scheme was sound. What's surprised me is how completely the players have internalized it under real game pressure.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_major_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "How much they've grown together. The trust and communication in this group right now is at a level I didn't expect this soon. It's special to watch.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'prestige_major_up', 'fan_interest_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': 'Nothing surprises me. This is what happens when players meet the standard every day. I expected this. They delivered it.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_major_up']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "Their consistency, honestly. Winning one or two games is easy. Winning ten requires something sustained that's hard to manufacture.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_major_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "How several players have exceeded their own ceilings. You set expectations based on what you've seen, and then some of these guys just keep breaking through. That's been remarkable.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'prestige_major_up', 'fan_interest_up']}]},
    {'id': 'winning_streak_historic_04', 'category': 'game_result', 'subcategory': 'winning_streak_historic', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'winning_streak', 'filters': {'min_streak': 10}}, 'weight': 3, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'The fan base and media attention must be growing. How do you shield the team from that?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "I embrace it individually. Each player needs to learn how to handle attention as part of their development. Shielding them from it doesn't prepare them for what's ahead.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'fan_interest_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "You don't need to shield anything if the standards are clear. My players know what's expected of them regardless of what's being written or said.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fan_interest_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "We enjoy it as a family. The fan support means everything to this program and we don't want to be disconnected from that. We just stay grounded in who we are.", 'effect_tags': ['fan_interest_up', 'team_chemistry_up']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "You keep the routine tight. Meetings, practice, film. You don't let the outside noise change the inside rhythm.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fan_interest_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "The system does the shielding. When players are focused on their assignments and their reads, there isn't room for distraction. Execution crowds out noise.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fan_interest_up']}]},
    {'id': 'losing_streak_01', 'category': 'game_result', 'subcategory': 'losing_streak', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'losing_streak', 'filters': {'min_streak': 3, 'max_streak': 9}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': "Three losses in a row now. What's the root cause and how do you fix it?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "We've lost our collective identity a little. When a team stops playing for each other and starts playing for themselves, you see this. We have to reconnect.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_down', 'fight_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "The system is breaking down in specific phases that are compounding into losses. We've identified the issues on film and we have a plan to address them.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "We're not holding the standard. Plain and simple. That changes tomorrow morning. It will be uncomfortable but it will change.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "It's a combination of things — some execution issues, some confidence issues. We'll address them and get back on track.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_down', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Individual players are performing below their level right now. Whether that's physical, mental, or developmental — we're going to find out and address it specifically.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_down', 'discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}]},
    {'id': 'losing_streak_02', 'category': 'game_result', 'subcategory': 'losing_streak', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'losing_streak', 'filters': {'min_streak': 3, 'max_streak': 9}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'How do you keep a locker room together through a stretch like this?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "You hold everyone to the same standard — yourself included. When accountability is equal and consistent, finger-pointing doesn't happen.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "Communication. You keep the lines open and make sure nobody feels isolated. That's how teams survive rough stretches.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': 'You invest in each player individually. A losing streak can make players feel invisible. We make sure every person on this roster knows exactly what we see in them.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'team_chemistry_up']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': 'You give the locker room clarity. Confusion breeds blame. A clear picture of what went wrong and a clear plan to fix it keeps a team united.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'team_chemistry_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "You lean into the relationships you've built. This is exactly what the culture is for — not just the good times. You find out what you've built when things go wrong.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up', 'player_em_up']}]},
    {'id': 'losing_streak_03', 'category': 'game_result', 'subcategory': 'losing_streak', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'losing_streak', 'filters': {'min_streak': 3, 'max_streak': 9}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'Is there any consideration of making changes — lineup, scheme, anything structural?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "We evaluate the scheme against the results constantly. If adjustments are needed, we make them. But we don't abandon a sound system because of a rough stretch.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "Any changes we make will be about getting our best people in the best position to succeed together. It's never about shaking things up for the sake of it.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "Every option is on the table. Players earn their spots in this program every day. That doesn't change because of a losing streak — it becomes more important.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "We're always evaluating. That's our job. Any changes will be based on what we believe gives this team the best chance to win.", 'effect_tags': ['red_herring']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "We look at each individual role and whether the player in that role is the right fit right now. Development sometimes means making hard decisions. We're not afraid of them.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}]},
    {'id': 'losing_streak_04', 'category': 'game_result', 'subcategory': 'losing_streak', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'losing_streak', 'filters': {'min_streak': 3, 'max_streak': 9}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'What do you need to see from this team to believe they can turn this around?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': 'I need to see individual players take personal ownership of their role in the losing streak. No excuses, no blame. Just honest self-assessment and a commitment to be better.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "I need to see them do the right things in practice. Not what I ask for — what the standard requires. There's a difference and this team knows it.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "Competitive effort and execution for forty minutes. We'll figure out the rest from there.", 'effect_tags': ['fight_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "I need to see them compete for each other again the way they did earlier in the year. When this team is playing for each other, they're very hard to beat.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up', 'player_em_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "I need to see the system executed for forty minutes without deviation. Every time we've abandoned the scheme under pressure this week, we've lost the game right there.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}]},
    {'id': 'losing_streak_historic_01', 'category': 'game_result', 'subcategory': 'losing_streak_historic', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'losing_streak', 'filters': {'min_streak': 10}}, 'weight': 3, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'Ten consecutive losses is a difficult place to be. How honest are you being with yourself and your staff right now?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "Completely honest. I know exactly what the problems are and I know exactly what it will take to fix them. The question is whether everyone in this program is willing to do what's required.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_major_down']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "The film doesn't lie. We've been brutally honest in our evaluation. There are systemic execution issues that have compounded over this stretch and we're addressing them one by one.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_major_down']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "Very honest. This isn't a situation where you can sugarcoat anything. We know what's wrong and we're working to fix it.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_major_down', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "Completely. And the honesty starts with me. I owe these players a clear picture of where we are and a real path forward. That's what I'm focused on providing.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_major_down']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "As honest as I've ever been. I've had hard individual conversations with every player on this roster. We're not hiding from what's happening. We're facing it directly.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up', 'prestige_major_down']}]},
    {'id': 'losing_streak_historic_02', 'category': 'game_result', 'subcategory': 'losing_streak_historic', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'losing_streak', 'filters': {'min_streak': 10}}, 'weight': 3, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'At what point does a losing streak this long become a culture problem rather than an execution problem?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "It's always both. Execution problems that go uncorrected become culture problems. And culture problems make execution problems worse. We're breaking that cycle starting now.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_down', 'fight_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "That's a fair question. We're evaluating everything — execution, preparation, culture. All of it is on the table.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_major_down', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "When the scheme is sound but the execution keeps breaking down, you have to look at the people running it. That's where we are and we're not afraid to confront it.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_major_down']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "I'll tell you when it becomes a culture problem — when I stop seeing players compete. I haven't seen that yet. What I've seen is a team that's struggling, not a team that's quit.", 'effect_tags': ['fight_up', 'discipline_up', 'prestige_major_down']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "When individual players stop believing in themselves. That's the line. And honestly, some of our guys are close to it. That's the most urgent thing I'm managing right now.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_down', 'discipline_up', 'prestige_major_down']}]},
    {'id': 'losing_streak_historic_03', 'category': 'game_result', 'subcategory': 'losing_streak_historic', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'losing_streak', 'filters': {'min_streak': 10}}, 'weight': 3, 'player_slot': None, 'text': "What's your message to the fan base during a stretch like this?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': 'That we hear them and we share their frustration. And that the people in this building are working to fix it. We owe them results and we intend to deliver.', 'effect_tags': ['fan_interest_down', 'fight_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "Don't give up on these kids. They're going through something difficult and the support of this community means more than you know. We need them right now.", 'effect_tags': ['fan_interest_down', 'team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "We're working through it. We understand the frustration. We ask for patience and we'll earn it back with results.", 'effect_tags': ['fan_interest_down', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': 'Come watch these players grow. This stretch is hard, but the development happening in this program is real. The results will reflect that.', 'effect_tags': ['fan_interest_down', 'player_em_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "Trust the process. The system works — we've seen that. We're in an execution trough that we will get out of. Programs that commit to a sound system don't stay down.", 'effect_tags': ['fan_interest_down', 'discipline_up']}]},
    {'id': 'losing_streak_historic_04', 'category': 'game_result', 'subcategory': 'losing_streak_historic', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'losing_streak', 'filters': {'min_streak': 10}}, 'weight': 3, 'player_slot': None, 'text': "Is your job security something you're thinking about right now?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "My job is to fix the execution issues that are causing these losses. That's what I'm focused on. Everything else is out of my control and I don't waste energy on things I can't control.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_major_down']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "I'm thinking about these players. My job security doesn't matter if I'm not doing right by them. That's where my focus is.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_up', 'fan_interest_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "No. I'm thinking about how to win the next game. That's the only thing I can control and the only thing that matters.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "I'll be honest — you can't be completely unaware of it. But it can't be your focus. You focus on that and you guarantee a worse outcome.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_major_down', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "The players deserve a coach who is fully committed to their development regardless of the record. That's who I'm trying to be every day. The record will turn.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'fight_up', 'fan_interest_up']}]},
    {'id': 'win_top_10_01', 'category': 'game_result', 'subcategory': 'win_top_10', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'win', 'filters': {'opponent_max_rank': 10}}, 'weight': 3, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'You just beat a top-10 team. What does a win like this mean for your program?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "It means our players belong at the highest level. This is the validation they've earned through their individual development. Moments like this are why we do the work.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'prestige_major_up', 'fan_interest_up', 'team_mo_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': 'It means the standard we hold every day is competitive at the highest level. We expected to be in this game. We expected to win.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_major_up', 'fan_interest_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "It's a significant win for this program. It shows we can compete with the best. Now we have to show we can do it consistently.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_major_up', 'fan_interest_up', 'team_mo_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "It means everything to this community and to these players. Beating a team like that requires everything you have and this group gave everything they had. I couldn't be more proud.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'prestige_major_up', 'fan_interest_up', 'team_mo_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "It means the system is elite-level competitive. We didn't out-talent them — we out-executed them. That's a schematic victory as much as anything.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_major_up', 'discipline_up', 'fan_interest_up']}]},
    {'id': 'win_top_10_02', 'category': 'game_result', 'subcategory': 'win_top_10', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'win', 'filters': {'opponent_max_rank': 10}}, 'weight': 3, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'Did anything about the way your team played tonight surprise you?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "No. I've seen this team prepare all week. The only thing that would have surprised me is if they hadn't competed at this level.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_major_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': 'The composure. Against a team like that, in an environment like this — staying composed and playing our game is harder than it sounds. This group handled it beautifully.', 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_up', 'prestige_major_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "They rose to the moment. That's what you hope for against elite competition. You don't always get it.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_major_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': 'The execution level. Top-10 teams force you to execute at a level that reveals every crack in the scheme. We had very few cracks tonight. That genuinely impressed me.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_major_up', 'fan_interest_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Several players performed above what I'd seen from them in less demanding environments. Elite competition unlocks something in certain players. We found some of those players tonight.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'prestige_major_up', 'fan_interest_up']}]},
    {'id': 'win_top_10_03', 'category': 'game_result', 'subcategory': 'win_top_10', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'win', 'filters': {'opponent_max_rank': 10}}, 'weight': 3, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'How do you prevent this from becoming a ceiling rather than a stepping stone?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "By reminding this group what got us here. It wasn't one big game — it was a thousand small moments of choosing each other. We keep making those choices.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': 'By not treating it as an arrival. We go back to the film tonight and find the mistakes. Every win has them. The goal is to be better next time, not to celebrate this one indefinitely.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_major_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "Same way I always do. Tomorrow we're back in the gym at the same standard with the same expectations. A big win earns you nothing in this program.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "By keeping perspective. It's a great win. It's one game. We have more basketball to play.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "By making sure each player understands that tonight was evidence of what's possible, not a destination. The ceiling is higher than this. We have to keep reaching.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'prestige_major_up']}]},
    {'id': 'win_top_10_04', 'category': 'game_result', 'subcategory': 'win_top_10', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'win', 'filters': {'opponent_max_rank': 10}}, 'weight': 3, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'Does a win like this change how you think about what this team is capable of this season?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "It's encouraging. It tells us we belong in these conversations. Where we go from here depends on how we respond to this.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_major_up', 'fan_interest_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': 'It confirms what I already believed about this roster. The talent has always been here. The question was whether the individual development was catching up. Tonight it did.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'prestige_major_up', 'fan_interest_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': 'I knew what this team was capable of. Tonight proved it to everyone else. Now we have to prove it consistently.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_major_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': 'It confirms the system can compete at any level. That was always the design. Now we know the execution has reached that level too.', 'effect_tags': ['prestige_major_up', 'discipline_up', 'fan_interest_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "It changes how the players think about what they're capable of. And that matters more than anything I could say in a film room. Belief is self-reinforcing once it's real.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_up', 'prestige_major_up']}]},
    {'id': 'win_major_upset_01', 'category': 'game_result', 'subcategory': 'win_major_upset', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'win', 'filters': {'opponent_rank_gap_min': 30, 'opponent_higher': True}}, 'weight': 3, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'Nobody gave you much of a chance tonight. How did your team pull off the upset?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "We gave us a chance. Nobody in that locker room doubted this team tonight. The rankings don't play the game.", 'effect_tags': ['fight_up', 'discipline_up', 'prestige_major_up', 'team_mo_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': 'The system creates a leveling effect. A well-executed scheme beats raw talent more often than people think. Tonight is a good example of that.', 'effect_tags': ['prestige_major_up', 'discipline_up', 'fan_interest_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "They played for something bigger than the scoreboard. When a team fully commits to each other, they become capable of things that outsiders can't predict or measure.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_major_up', 'team_mo_up']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "We came in with a plan, we executed it, and our guys competed their hearts out. Sometimes that's enough.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_major_up', 'team_mo_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': 'Individual players delivered performances above their typical ceiling. In a game like this, that kind of individual elevation is the difference.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'prestige_major_up', 'fan_interest_up']}]},
    {'id': 'win_major_upset_02', 'category': 'game_result', 'subcategory': 'win_major_upset', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'win', 'filters': {'opponent_rank_gap_min': 30, 'opponent_higher': True}}, 'weight': 3, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'Is this the most significant win of your tenure here?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': 'In terms of the scoreboard, probably. But honestly, some of the quieter wins in that locker room — watching this group grow into who they are — those matter more to me.', 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'prestige_major_up', 'fan_interest_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "It's the most significant result. Whether it's the most significant win depends on what we do next. Results have to be sustained to mean anything.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_major_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "It's up there. We'll have time to reflect on that. Right now I'm just proud of this group and what they accomplished tonight.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_major_up', 'fan_interest_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "From a schematic standpoint — executing at the level required to beat a team like that — yes, this is a significant validation of what we're building.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_major_up', 'discipline_up', 'fan_interest_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Ask me again at the end of the season. This group has more in them. I don't want them or anyone else thinking this is the peak.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'prestige_major_up', 'fan_interest_up']}]},
    {'id': 'win_major_upset_03', 'category': 'game_result', 'subcategory': 'win_major_upset', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'win', 'filters': {'opponent_rank_gap_min': 30, 'opponent_higher': True}}, 'weight': 3, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'What was the gameplan coming in against a program of that caliber?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': 'We identified two or three schematic advantages they give up regardless of opponent and we built everything around exploiting those. The players executed the plan nearly perfectly.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_major_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "The same as always. Hold our standard on defense, execute on offense, and compete for forty minutes. The ranking doesn't change the game plan in this program.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_major_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': 'We tried to control what we could control and limit their strengths. We executed that well tonight.', 'effect_tags': ['prestige_major_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "We told our guys to play free. Don't play scared of the moment, play excited by it. The best thing that happened was this team fully embraced the challenge.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_major_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "We identified their defensive vulnerabilities and matched them to our players' individual strengths. Every player knew exactly what his opportunity was and went after it.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up', 'prestige_major_up']}]},
    {'id': 'win_major_upset_04', 'category': 'game_result', 'subcategory': 'win_major_upset', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'win', 'filters': {'opponent_rank_gap_min': 30, 'opponent_higher': True}}, 'weight': 3, 'player_slot': None, 'text': "How much does a win like this do for recruiting and the program's profile?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "It helps. But recruits are watching how you handle wins as much as the wins themselves. We'll handle this one the right way.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_major_up', 'fan_interest_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "It shows what this program is about. Any recruit watching tonight saw a team that plays for each other and competes with everything they have. That's the program we're building.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_major_up', 'fan_interest_up', 'team_chemistry_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "Wins like this get attention. We hope the right people are watching. But the work doesn't change regardless.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_major_up', 'fan_interest_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "It tells recruits that we develop players who can compete at the highest level. That's the best recruiting pitch we have. And tonight was a live demonstration.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_major_up', 'fan_interest_up', 'player_em_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "It demonstrates that players who commit to our system can compete against anyone. For a recruit evaluating programs, that's meaningful information.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_major_up', 'fan_interest_up', 'discipline_up']}]},
    {'id': 'loss_to_weak_opponent_01', 'category': 'game_result', 'subcategory': 'loss_to_weak_opponent', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'loss', 'filters': {'opponent_min_rank': 110}}, 'weight': 3, 'player_slot': None, 'text': "That's a result nobody in your program expected. How do you explain it?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "I can't explain it in a way that makes it acceptable. It's not acceptable. We were not ready to play and that starts with me and ends with every player in that locker room.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_major_down', 'fan_interest_down']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "We completely abandoned the system. From the opening tip, we were making individual decisions that had nothing to do with what we've installed. That's a preparation and focus failure.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_major_down', 'fan_interest_down']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "They played well and we didn't play well. Beyond that, I don't want to make excuses. It's on us.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_major_down', 'fan_interest_down', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "We lost who we are tonight. We didn't play for each other, we didn't compete with urgency, and a good team made us pay for it. This is not us. We'll find our way back.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_down', 'fight_up', 'prestige_major_down', 'fan_interest_down']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Individual players were not where they needed to be mentally or physically tonight. Whether that's on me for how I prepared them or on them — we'll figure that out. Either way it changes.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_down', 'discipline_up', 'prestige_major_down', 'fan_interest_down']}]},
    {'id': 'loss_to_weak_opponent_02', 'category': 'game_result', 'subcategory': 'loss_to_weak_opponent', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'loss', 'filters': {'opponent_min_rank': 110}}, 'weight': 3, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'Is there any concern about complacency becoming a recurring issue with this group?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "There's concern. And we're going to address it as a program — not as a disciplinary issue but as a cultural one. Complacency is a culture problem and the solution is culture.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_down', 'discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': 'After tonight — yes. And that concern will be communicated very clearly to this team starting first thing tomorrow. What happened tonight cannot happen again.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_major_down']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "It's something we have to look at honestly. You can't lose a game like this and not ask those questions.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_major_down', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "The system doesn't allow for complacency if it's being executed correctly. Tonight it wasn't. The question is why the execution level dropped so dramatically. That's what we're finding out.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_major_down']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "I'm more concerned with individual focus and motivation than complacency as a label. Some players need to recommit to their individual standards. That conversation is happening.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_down', 'discipline_up', 'fight_up']}]},
    {'id': 'loss_to_weak_opponent_03', 'category': 'game_result', 'subcategory': 'loss_to_weak_opponent', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'loss', 'filters': {'opponent_min_rank': 110}}, 'weight': 3, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'What do you say to your fan base after a result like this?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "I'm sorry. That wasn't good enough. We know it. And I promise you it will not happen again.", 'effect_tags': ['fan_interest_down', 'discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "I tell them we let them down tonight and that the players and I are going to spend significant time understanding why. And then we're going to fix it.", 'effect_tags': ['fan_interest_down', 'player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "We apologize for the performance and commit to doing better. That's all you can say.", 'effect_tags': ['fan_interest_down', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "That this result does not reflect the program we're building. We have a system and a standard. Tonight we failed to meet both. We will correct that.", 'effect_tags': ['fan_interest_down', 'discipline_up', 'prestige_major_down']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "That we owe them better and we know it. And that the character I've seen in this program tells me this group will respond. But we have to earn that trust back.", 'effect_tags': ['fan_interest_down', 'team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up']}]},
    {'id': 'loss_to_weak_opponent_04', 'category': 'game_result', 'subcategory': 'loss_to_weak_opponent', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'loss', 'filters': {'opponent_min_rank': 110}}, 'weight': 3, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'Are there consequences for what happened tonight — for players, for the program?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': 'Consequences are handled internally. But yes — in this program, performances like tonight have consequences. Every player on that floor tonight knows that.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_major_down']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': 'The consequence is that we go back to fundamentals. Every player runs the scheme until they can run it in their sleep. That starts tomorrow.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_major_down']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "The consequence is that we look each other in the eye and decide who we're going to be. That's the hardest consequence and the most important one.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_down', 'fight_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "We'll address that internally. What I can say is that tonight's performance is not acceptable and there will be a response.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_major_down', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Every player's role is re-evaluated after a result like this. Not as punishment — but because we have to find out who is ready to compete at the level this program requires.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_down', 'discipline_up', 'prestige_major_down']}]},
    {'id': 'loss_major_upset_01', 'category': 'game_result', 'subcategory': 'loss_major_upset', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'loss', 'filters': {'opponent_rank_gap_min': 30, 'opponent_lower': True}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': "That's a result your program doesn't expect to see. What happened?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "We got out-executed. A well-prepared team with a sound scheme can beat a more talented team. We know that — we've used it ourselves. Tonight it was used against us.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_down', 'fan_interest_down']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "We weren't ready to play and they were. There's no more complicated explanation than that. We'll be ready next time.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "They played very well and we didn't bring our best. Credit to them. We have to look at ourselves honestly.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_down', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "We didn't play with the collective intensity that makes us who we are. When a team with everything to gain plays a team that showed up expecting to win — the motivated team wins. That's what happened.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_down', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Individual players underperformed significantly against a team where that margin didn't allow for it. We'll look at the individual accountability piece very carefully.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_down', 'discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}]},
    {'id': 'loss_major_upset_02', 'category': 'game_result', 'subcategory': 'loss_major_upset', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'loss', 'filters': {'opponent_rank_gap_min': 30, 'opponent_lower': True}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': "Do you think your team underestimated tonight's opponent?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "If they did, that's a failure of preparation and leadership on my part. I will not allow this team to underestimate anyone. That ends tonight.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Some players may have. And that's an individual accountability issue we'll address specifically with each one. Underestimating an opponent is a choice and it's the wrong one.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_down', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "I think that's part of it. We'll make sure it's never part of it again.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_down', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "The system doesn't allow for underestimation — you're either executing or you're not. We weren't executing. Whether that came from underestimation or something else, the fix is the same.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "Possibly. And that's on all of us to address. In the culture we're building, every opponent is respected because every game is an opportunity to be who we say we are.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_down', 'discipline_up', 'fight_up']}]},
    {'id': 'loss_major_upset_03', 'category': 'game_result', 'subcategory': 'loss_major_upset', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'loss', 'filters': {'opponent_rank_gap_min': 30, 'opponent_lower': True}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': "How damaging is a result like this to the program's momentum and standing?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "As damaging as we let it be. The character of a program is revealed in how it responds to setbacks. We'll respond the right way.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_down', 'team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "It's a setback. We'll absorb it and move forward. Programs that can't do that don't last.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_down', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "Damaging. I won't minimize that. The question is whether it stays damaging or becomes a turning point. That's entirely up to this group.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_down', 'fight_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "The momentum impact is real. But momentum is rebuilt through execution. We get back to the system, we execute consistently, and the results follow. That's the path.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_down', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "In the short term, significant. But I've seen programs bounce back from worse when individual players decide to take ownership. That's what I'm asking for right now.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_down', 'player_em_up', 'fan_interest_down']}]},
    {'id': 'loss_major_upset_04', 'category': 'game_result', 'subcategory': 'loss_major_upset', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'loss', 'filters': {'opponent_rank_gap_min': 30, 'opponent_lower': True}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': "What's the immediate priority heading into the next game?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': 'Individual accountability. Every player needs to know exactly what his role was tonight, how he performed against that role, and what the expectation is going forward.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': 'Getting this team reconnected. We played like strangers tonight. Before we fix anything tactical, we need to find each other again in that locker room.', 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': 'Standards. We return to them immediately. Everything else — strategy, lineup, scheme — follows from holding the standard.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "Get back to work. Film session tomorrow, hard practice, and then we move forward. You can't undo tonight but you can control what comes next.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "Return to the fundamentals of the system. We ran twelve sets incorrectly tonight. We're going to run every one of them correctly in practice before we play another game.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}]},
    {'id': 'come_from_behind_win_01', 'category': 'game_result', 'subcategory': 'come_from_behind_win', 'tier': 2, 'requires_tracking': True, 'trigger': {'condition': 'come_from_behind_win', 'filters': {'trailing_entering_q4': True}}, 'weight': 3, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'You were trailing heading into the fourth quarter and found a way to win. What happened in that locker room at the break?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "I told them what I needed from them and I expected them to deliver it. They did. That's the relationship we've built in this program.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_up', 'team_mo_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "I didn't say much. The players said it. That locker room has a voice of its own and when it needed to speak, it did. I just tried to stay out of the way.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_up', 'team_mo_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': 'We identified two defensive adjustments and one offensive change. Specific, concrete, executable. The players walked out knowing exactly what they had to do differently.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up', 'team_mo_up']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "We made some adjustments and the team responded. That's a credit to their competitive character.", 'effect_tags': ['team_mo_up', 'prestige_minor_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': 'I challenged each player specifically. Not the team — each individual. I told them what I needed from them personally in the fourth quarter. And they delivered.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_up', 'team_mo_up']}]},
    {'id': 'come_from_behind_win_02', 'category': 'game_result', 'subcategory': 'come_from_behind_win', 'tier': 2, 'requires_tracking': True, 'trigger': {'condition': 'come_from_behind_win', 'filters': {'trailing_entering_q4': True}}, 'weight': 3, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'What does it mean to have a team that can win games in the fourth quarter like that?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "It means the system holds under pressure. A scheme that breaks down when you're behind isn't really a scheme. Ours held and it delivered.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "It means this is a hard team. You don't come back in the fourth quarter without hardness. We've built that here.", 'effect_tags': ['fight_up', 'discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "It means you can trust this team in big moments. That's not something you can manufacture. These guys have earned that trust.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_up', 'team_mo_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "It means individual players are developing the mental fortitude to compete when the pressure is highest. That's as valuable a skill as anything you can develop.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'prestige_minor_up', 'team_mo_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "It means this team genuinely trusts each other when everything is on the line. That kind of trust doesn't come from a playbook. It comes from everything we build every day.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}]},
    {'id': 'come_from_behind_win_03', 'category': 'game_result', 'subcategory': 'come_from_behind_win', 'tier': 2, 'requires_tracking': True, 'trigger': {'condition': 'come_from_behind_win', 'filters': {'trailing_entering_q4': True}}, 'weight': 3, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'Was there a moment in the fourth quarter where you felt the game shift?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "There was a possession where two players made a play for each other that they didn't have to make. That's when I knew. When players make those plays, the game changes.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "When we started executing the defensive stops I demanded. One stop led to another and the momentum followed. That's always how it works.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': 'There were a few moments. Momentum games have them. Our guys kept competing until we got enough of them.', 'effect_tags': ['team_mo_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "When we made the defensive adjustment I called at the break and it worked on back-to-back possessions. You could see the players' belief in the scheme go up in real time.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'team_mo_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "One specific player made a play that changed the game's energy. I won't name him here — he'll know. But that was the moment.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'team_mo_up']}]},
    {'id': 'come_from_behind_win_04', 'category': 'game_result', 'subcategory': 'come_from_behind_win', 'tier': 2, 'requires_tracking': True, 'trigger': {'condition': 'come_from_behind_win', 'filters': {'trailing_entering_q4': True}}, 'weight': 3, 'player_slot': None, 'text': "Comebacks require a belief that you can still win when everything suggests otherwise. Where does this team's belief come from?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "It comes from individual preparation. When a player knows he's done the work, he trusts himself in pressure moments. Multiply that across a roster and you get what you saw tonight.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': 'It comes from the standard we hold every day. Hard days in practice build the belief that you can handle hard moments in games.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': 'The system gives them something to trust when instinct says panic. They know if they execute the scheme, they give themselves a chance. That knowledge is calming under pressure.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'team_mo_up']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "From each other. That's the simplest answer and probably the truest one.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "From the relationships in that locker room. You can't manufacture belief in a pressure situation. It has to be built day by day. These guys have been building it all year.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}]},
    {'id': 'blown_loss_01', 'category': 'game_result', 'subcategory': 'blown_loss', 'tier': 2, 'requires_tracking': True, 'trigger': {'condition': 'blown_loss', 'filters': {'leading_entering_q4': True}}, 'weight': 3, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'You had the lead heading into the fourth quarter and it slipped away. What happened?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "We stopped competing. When you stop competing in the fourth quarter, you lose. I don't care what the scoreboard said at the three-quarter mark.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_down', 'team_mo_down']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "We abandoned the scheme when the pressure mounted. Played not to lose instead of playing to win. You can't run a system halfway — you either trust it or you don't.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_down', 'team_mo_down']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "We made a few bad decisions when we needed good ones. They made good ones. That's how you lose a lead in the fourth.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_down', 'team_mo_down', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "We stopped playing for each other and started playing scared. When individuals play scared, teams fall apart. That's what happened in the fourth quarter.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_down', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_down', 'team_mo_down']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Several individual players tightened up when the game was on the line. That's a mental preparation issue and it's something we'll address specifically.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_down', 'discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_down', 'team_mo_down']}]},
    {'id': 'blown_loss_02', 'category': 'game_result', 'subcategory': 'blown_loss', 'tier': 2, 'requires_tracking': True, 'trigger': {'condition': 'blown_loss', 'filters': {'leading_entering_q4': True}}, 'weight': 3, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'Is this the most frustrating kind of loss — having it and then giving it back?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "Every loss is frustrating when you don't meet the standard. But yes — giving a game away in the fourth quarter is particularly unacceptable. We will not do it again.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "It's up there. But the only thing to do is figure out why it happened and make sure it doesn't happen again.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_down', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "It's a painful one. But I've seen painful losses make teams better. How this group responds to tonight will say a lot about who they are.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_down', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "From a schematic standpoint — yes. We had the game managed and then stopped managing it. That's a discipline problem and it's correctable.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_down', 'team_mo_down']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Yes. And it's also the most instructive. The players who held their composure and the players who didn't — that information is invaluable for how I deploy this roster going forward.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}]},
    {'id': 'blown_loss_03', 'category': 'game_result', 'subcategory': 'blown_loss', 'tier': 2, 'requires_tracking': True, 'trigger': {'condition': 'blown_loss', 'filters': {'leading_entering_q4': True}}, 'weight': 3, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'Is closing out games something this team has struggled with before?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "It's something the system addresses specifically — how you play with a lead is built into the scheme. Tonight we didn't execute those principles. That's on us to correct.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "It's something we've worked on. Closing out games requires trust — trust in your teammates to keep competing, trust in yourself to make the right play. We lost that trust tonight.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_down', 'discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "We've struggled with it at times. That ends. Fourth quarters are not a phase of the game — they're the game. We play our best basketball when the margin is smallest.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "It's been an area of focus. Obviously we have more work to do.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_down', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': 'Some individuals have, yes. And those are specific mental and preparation issues we address individually. Closing games is partly skill and partly mental strength. We develop both.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up', 'fight_up']}]},
    {'id': 'blown_loss_04', 'category': 'game_result', 'subcategory': 'blown_loss', 'tier': 2, 'requires_tracking': True, 'trigger': {'condition': 'blown_loss', 'filters': {'leading_entering_q4': True}}, 'weight': 3, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'What changes in your approach to the next game after giving one away like this?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "My approach to fourth-quarter rotations changes. I have clearer information now about who competes in pressure moments and who doesn't. I'll use that information.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "Practice intensity goes up immediately. Comfortable leads make soft teams. We're going to be uncomfortable in practice until fourth quarter execution is where it needs to be.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "The conversation in the locker room changes. We talk directly about competing for each other when the game is on the line. That's a cultural message, not a tactical one.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "We'll specifically prepare for late-game situations. Put the players in those scenarios in practice and make sure they're ready when it matters.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "We add late-game execution specifically to the install. There are decisions that have to be automatic in the last four minutes and we'll drill those until they are.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}]},
    {'id': 'win_over_conference_leader_01', 'category': 'conference', 'subcategory': 'win_over_conference_leader', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'win', 'filters': {'opponent_is_conference_leader': True}}, 'weight': 3, 'player_slot': None, 'text': "You just beat the conference leader. What does that do for your team's standing and confidence?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "It tells everyone in this conference what we are. We don't back down from anyone. Tonight proved that.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_up', 'fan_interest_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "It validates the individual development we've invested in all season. These players are ready to compete at the top of this conference. Tonight confirmed it.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'prestige_minor_up', 'fan_interest_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "It's a big win for our conference standing and for our confidence. We'll enjoy it and then get ready for the next game.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_up', 'fan_interest_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': 'It tells this locker room they belong at the top of this conference. That belief is worth more than the win itself.', 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_up', 'prestige_minor_up', 'fan_interest_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "It confirms we're schematically competitive with the best teams in this conference. The system works at the highest level of this league. That's significant.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_up', 'discipline_up', 'fan_interest_up']}]},
    {'id': 'win_over_conference_leader_02', 'category': 'conference', 'subcategory': 'win_over_conference_leader', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'win', 'filters': {'opponent_is_conference_leader': True}}, 'weight': 3, 'player_slot': None, 'text': "Does beating the conference leader change how you think about this team's ceiling this season?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': 'It confirms what the system is capable of when we execute correctly. The ceiling has always been there — tonight we touched it.', 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "It changes what the players believe they're capable of. And belief is the ceiling. When this group believes they can compete with anyone — anything is possible.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "I already knew what this team was capable of. Now they know it too. That's the difference.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': 'It opens up possibilities. How we respond over the next few games will tell us whether tonight was a peak or a baseline.', 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Individual players raised their game to a level I hadn't seen from them against top competition. If they can sustain that — and I believe they can — the ceiling is very high.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'prestige_minor_up', 'fan_interest_up']}]},
    {'id': 'win_over_conference_leader_03', 'category': 'conference', 'subcategory': 'win_over_conference_leader', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'win', 'filters': {'opponent_is_conference_leader': True}}, 'weight': 3, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'What did your team do specifically that gave you an advantage tonight?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "We competed with more urgency than them for more possessions than them. It's that simple. When a team wants it more, over forty minutes, it shows.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "Defense. We held our defensive standard for forty minutes. That's what beat them.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': 'We executed in the moments that mattered and we made them uncomfortable defensively. Both sides of the ball contributed.', 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_up', 'discipline_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Individual matchups. We identified their vulnerabilities and matched our players' strengths against them. That advantage was won in preparation, not in the game.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': 'We exploited two specific schematic advantages they give up. We identified those in film, built our offense around them, and executed the plan. It worked exactly as designed.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up', 'fan_interest_up']}]},
    {'id': 'win_over_conference_leader_04', 'category': 'conference', 'subcategory': 'win_over_conference_leader', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'win', 'filters': {'opponent_is_conference_leader': True}}, 'weight': 3, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'How does this result affect the conference race?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "It tightens things up significantly. A lot of basketball left to be played but we've made ourselves relevant in the conversation.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_up', 'fan_interest_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "It tells the rest of this conference that we're here. The conversation about who leads this league just got more interesting.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up', 'fan_interest_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "It creates a schematic problem for every team in this conference. They've now seen what we're capable of executing. Adjusting to that is not easy.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_up', 'fan_interest_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': 'It shows that this roster can compete for a conference title. Whether we do depends on these players continuing to develop and build on what they showed tonight.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'prestige_minor_up', 'fan_interest_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': 'It puts this program back where we belong — at the center of the conversation. This team and this community deserve that. Tonight is a step toward making it a reality.', 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'prestige_minor_up', 'fan_interest_up']}]},
    {'id': 'repeat_win_vs_opponent_01', 'category': 'conference', 'subcategory': 'repeat_win_vs_opponent', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'win', 'filters': {'wins_vs_opponent_this_season_min': 2}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': "You've beaten this opponent multiple times this season now. What does that tell you about your program versus theirs?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "It tells you the gap is real. If you can beat a team consistently, it's not a fluke. It's a reflection of who's built their program better.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "It tells me the system has found something real against their scheme. They've had time to adjust and they haven't been able to. That's a meaningful competitive advantage.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up', 'fan_interest_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "Every game is its own game. We've beaten them more than once. That's a good thing. We'll see what the postseason holds.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "It tells me this team doesn't lose focus against a familiar opponent. Complacency is real — this group hasn't shown it, and that matters.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': 'Our players have learned this opponent. The second and third time around, individual matchups have a history. Our guys have used that history to their advantage.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}]},
    {'id': 'repeat_win_vs_opponent_02', 'category': 'conference', 'subcategory': 'repeat_win_vs_opponent', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'win', 'filters': {'wins_vs_opponent_this_season_min': 2}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'Does familiarity with an opponent make it harder or easier to prepare?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "Easier for the scheme, harder for the execution focus. You know exactly what they'll do, but players can get overconfident. We manage that balance deliberately.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Easier for individual players. Knowing your matchup's tendencies is a real advantage. Our players have used every game against them as a learning experience.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "Neither changes the standard. You prepare the same way every week. The opponent doesn't change the approach.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': 'Both, honestly. You know what to expect but you also have to guard against assuming you know too much.', 'effect_tags': ['red_herring']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "The preparation is easier. The focus is harder. This team has handled both well. That's a sign of a mature group.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'discipline_up']}]},
    {'id': 'repeat_win_vs_opponent_03', 'category': 'conference', 'subcategory': 'repeat_win_vs_opponent', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'win', 'filters': {'wins_vs_opponent_this_season_min': 2}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'What adjustments did they make from the last time you played, and how did your team handle them?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "They made two or three schematic changes we anticipated. We had counters built into the plan. The players executed the counters well. That's a chess match and tonight we won it.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "They made adjustments. Our guys made adjustments. We were better tonight. That's the whole story.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': 'They mixed things up defensively. We handled it reasonably well. There are still things to clean up but the result was what we needed.', 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': 'They shifted some individual matchups trying to disrupt our flow. Our players read those adjustments well because we spent time specifically preparing for them.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': 'They tried to disrupt our rhythm with some different looks. This team handled it with composure. That composure comes from knowing each other and trusting each other deeply.', 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'discipline_up']}]},
    {'id': 'repeat_win_vs_opponent_04', 'category': 'conference', 'subcategory': 'repeat_win_vs_opponent', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'win', 'filters': {'wins_vs_opponent_this_season_min': 2}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'If you meet them again in the postseason, how do you approach that differently?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "Same preparation, higher stakes. That's the postseason. The team that holds their standard when it matters most wins. We've shown we can do that against this opponent.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "You assume they've solved every problem we've given them. Postseason opponents are always more dangerous than the regular season version.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "We'd expect them to make significant schematic changes. We'd have to go back to the film and build a new plan from scratch. That's postseason preparation — nothing carries over.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "With the same mentality. Our guys know how to compete against this team. The trust and familiarity actually helps us. We'd back ourselves in that matchup.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Individual matchups would be studied more deeply. Three games of data against specific players is a significant preparation advantage. We'd use every bit of it.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}]},
    {'id': 'repeat_loss_vs_opponent_01', 'category': 'conference', 'subcategory': 'repeat_loss_vs_opponent', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'loss', 'filters': {'losses_vs_opponent_this_season_min': 2}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': "They've beaten you more than once this season. What are they doing that your team hasn't been able to solve?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "They've found a schematic answer to two or three things we rely on. We've made adjustments each game and they've countered. That's a coaching staff doing their job well. We have to find a different solution.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "They're more disciplined than us when it comes to that matchup. We're going to fix that. I don't lose to the same team three times.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "They've played well in every matchup against us. Credit to them. We have to find answers that we haven't found yet.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_down', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Specific individual matchups have been difficult for us. There are players on that team that we have not found the right answer to. That's a development challenge and we'll work on it.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_down', 'discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "They play with a consistency and a togetherness that we haven't matched in these games. That's the honest answer. And we're going to find that level before we meet them again.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_down', 'fight_up', 'discipline_up']}]},
    {'id': 'repeat_loss_vs_opponent_02', 'category': 'conference', 'subcategory': 'repeat_loss_vs_opponent', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'loss', 'filters': {'losses_vs_opponent_this_season_min': 2}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'Does losing to the same opponent more than once in a season create a mental hurdle going forward?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "Only if I allow it to. I won't. This team knows how to compete. They also know they're capable of beating anyone. That belief doesn't change because of a series result.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "For some individual players it can. That's why I address it directly with each person. Losing to the same opponent twice requires a specific mental reset that we'll work through.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_down', 'discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "It can if you let it become one. We won't. We'll look at the film, identify what we need to do differently, and come back ready.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "Not with this group. They've shown they respond to adversity by pulling together, not apart. A series loss makes us hungrier. That's who they are.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "The system doesn't carry emotional baggage from game to game. We reset, we build a new plan, and we execute it. The next matchup is a fresh problem. We'll solve it.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'team_mo_up']}]},
    {'id': 'repeat_loss_vs_opponent_03', 'category': 'conference', 'subcategory': 'repeat_loss_vs_opponent', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'loss', 'filters': {'losses_vs_opponent_this_season_min': 2}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'What specifically changes in your preparation if you see them again?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "Everything. Three games of data means we know exactly what they do and what we haven't answered. We rebuild the plan from scratch and find the answers we haven't found yet.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "The emotional preparation changes. Our guys need to approach the next matchup with a healthy hunger rather than anxiety. That's a culture conversation we'll have before anything tactical.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up', 'player_em_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "The focus level changes. We haven't matched their intensity in these games. That's unacceptable and it will not be an issue the next time we face them.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "We go deeper on their adjustments and build more counters. They've made us uncomfortable — we need to return the favor.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': 'Individual matchup preparation gets much more specific. We know which of their players have hurt us and which of ours have struggled against them. That information drives everything.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}]},
    {'id': 'repeat_loss_vs_opponent_04', 'category': 'conference', 'subcategory': 'repeat_loss_vs_opponent', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'loss', 'filters': {'losses_vs_opponent_this_season_min': 2}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': "Is there anything you respect about how they've beaten you?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "They've been more consistent than us in these games. I respect consistency. I also intend to match it and surpass it.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "They play together. Every time we've faced them, they've been a cohesive unit. That's something to admire and something we're building toward ourselves.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "They've been well-prepared and well-coached in both games. You have to give them credit for that.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_down', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "Their preparation. They've scouted us well and they've made adjustments faster than we have. That's a coaching staff and a program doing things the right way. We'll learn from it.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Their best players have shown up in these matchups. That's not easy to do. They have players who perform when the stakes are high. We're developing that in our own roster.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}]},
    {'id': 'fg_pct_advantage_01', 'category': 'team_performance', 'subcategory': 'fg_pct_advantage', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'fg_pct_gap', 'filters': {'user_advantage_min': 10}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'Your team shot the ball significantly better than your opponent tonight. What was creating those looks?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': 'The spacing in our half-court offense created high-percentage looks all night. When the system generates the right shots, the percentages follow.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': 'Individual players were getting to their spots and taking shots within their skill set. High-quality shots come from players who know their game and trust it.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "We took the right shots. That's what we practice. When players follow the game plan, that's the result.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': 'Ball movement was good and we found open looks. When the ball moves, good things happen.', 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "Players were making decisions for each other — passing up decent looks to find great ones. That's team basketball and it shows up in the shooting numbers.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}]},
    {'id': 'fg_pct_advantage_02', 'category': 'team_performance', 'subcategory': 'fg_pct_advantage', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'fg_pct_gap', 'filters': {'user_advantage_min': 10}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'Shooting efficiency like that is hard to sustain. Is this your team playing near its ceiling offensively?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "No. The ceiling is higher. This is what good execution looks like. We'll hold the standard and let the results speak.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "Tonight validated the shot selection principles we've installed. The question isn't whether we can replicate it — it's whether we trust the process enough to let it happen consistently.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "It was a good shooting night. We'll take them when they come and not read too much into any single game's efficiency.", 'effect_tags': ['red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "For some players this is closer to their ceiling, yes. For others, this is what I expect regularly. The development gap is telling and we'll close it.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': 'When this team is playing free and playing for each other, this is who they are offensively. The question is how often we can get to that place mentally.', 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}]},
    {'id': 'fg_pct_advantage_03', 'category': 'team_performance', 'subcategory': 'fg_pct_advantage', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'fg_pct_gap', 'filters': {'user_advantage_min': 10}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'Does a night like this create pressure on the defense to keep up? How do you keep the team balanced?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': 'We talk about it constantly — offense gets the highlights but defense is what makes us who we are. The guys understand that balance. Tonight they showed both.', 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "The system doesn't allow the two sides to become independent. Defensive stops create offensive opportunities and vice versa. You build one and you build the other.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "Good offense and good defense aren't in competition. You need both. We preach that and tonight we showed it.", 'effect_tags': ['red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "Defense is non-negotiable in this program. I don't care how well we shoot — if the defense slips, we address it. Both sides are held to the same standard.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "I challenge each player to own both ends. Offense and defense aren't separate identities for our guys — every player is expected to compete on both sides every night.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}]},
    {'id': 'fg_pct_advantage_04', 'category': 'team_performance', 'subcategory': 'fg_pct_advantage', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'fg_pct_gap', 'filters': {'user_advantage_min': 10}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'Was there a specific offensive action or set that was particularly effective tonight?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "Two or three actions in particular generated the looks we wanted. I'll keep those between us and our opponents' film room, but the scheme worked as designed.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "The whole offense worked. That's the point. It's not one play — it's the execution of the entire system from possession to possession.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "We moved the ball well and found open shooters. I'll leave the specifics for the film room.", 'effect_tags': ['red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Specific players were reading the defense and making the right play off their initial action. That's IQ development showing up in real time.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': 'Honestly the best thing was the trust. Players were reading each other and making decisions together rather than forcing individual actions. That unselfishness creates efficient offense.', 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}]},
    {'id': 'fg_pct_disadvantage_01', 'category': 'team_performance', 'subcategory': 'fg_pct_disadvantage', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'fg_pct_gap', 'filters': {'opponent_advantage_min': 10}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'Your opponent shot the ball significantly better than you tonight. What went wrong defensively?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "We gave up too many high-percentage looks. Whether that's our positioning, our effort, or our scheme, it wasn't good enough. We address it tomorrow.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "The defensive scheme broke down in specific phases. They found actions we weren't prepared for and we didn't adjust quickly enough. That's a preparation and communication failure.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "They shot the ball well and we didn't do enough to make it difficult. We have to be harder to shoot against.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_down', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "Our defensive communication broke down. When we're not talking on defense, we give up easy looks. That's a trust and attention issue we'll work through together.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_down', 'discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Individual defenders were out of position repeatedly. Whether that's technique, focus, or effort — each player knows what happened on his possessions and we'll address it specifically.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_down', 'discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}]},
    {'id': 'fg_pct_disadvantage_02', 'category': 'team_performance', 'subcategory': 'fg_pct_disadvantage', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'fg_pct_gap', 'filters': {'opponent_advantage_min': 10}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'Is this a scheme problem, an effort problem, or something else entirely?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "Honestly — both. The scheme had the right reads and we didn't execute them. That's an effort and attention problem on top of what was already a difficult assignment.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "Effort. The scheme is sound. When players commit to it, we're a good defensive team. Tonight they didn't commit at the level the scheme requires.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "A combination. We'll sort through the film and separate what was scheme and what was execution.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_down', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "It varies by player. Some guys had effort issues, some had technique issues. That's why we address defense individually rather than as a collective problem.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_down', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "I think it was a focus problem. We weren't locked in collectively. When the group loses its defensive focus together, the scheme doesn't matter. That's the real issue.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_down', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}]},
    {'id': 'fg_pct_disadvantage_03', 'category': 'team_performance', 'subcategory': 'fg_pct_disadvantage', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'fg_pct_gap', 'filters': {'opponent_advantage_min': 10}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': "When you're getting outshot that badly, what's the adjustment process look like at halftime?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': 'You bring the group together and name the problem directly. Not to blame anyone — but everyone needs to see the same picture. Then you ask them to recommit to each other defensively.', 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "You make it clear that the standard isn't being met and that the second half will look different. I don't sugarcoat it at halftime. The players know what's expected.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': 'You identify the two or three things creating the most damage, communicate the adjustments clearly, and get out of the way and let the players execute.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': 'You go straight to the specific actions that hurt you. Not a general speech — specific counters to specific actions. The players need answers, not emotion, at halftime.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "You have individual conversations. The defensive breakdown isn't uniform — some guys had specific problems. You address those specifically so they walk out with a personal assignment, not a group lecture.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}]},
    {'id': 'fg_pct_disadvantage_04', 'category': 'team_performance', 'subcategory': 'fg_pct_disadvantage', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'fg_pct_gap', 'filters': {'opponent_advantage_min': 10}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'Getting outshot by that margin — does that reflect a matchup problem or something more systemic in your program right now?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': 'Some of both. There were matchup challenges we knew going in. But the execution gaps were larger than what any matchup accounts for. Those gaps are individual development issues.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_down', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "It's hard to say after one game. We'll look at the film and get a clearer picture before drawing any larger conclusions.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_down', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "It's a matchup-specific problem that exposed a system gap. We'll address the gap so the next time we face a similar challenge, we have a better answer.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': 'It reflects a standard problem. When players hold the standard defensively, no matchup produces numbers like that. We have to get back to the standard.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "It reflects a collective focus problem more than anything else. The talent is there. The scheme is there. What wasn't there tonight was the shared intensity. That's cultural and we'll address it as such.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_down', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}]},
    {'id': 'fastbreak_advantage_01', 'category': 'team_performance', 'subcategory': 'fastbreak_advantage', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'fastbreak_pts_gap', 'filters': {'user_advantage_min': 10}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'Your team dominated in transition tonight. What was generating those fast break opportunities?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': 'The defensive-to-offensive transition system was working exactly as designed. When you get the right players running the right lanes off a stop, those points are almost automatic.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': 'Defensive intensity. Every fast break starts with a stop or a rebound. We competed hard enough on the defensive end to create those opportunities.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "We got out in transition and our guys finished. When you're getting those looks, you have to convert them. Tonight we did.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Players who excel in space got into space early. Once certain guys get momentum going downhill, they're very hard to stop. We put them in position to do that.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "The whole team was running together. Fast breaks aren't just the ball handler — they're five guys sprinting together in the same direction. That requires trust and it requires fitness. We had both tonight.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}]},
    {'id': 'fastbreak_advantage_02', 'category': 'team_performance', 'subcategory': 'fastbreak_advantage', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'fastbreak_pts_gap', 'filters': {'user_advantage_min': 10}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'Transition offense is such a momentum builder. Did you feel that energy shift the game at any point tonight?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "Absolutely. There's a moment when the other team realizes they can't get back — you can feel the energy in the building change. Our guys fed off that and it snowballed.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up', 'team_mo_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': 'Transition points change the complexion of games quickly. We got on a few runs that gave us some breathing room and changed the feel of the game.', 'effect_tags': ['team_mo_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "That's what transition offense does when you execute it — it breaks opponents physically and mentally. We've practiced it specifically for that reason.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'team_mo_up']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "There was a sequence in the third quarter where we converted three straight transition opportunities. That's when the game opened up. The system did its job.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up', 'team_mo_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': 'A few players got into a rhythm in transition that was contagious. Once certain guys start rolling downhill, the whole team elevates. We need those players to be that ignition consistently.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'team_mo_up']}]},
    {'id': 'fastbreak_advantage_03', 'category': 'team_performance', 'subcategory': 'fastbreak_advantage', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'fastbreak_pts_gap', 'filters': {'user_advantage_min': 10}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'How much of your transition success tonight came from defense versus offensive rebounding?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "Primarily defense. Stops into outlet passes into numbered advantages — that's the sequence we install. We got enough stops tonight to make it a real factor.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': 'A mix of both. We got stops and we also got some second-chance situations that led to transition. The offense was clicking on multiple levels tonight.', 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': 'Defense. Everything in this program starts on defense. The fast break points tonight were a direct result of the defensive intensity we brought from the opening tip.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "Both contributed but what impressed me most was how quickly we all got into transition together. Five guys moving in the same direction — that's a team thing, not an individual thing.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': 'Our guards deserves specific credit for initiating the break quickly. Their decision-making in the first two seconds of transition created the numbers advantages that led to those points.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}]},
    {'id': 'fastbreak_advantage_04', 'category': 'team_performance', 'subcategory': 'fastbreak_advantage', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'fastbreak_pts_gap', 'filters': {'user_advantage_min': 10}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'Is being a good transition team a priority for your program, or is it a byproduct of other things you do well?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "It's built into the system. Transition offense is installed — we have specific actions and spacing principles for numbered advantages. It's not an accident when it works.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "It's a byproduct of defense and conditioning. You can't coach a team to run without also coaching them to defend and to be in shape. Do those two things and the fast breaks come.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': 'Both. We emphasize it, but it only works when the foundational stuff — defense, rebounding, conditioning — is in place.', 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "It's a mindset priority. We want to play with pace and play with joy. Fast breaks come from that mentality. When this team is playing free, they run.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "For certain players it's a priority because it's where they're most dangerous. We design our transition principles around putting those players in space as quickly as possible.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}]},
    {'id': 'fastbreak_disadvantage_01', 'category': 'team_performance', 'subcategory': 'fastbreak_disadvantage', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'fastbreak_pts_gap', 'filters': {'opponent_advantage_min': 10}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'You got badly outscored in transition tonight. What was breaking down?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "Defensive transition discipline. We didn't get back, we didn't protect the paint, and they ran us off the floor in stretches. That's a conditioning and commitment issue.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "We violated the transition defense principles repeatedly. When you don't stop the ball and you don't get numbers back, those points are on the scheme — specifically on us not executing it.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "We didn't get back and they made us pay for it. That's a correctable problem.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_down', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "We stopped competing together defensively after turnovers and misses. It takes five guys to defend the break and we weren't doing it as five. That's a collective accountability issue.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_down', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Specific players who are supposed to get back weren't getting back. That's a defined role in this program. If you're not fulfilling your transition role, you're going to hear about it.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_down', 'discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}]},
    {'id': 'fastbreak_disadvantage_02', 'category': 'team_performance', 'subcategory': 'fastbreak_disadvantage', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'fastbreak_pts_gap', 'filters': {'opponent_advantage_min': 10}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'Transition defense is often a reflection of effort and attention. How do you fix that without it becoming a character indictment of your players?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "You separate the effort question from the individual player. You show them specifically what role they're supposed to fill on transition defense and you practice it until it's automatic. You make it about the skill, not the character.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "You remind them that getting back is how you protect each other. It's not a personal effort question — it's a team accountability question. When you don't get back, you're leaving your teammate alone.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "I don't avoid the character question when it applies. Transition defense is effort. If you're not giving effort, that says something. We address it directly.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': 'You focus on the habit. Practice it repeatedly until the right response is automatic. When it becomes habit, effort becomes less of the issue.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': 'You make it a system question — who is supposed to be where and when. Then you run drills that replicate the exact situations that caused the breakdowns. You fix the behavior without the editorial.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}]},
    {'id': 'fastbreak_disadvantage_03', 'category': 'team_performance', 'subcategory': 'fastbreak_disadvantage', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'fastbreak_pts_gap', 'filters': {'opponent_advantage_min': 10}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'Does a team that runs as well as your opponent tonight present a specific schematic problem for you?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "Every fast-paced team presents a specific preparation challenge. We had answers in the scheme that we didn't execute. We'll revisit those and be sharper next time.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "Any team presents a problem if you don't compete hard enough to take away what they do best. We didn't compete hard enough in transition defense. Simple.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': 'Fast-paced teams challenge everyone. The key is not turning the ball over and not giving them easy outlets. We did both too much tonight.', 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_down', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "It's a conditioning and decision-making challenge for individual players. You have to make better decisions with the ball and have the conditioning to get back every single trip. Both are improvable.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "Teams that run well expose whether a group is genuinely competing for each other. The easy thing to do when you're tired is stop getting back. The hard thing is doing it anyway. We have to build that commitment.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_down', 'fight_up', 'discipline_up']}]},
    {'id': 'fastbreak_disadvantage_04', 'category': 'team_performance', 'subcategory': 'fastbreak_disadvantage', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'fastbreak_pts_gap', 'filters': {'opponent_advantage_min': 10}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'Is this a conditioning issue, or is it purely a decision-making and execution problem?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "Both, and I won't pretend otherwise. We'll address conditioning in practice and decision-making on film. Neither is acceptable at the level it was tonight.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "Primarily execution. Our transition defense principles are clear. When you see a breakdown on film, it's almost always a player who deviated from his assignment, not a player who couldn't get back.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "Probably a combination. We'll look at the film and get honest about which is which. Both are fixable.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_down', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Decision-making for most players, conditioning for a few. I know which guys need what and I'll address it on an individual basis.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_down', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "Honestly, I think it's a mental-effort issue disguised as a conditioning issue. When players really want to get back, they get back. We have to want it more than we did tonight.", 'effect_tags': ['fight_up', 'team_chemistry_down', 'prestige_minor_down']}]},
    {'id': 'paint_points_advantage_01', 'category': 'team_performance', 'subcategory': 'paint_points_advantage', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'paint_pts_gap', 'filters': {'user_advantage_min': 10}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'You dominated in the paint tonight. What were you doing to get to those interior positions so consistently?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': 'The spacing in our offense forces defenses to make a choice. When they extend to guard the perimeter, they open the paint. When they pack the paint, we shoot over them. Tonight they made the wrong choice consistently.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': 'We were physically tougher than them inside. Establishing the paint is about physicality and will. Tonight we had more of both.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': 'Good ball movement created driving lanes and post opportunities. We attacked the paint and finished well.', 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Our interior players were dominant in their individual matchups. When those guys are playing with aggression and physicality, they're very hard to keep out of the paint.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': 'The guards did a great job of making the right reads and getting the ball to the right places. Inside scoring is often a collective achievement — it takes everyone to create those opportunities.', 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}]},
    {'id': 'paint_points_advantage_02', 'category': 'team_performance', 'subcategory': 'paint_points_advantage', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'paint_pts_gap', 'filters': {'user_advantage_min': 10}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'Winning the paint often wins the game. Is interior dominance a pillar of your offensive identity?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "Toughness inside is non-negotiable for this program. You establish the paint, you control the game. That's not optional — that's the baseline.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': 'The system is designed to attack wherever the defense gives us the most. Tonight that was the paint. Other nights it may be the three-point line. We take what the defense offers.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "We want to be balanced. But if you can win in the paint, you're going to win more often than not. We'll always take it.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': 'For certain players it absolutely is. We invest heavily in developing interior scoring and footwork. When those players dominate inside, it validates that work.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "Winning inside requires five guys working together — screens, reads, physicality, finishing. It's one of the more collective offensive achievements. When we do it well, it says a lot about our togetherness.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}]},
    {'id': 'paint_points_advantage_03', 'category': 'team_performance', 'subcategory': 'paint_points_advantage', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'paint_pts_gap', 'filters': {'user_advantage_min': 10}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'Does winning the paint this convincingly say something about the physical matchup tonight, or is this replicable against any opponent?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': 'Some of it was matchup-specific. But the physicality and the technique our guys showed tonight is replicable. The matchup created the opportunity — our players took advantage of it. That part is theirs.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "The physicality is replicable. The matchup was favorable, but physical toughness doesn't depend on who you're playing. We brought it tonight. We bring it every night.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "Partly matchup, partly us playing well. We'll see what the film tells us about what we can take into future games.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "The scheme is replicable. We'll face tougher interior defenders, but the principles that created these looks work against any defense. It's about execution, not just matchup.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "The trust between our guards and our bigs is replicable. That's about relationships and reads, not matchup. As long as we're playing for each other inside, we can do this against anyone.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}]},
    {'id': 'paint_points_advantage_04', 'category': 'team_performance', 'subcategory': 'paint_points_advantage', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'paint_pts_gap', 'filters': {'user_advantage_min': 10}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'Interior success often leads to better three-point opportunities as well. Did you see that ripple effect tonight?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': 'Absolutely. When defenses collapse to stop the paint game, they give up corner threes and mid-range pull-ups. We identified those kick-out opportunities and converted at a good rate.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': 'Yes. When you force the defense to make a choice, somebody gets open. We found those open looks more consistently tonight.', 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': 'Specific players were reading the kick-out at exactly the right moment. That IQ piece — knowing when to keep attacking and when to pass — is what separates good offensive players from great ones.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "We made them choose. And when you make a defense choose, someone's open. Our guys were disciplined enough to find that open player rather than forcing the interior.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "The unselfishness was real tonight. Players drove, drew the help, and found teammates. That's what makes this offense hard to guard — five guys all making the right decision.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}]},
    {'id': 'paint_points_disadvantage_01', 'category': 'team_performance', 'subcategory': 'paint_points_disadvantage', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'paint_pts_gap', 'filters': {'opponent_advantage_min': 10}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': "You got beaten badly in the paint tonight. What's the root of that problem?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "We weren't physical enough. Period. Protecting the paint is about physicality and toughness. We didn't bring enough of either. That changes in practice starting tomorrow.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "Our interior defense scheme broke down in two specific ways. We'll address those on film. It's fixable but it requires everyone understanding their role and executing it.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': 'They had a physical advantage and they used it. We have to find better answers to interior pressure.', 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_down', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Individual defensive players were out-positioned or out-physicaled. Some of that is developmental — we'll work on technique and strength. Some of it is focus, and we'll address that separately.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_down', 'discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "We didn't protect each other inside. Interior defense requires help, communication, and commitment from everyone. When we don't have all three, this is what happens.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_down', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}]},
    {'id': 'paint_points_disadvantage_02', 'category': 'team_performance', 'subcategory': 'paint_points_disadvantage', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'paint_pts_gap', 'filters': {'opponent_advantage_min': 10}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'Is losing the paint battle a personnel problem or a scheme problem for your program right now?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "Primarily scheme execution. We have the right concepts — we just didn't run them with enough consistency or physicality. Personnel is part of any assessment but I don't want to use it as a crutch.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "It's a will problem, not a personnel problem. Our players are physically capable of defending the paint. They have to choose to do it. That choice wasn't made tonight.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "Both play a role. We'll be honest in our evaluation and address whichever has the bigger contribution to tonight's result.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_down', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "It's a combination of individual development gaps and scheme execution. Some players need more physical development, some need more technique work, and all of them need to execute better. We'll address each specifically.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_down', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "It's a competitive mindset problem. We need guys who take it personally when someone scores on them in the paint. That edge — that interior pride — is something we're building.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_down', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}]},
    {'id': 'paint_points_disadvantage_03', 'category': 'team_performance', 'subcategory': 'paint_points_disadvantage', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'paint_pts_gap', 'filters': {'opponent_advantage_min': 10}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': "How do you defend a team that's physically dominant inside without fouling excessively or giving up corner threes?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "You defend before the catch. The best way to protect the paint is to keep the ball out of it in the first place. We didn't do that — we let them catch inside their comfort zones and then tried to guard them. That's too late.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "You use your body to make them uncomfortable without fouling. Legal physical play on every possession. It's a technique and conditioning question — can you maintain that physicality for forty minutes? We couldn't tonight.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "You have to pick your battles. Force them left, take away their favorite spots, and make their role players beat you. We didn't do that consistently enough.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_down', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Individual technique at the point of attack. Positioning, footwork, early hands on the catcher. We'll drill each player on the specific situations where they were vulnerable tonight.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "You defend it together. One defender can't stop a dominant interior player alone. Everyone has to be in the right spot to force the catch away from power position. That's a communication and trust issue — five guys, one goal.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'discipline_up']}]},
    {'id': 'paint_points_disadvantage_04', 'category': 'team_performance', 'subcategory': 'paint_points_disadvantage', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'paint_pts_gap', 'filters': {'opponent_advantage_min': 10}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'Does losing the paint this badly indicate you need to rethink personnel or matchup decisions in the next game?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "It raises questions about specific individual matchups. We'll look at whether different deployment creates better answers inside. Development and deployment are both factors here.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "Personnel decisions earn their way in practice. If players need to be moved around, it's because someone else earned it. The film will tell us who did and who didn't.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "Possibly. We'll look at the matchups on film and evaluate whether we can get better answers with different personnel combinations.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_down', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "Before I move personnel around, I want to know whether the execution was the real problem. Changing personnel to solve an execution problem is a false solution. Let's fix the execution first.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "More than personnel, I'm thinking about who in this program has the edge and the willingness to defend the paint the way it needs to be defended. That's a character question as much as a matchup question.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_down', 'fight_up', 'discipline_up']}]},
    {'id': 'bench_scoring_high_01', 'category': 'team_performance', 'subcategory': 'bench_scoring_high', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'bench_pts', 'filters': {'user_bench_min': 20}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'Your bench contributed significantly tonight. What does that kind of depth do for a program?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "It tells you the culture goes fourteen deep. When reserve players come in and compete at that level, it means everyone in that locker room is invested — not just the starters. That's special.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'prestige_minor_up', 'fan_interest_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': 'It tells you competition in practice is real. When players know that the guy behind them is ready, everybody elevates. The bench production tonight came from practice standards, not just tonight.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': 'It gives you flexibility and keeps starters fresh. Bench depth is a significant competitive advantage over a long season.', 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': 'It means development is happening across the full roster. Players who were role players six months ago are producing at a meaningful level. That growth is real and it matters for our ceiling as a team.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'prestige_minor_up', 'fan_interest_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "It means the system scales. When second-unit players can execute the same principles at a high level, the opponent can't adjust for the personnel change. That's a competitive structural advantage.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}]},
    {'id': 'bench_scoring_high_02', 'category': 'team_performance', 'subcategory': 'bench_scoring_high', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'bench_pts', 'filters': {'user_bench_min': 20}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'How much credit do the starters deserve for setting the tone that allowed the bench to step in and produce?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "A great deal. And honestly, the bench producing also takes pressure off the starters to carry everything. That's how a team is supposed to function. Everyone contributing to a single goal.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "The starters established the standard. The bench met it. That's the program working as intended.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "It's a team game and everyone contributes. Starters set a tone, bench players respond to it. Tonight both groups did their jobs.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Fair amount. But the bench players deserve individual credit too. They came in ready, they made plays, and they affected the game. That's individual preparation paying off at the right moment.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': 'The starters built a lead and a structure that the bench could operate within. But the bench executed. Both matter and both deserve recognition.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'team_chemistry_up']}]},
    {'id': 'bench_scoring_high_03', 'category': 'team_performance', 'subcategory': 'bench_scoring_high', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'bench_pts', 'filters': {'user_bench_min': 20}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'When your bench produces like that, does it create any internal competition dynamics you have to manage?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "I welcome that competition. When reserve players outperform starters, lineups change. Every player in this program knows that. It's not a management issue — it's the system working correctly.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': 'Healthy competition, yes. And I address it individually — I make sure every player knows where they stand and what they need to do to expand their role. Clarity prevents the kind of friction that hurts teams.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "Competition for minutes is healthy. We manage it by being clear about what we're looking for from every player. As long as communication is good, it stays positive.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "The system manages it. Each player has a defined role and knows what success looks like in that role. Bench production doesn't create conflict because everyone is evaluated against their role, not against each other.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'team_chemistry_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "When the culture is right, bench production doesn't create division — it creates pride. Players who started tonight are genuinely happy for the guys who came in and produced. That's the culture we've built.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_up']}]},
    {'id': 'bench_scoring_high_04', 'category': 'team_performance', 'subcategory': 'bench_scoring_high', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'bench_pts', 'filters': {'user_bench_min': 20}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': "Over a long season, bench depth becomes critical. How do you keep reserve players engaged and ready when they don't play as much in some games?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Individual conversations. Every reserve player gets a clear picture of their role, what they're being developed for, and what the path looks like. When players have a personal roadmap, they stay engaged.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': 'You make them feel essential to the culture, not just the roster. There are practices, film sessions, locker room moments where reserve players set the tone. We make sure they know how much that matters.', 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "They stay ready because they know the opportunity comes. Every player in this program who's prepared has had a moment. Tonight's production is proof of that.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': 'Clear communication and meaningful reps in practice. Reserve players who get good work in practice stay sharp and stay motivated.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "I invest as much coaching energy in the second unit as the first. They run the same system, get the same film attention, and understand the same principles. They're not an afterthought and they know it.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'player_em_up']}]},
    {'id': 'bench_scoring_low_01', 'category': 'team_performance', 'subcategory': 'bench_scoring_low', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'bench_pts', 'filters': {'user_bench_max': 5}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'Your bench was almost a non-factor offensively tonight. Is that a depth problem or a deployment problem?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "A readiness problem. When your bench comes in and doesn't produce, it's because they weren't ready to play at the level the game demanded. That starts in practice and it ends in games like tonight.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': 'Some of both. The deployment decisions were based on what the game required at each moment. The production numbers reflect both how much they played and how well they executed when they did.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "It's something we need to look at honestly. Whether it's depth, deployment, or readiness — it needs to improve over the course of the season.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_down', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "The development gap between our starters and our reserves showed tonight. That's an honest assessment and it's one we'll address in individual player work over the next stretch of games.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_down', 'discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "I'd rather ask whether our bench players feel confident and ready when their number is called. If the answer is no, that's a culture and preparation issue that starts with how we treat the full roster every day in practice.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_down', 'player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}]},
    {'id': 'bench_scoring_low_02', 'category': 'team_performance', 'subcategory': 'bench_scoring_low', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'bench_pts', 'filters': {'user_bench_max': 5}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': "Over a long season, you can't win with just your starters carrying everything. How do you build bench productivity?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': 'You invest in those players as people first. When reserve players feel valued and connected to the mission, they come in ready to compete. That investment has to start well before game night.', 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': 'You give them system ownership. Reserve players who fully understand the scheme can execute it confidently in limited minutes. The problem is usually that second-unit players know less of the system, not that they have less talent.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'player_em_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': 'Consistent reps, clear roles, and meaningful competition in practice. Bench players develop in practice and execute in games. We need to maximize both.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': 'Competition. Make the starters earn their spots every day and give the reserves real opportunities to take them. When the competition is genuine, the whole roster elevates.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Individual development plans for every reserve player. They need to know specifically what they're working on and specifically what production level earns them more minutes. Vague development doesn't produce results.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}]},
    {'id': 'bench_scoring_low_03', 'category': 'team_performance', 'subcategory': 'bench_scoring_low', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'bench_pts', 'filters': {'user_bench_max': 5}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'Does a night like this put more pressure on your starters going forward, knowing they have less margin for error?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "Every player in this program operates under the same standard. Starters know what's expected of them. Tonight they carried the load. That won't always be possible and we need to fix the depth issue.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "It tells me we need to accelerate the development of certain reserve players. The starters can't carry the whole season. That's not sustainable and it's not fair to them.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "Somewhat. But good starters know how to manage their energy and effort over forty minutes. Tonight they did. We need to build depth so they don't have to do that every night.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_down', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': 'I try not to frame it as pressure. I frame it as an opportunity for the starters to continue leading and an opportunity for the reserves to step up. Both of those narratives are true. Both require response.', 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "It means we'll need to be more strategic in managing starter minutes. If the bench can't sustain, the starters need to be protected through rotation timing. That's a scheme and game-management adjustment.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}]},
    {'id': 'bench_scoring_low_04', 'category': 'team_performance', 'subcategory': 'bench_scoring_low', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'bench_pts', 'filters': {'user_bench_max': 5}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'Is bench production something your program is actively recruiting to address, or do you believe the current roster can develop enough to solve it?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "I believe in development first. The talent to produce is on this roster. The question is whether the developmental investment is producing results fast enough. If it's not, recruiting becomes more urgent.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': 'We recruit for depth the same way we recruit for everything — on merit and fit. Right now my focus is on developing what we have. Recruiting is ongoing and will address the depth as the next classes come in.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "Both, honestly. You develop what you have and recruit to strengthen what you're missing. That's what every program does.", 'effect_tags': ['red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': 'We recruit players who want to be here and compete for something. Depth comes from that culture. Players who are invested in the program are the ones who make you hard to beat off the bench.', 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fan_interest_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "The system is designed to maximize every player on the roster. If reserve players are underproducing, the question is whether the system exposure is deep enough. We'll address that specifically before looking at personnel changes.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}]},
    {'id': 'three_point_hot_01', 'category': 'team_performance', 'subcategory': 'three_point_hot', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'three_pt_pct', 'filters': {'user_min_pct': 40, 'user_min_attempts': 10}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'You shot it extremely well from three tonight. Was that the game plan or did it evolve from how the defense was playing you?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': 'We targeted specific looks off specific actions based on our scouting. When those looks came — and they came because of how they defended — our players had the confidence to take them. Preparation meeting execution.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': 'A bit of both. We always want to attack the three-point line when the defense gives it to us. Tonight they gave it to us a lot and we made them pay.', 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': 'We took what they gave us. When the defense gives you threes, you shoot threes. Our guys were ready to shoot them and did.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': 'Players were getting to their spots and shooting with rhythm and confidence. When individual players trust their shot within the flow of the offense, results like tonight happen.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': 'We found shooters. The ball moved and found the open man. When your players trust each other enough to keep making that extra pass, the shooters get clean looks and clean looks fall.', 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}]},
    {'id': 'three_point_hot_02', 'category': 'team_performance', 'subcategory': 'three_point_hot', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'three_pt_pct', 'filters': {'user_min_pct': 40, 'user_min_attempts': 10}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': "Three-point shooting can be volatile game to game. How do you build a program that's consistently good from range rather than hot-and-cold?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': 'You build the scheme around shot quality first. High-percentage three-point attempts — corner kicks, rhythm pull-ups off the dribble — are more consistent than contested catch-and-shoot threes. Discipline the shot selection and the variance drops.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Individual shooting development. Repetition, footwork, release consistency — those reduce the variance over time. Shooters who can replicate their mechanics under pressure are consistent shooters. That's developmental work, not luck.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': 'You build shooters in practice and you hold them to a shot selection standard in games. Good shooters taking good shots produce consistent results. Those are both coachable.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "Honest assessment of who your shooters are and building an offense that gets them open looks. You can't force consistency — you can only maximize the conditions for it.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': 'Confidence and rhythm. Players who trust their teammates to get them the ball in the right spots, and who play freely rather than mechanically, shoot more consistently. The culture supports the shot.', 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_up']}]},
    {'id': 'three_point_hot_03', 'category': 'team_performance', 'subcategory': 'three_point_hot', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'three_pt_pct', 'filters': {'user_min_pct': 40, 'user_min_attempts': 10}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'A night like this forces opponents to adjust. How do you expect them to come back and try to take the three away next time?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "They'll extend their defense and try to take away the catch. That opens the drive. We'll be ready. The system has answers for defensive adjustments — that's part of what we install.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': 'Let them try to take it away. Every adjustment they make opens something else. Our players are prepared to attack whatever they give us.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "They'll shade coverage toward our shooters. We'll have to work harder to get open and we'll have to attack off the close-out. That's an adjustment we can make.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': 'Individual players who can create off the dribble become more important when the defense extends. We have those players. When the perimeter gets contested, we go to our drives and our pull-up game.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "They'll try to disrupt our rhythm — more pressure, more switching. Our answer is to keep moving the ball and trusting each other to find the next open player. That unselfishness is what beats defensive adjustments.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'discipline_up']}]},
    {'id': 'three_point_hot_04', 'category': 'team_performance', 'subcategory': 'three_point_hot', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'three_pt_pct', 'filters': {'user_min_pct': 40, 'user_min_attempts': 10}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'Is there a risk that a hot shooting night leads to over-reliance on the three-point shot going forward?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "Not in this program. I have shot selection standards and players know what they are. Hot or cold, the standard doesn't change.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "The system governs shot selection, not recent results. Players are trained to read what the defense gives them, not to hunt shots based on last game's percentage. That's the discipline we install.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "It's a real risk. We'll address it on film — reinforce the right shot selection decisions and flag anything that was fortune rather than process.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "I'll have individual conversations with each player about their shot selection tonight — good and bad. You want them confident but disciplined. Hot nights can inflate confidence beyond what the shot selection warrants.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "The team's reaction to a hot night tells you a lot about its maturity. When players celebrate good ball movement and right decisions rather than just made shots, they're less susceptible to that drift.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'discipline_up']}]},
    {'id': 'three_point_cold_01', 'category': 'team_performance', 'subcategory': 'three_point_cold', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'three_pt_pct', 'filters': {'user_max_pct': 20, 'user_min_attempts': 10}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': "The three-point shooting was really difficult tonight. When that's not falling, how do you adjust on the fly?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "You redirect the offense toward interior attack. The scheme has built-in reads that adjust based on defensive response. When the three isn't falling, you drive, you post, you get to the free throw line.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "You keep attacking and you don't change your process. Good shots that don't fall tonight will fall tomorrow. The problem isn't the scheme — it was the execution today.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "You try to get easier looks. Attack the paint, get to the free throw line, take what the defense gives you rather than forcing threes that aren't going in.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "You move the ball to your most reliable mid-range and interior players. When the perimeter game isn't there, certain individual players become more important. We have to find those guys quickly.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "You trust each other on the other end. When the shots aren't falling, the answer is always defense. Lock in defensively as a group and let the offense come from stops rather than forcing it.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up']}]},
    {'id': 'three_point_cold_02', 'category': 'team_performance', 'subcategory': 'three_point_cold', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'three_pt_pct', 'filters': {'user_max_pct': 20, 'user_min_attempts': 10}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': "Was it a shot selection problem, a defensive contest problem, or just one of those nights where shots don't fall?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "We'll look at the film and categorize every three-point attempt. Contested, uncontested, in-rhythm, off-balance. Until we do that, I'm not going to assign blame to variance versus decision-making.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Some of both, honestly. There were contested threes we shouldn't have taken and some open ones that didn't fall. I'll address the shot selection with specific players and accept the variance on the rest.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "Shot selection. I saw too many contested threes and threes that weren't in our flow. We have standards for when we shoot them and we violated those standards tonight.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "Some nights shots don't fall even when you do everything right. We'll look at the film and separate legitimate shot selection issues from variance. They require different responses.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_down', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "When shots aren't falling, the answer is to increase ball movement and trust. Too often teams tighten up and start iso-ing when it's cold. We went away from our system tonight and that made it worse.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_down', 'discipline_up']}]},
    {'id': 'three_point_cold_03', 'category': 'team_performance', 'subcategory': 'three_point_cold', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'three_pt_pct', 'filters': {'user_max_pct': 20, 'user_min_attempts': 10}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': "A cold shooting night can affect the whole team's rhythm. How do you keep players mentally in it when shots aren't going down?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': 'You redirect their energy to what they can control. Defense, rebounding, communication. When the shots stop falling, the best thing a player can do is compete harder on the other end. We talk about that constantly.', 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "You play through it. Mental toughness is specifically about competing when results aren't going your way. The players who can do that earn minutes in this program.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "You focus on the next possession. You can't un-miss a shot. You can make the next defensive play or the next smart pass. Stay present.", 'effect_tags': ['fight_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Individual conversations during timeouts and dead balls. Remind specific players of what they do well beyond shooting. Redirect their confidence toward what's working rather than what isn't.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "You find ways to get them in rhythm. Drive and kick creates open threes and layups. When players attack in transition and get to the line, the shooting opens up. You don't abandon the shooters — you rebuild their rhythm through the system.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'player_em_up']}]},
    {'id': 'three_point_cold_04', 'category': 'team_performance', 'subcategory': 'three_point_cold', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'three_pt_pct', 'filters': {'user_max_pct': 20, 'user_min_attempts': 10}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': "Should your team have gone away from the three-point shot earlier tonight when it became clear it wasn't working?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "The scheme adjusts based on shot quality, not results. If the looks were good but they weren't falling, you continue taking them. If the looks became poor, we should have adjusted sooner. I need to look at the film to tell you which applies tonight.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "If the shots were within our shot selection standards, no. You don't abandon a system because of variance. If they weren't within the standards, then yes — we should have adjusted. Both are on the table tonight.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "Possibly. We'll look at the film and evaluate whether better shot selection would have produced more efficient offense. It's a fair question.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_down', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "For some players, yes. There are players who force threes when their shot isn't there rather than finding something they can make. That's an individual decision-making issue and we'll address it specifically.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_down', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "I think we pressed. When shots aren't falling, players try harder to make them rather than trusting the offense to create better looks. That tension is what we need to manage better as a group.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_down', 'discipline_up']}]},
    {'id': 'unanswered_run_user_01', 'category': 'team_performance', 'subcategory': 'unanswered_run_user', 'tier': 2, 'requires_tracking': True, 'trigger': {'condition': 'unanswered_run', 'filters': {'user_run_min': 10}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'Your team went on a big run tonight that changed the game. What triggered it?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "Energy. When this group gets locked in together and starts competing at a high level on both ends, momentum builds fast. One play leads to another and it becomes contagious. That's the team showing what it can be.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up', 'team_mo_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "A specific defensive sequence that created transition opportunities. We got stops, we converted, and their offense started pressing. Once that cycle starts — stops into scores into defensive pressure — it's hard to break.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up', 'team_mo_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': 'We got some momentum going and fed off it. Those runs happen when a team is competing hard and making plays on both ends.', 'effect_tags': ['team_mo_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': 'Defensive intensity. Runs start on defense. When we clamped down and forced stops, the offense fed off that energy and the run built from there.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'team_mo_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Individual players elevating at the same time. When two or three guys get locked in simultaneously, momentum builds quickly. Tonight it cascaded across the whole group and we couldn't be stopped for a stretch.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'fight_up', 'team_mo_up']}]},
    {'id': 'unanswered_run_user_02', 'category': 'team_performance', 'subcategory': 'unanswered_run_user', 'tier': 2, 'requires_tracking': True, 'trigger': {'condition': 'unanswered_run', 'filters': {'user_run_min': 10}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'When you go on a big run like that, what are you looking for from the opponent that might stop the momentum?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "A timeout and a schematic counter. Good coaches identify what's fueling the run and call time to disrupt the rhythm. We prepare our team for that — the run ends when they call time and we have to rebuild it from scratch.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "One made basket. That's usually what stops a run. You have to keep the defensive intensity from letting them exhale. If they can't score, the momentum doesn't break.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "A timeout and a reset. That's what coaches do. We try to maintain our level on both sides of the ball through any stoppage.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "Their best player getting a bucket and changing the feeling in their building. You stay locked in and you don't give them that emotional relief. The collective focus has to hold through any response.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "A single player who makes a big individual play. That's what breaks runs — one person who refuses to let it continue. We prepare our players to be that person for us, and to recognize when an opponent has that player.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}]},
    {'id': 'unanswered_run_user_03', 'category': 'team_performance', 'subcategory': 'unanswered_run_user', 'tier': 2, 'requires_tracking': True, 'trigger': {'condition': 'unanswered_run', 'filters': {'user_run_min': 10}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'Do you think about manufacturing runs, or do you see them as emergent from the way you play?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "You can manufacture the conditions for runs — specific defensive pressure schemes, transition actions, timeout management. You can't manufacture the run itself. You build the conditions and let the players create it.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': 'You create them with defensive intensity. I tell my teams that if they defend hard enough, the offense will follow. The run is always an output of the defensive end.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "Both. You set up the conditions — tempo, pressure, matchups — but ultimately the players have to make the plays. You can't script a run.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "Runs come from collective energy. You can build the culture that makes your team capable of going on runs, but you can't call a timeout and prescribe one. You cultivate the soil and the players grow the tree.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "I look at which players create energy and try to have them on the floor when we need a spark. But the run has to come from authentic competitive play — you can sequence the players but you can't force the basketball.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}]},
    {'id': 'unanswered_run_user_04', 'category': 'team_performance', 'subcategory': 'unanswered_run_user', 'tier': 2, 'requires_tracking': True, 'trigger': {'condition': 'unanswered_run', 'filters': {'user_run_min': 10}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'After a run like that, is there a risk your team lets up expecting the game to be in hand?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "I address it immediately. The standard is forty minutes. A ten-point run doesn't change what we're expected to do on the next possession. I don't let them exhale.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "We talk about it constantly — finishing is part of the character of this team. You don't let up because you've built a lead. You keep competing for each other.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "It's always a risk. We try to maintain the standard through runs in both directions. How you respond to your own success is just as important as how you respond to adversity.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "The system keeps them focused because there's always a next assignment. Players executing a scheme don't have time to coast. The next read is always there. That structure prevents the mental let-down.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'team_mo_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': 'I watch individual body language carefully after a run. The players who stay locked in are the ones I want on the floor. The ones who start celebrating before the game is over get addressed at the next stoppage.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}]},
    {'id': 'unanswered_run_opponent_01', 'category': 'team_performance', 'subcategory': 'unanswered_run_opponent', 'tier': 2, 'requires_tracking': True, 'trigger': {'condition': 'unanswered_run', 'filters': {'opponent_run_min': 10}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'Your opponent went on a big run tonight. What did you see that allowed that to happen?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "We stopped executing the defensive scheme for a stretch. Runs don't happen in a vacuum — they happen because something breaks down on your side. We have specific things to address on film.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "Defensive lapses and offensive turnovers feeding each other. Once the cycle starts — turnover, their score, our frustration, another turnover — it builds quickly. We needed to break it and we didn't fast enough.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "We lost our defensive focus for a stretch and they made us pay. That's something we'll address going forward.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_down', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "We lost our collective composure. One bad play led to another and we started playing as individuals trying to fix it rather than as a team absorbing it together. That's when runs get out of hand.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_down', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "A few players stopped competing at the level they needed to. When two or three players check out mentally during a run, it affects everyone. Those individuals know who they are and we'll address it.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_down', 'discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}]},
    {'id': 'unanswered_run_opponent_02', 'category': 'team_performance', 'subcategory': 'unanswered_run_opponent', 'tier': 2, 'requires_tracking': True, 'trigger': {'condition': 'unanswered_run', 'filters': {'opponent_run_min': 10}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'When your team is getting run on, when do you decide to call a timeout versus letting the team work through it?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "Three consecutive scores for the opponent is usually my threshold. At that point the run has structural causes that need a coach's intervention, not just player response.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "I want to see whether they can stop it themselves first. If they can, that's character being built. If they can't, I intervene. Tonight we needed more of both and I'll evaluate whether I timed the timeout correctly.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': 'You look for the moment when the run is becoming psychological as well as tactical. Once it starts affecting body language and decision-making, you have to stop it.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "You watch the team's spirit. If they're staying together, competing, communicating — you let them fight through it. If the body language is breaking down, you step in immediately. The culture tells you which situation you're in.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': 'I look for which individual player can break the run. If that player is on the floor and competing, I let them try. If not, I make a sub or call a timeout to get the right player in the right moment.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}]},
    {'id': 'unanswered_run_opponent_03', 'category': 'team_performance', 'subcategory': 'unanswered_run_opponent', 'tier': 2, 'requires_tracking': True, 'trigger': {'condition': 'unanswered_run', 'filters': {'opponent_run_min': 10}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'Did that run ultimately decide the game, or were you able to recover?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "We recovered. Runs happen to every team. What matters is how you respond. We responded well enough tonight. What I'm focused on now is preventing the run in the first place.", 'effect_tags': ['fight_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "We pulled together after the timeout and answered. That's who this group is — they don't fold. But we can't keep putting ourselves in those positions. We have to be better at preventing the run before it starts.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "We responded reasonably well. The run didn't define the game entirely, but it made things harder than they needed to be.", 'effect_tags': ['red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "We came out of the timeout with two specific adjustments and stopped the run. The recovery showed the system's resilience. The focus now is on understanding what allowed the run in the first place.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Individual players stepped up and stopped it. That's credit to them. But I also want to look at who on the floor contributed to it starting. Both are important conversations for development.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}]},
    {'id': 'unanswered_run_opponent_04', 'category': 'team_performance', 'subcategory': 'unanswered_run_opponent', 'tier': 2, 'requires_tracking': True, 'trigger': {'condition': 'unanswered_run', 'filters': {'opponent_run_min': 10}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': "How do you build a team that's harder to run on — that doesn't give up those extended scoring droughts?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "You develop players who are mentally consistent. Runs happen to teams with inconsistent mental effort. When every player maintains competitive intensity regardless of score or momentum, you're harder to run on.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "You build in system checkpoints — reads and rules that reset the team's behavior regardless of what just happened. Systems that require attention keep players from drifting during momentum swings.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "Standards. High standards for defensive effort and ball security don't disappear when you're on a cold stretch. That's what you build in practice — a standard that holds regardless of the scoreboard.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "Composure and communication. Teams that stay composed and keep talking during tough stretches stop runs faster. Those are coachable attributes and we'll keep working on them.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': 'You build the kind of relationships where players hold each other accountable in the moment. When a player goes cold, his teammates bring him back. That collective accountability is what prevents runs from becoming crises.', 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up', 'discipline_up']}]},
    {'id': 'first_blood_user_01', 'category': 'team_performance', 'subcategory': 'first_blood_user', 'tier': 2, 'requires_tracking': True, 'trigger': {'condition': 'first_blood', 'filters': {'user_scored_first_min': 5}}, 'weight': 1, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'You came out of the gate aggressively tonight, scoring the first several points. Is that something you specifically emphasize?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "Absolutely. Setting the tone in the first four minutes tells the opponent who they're dealing with. We don't ease into games. We attack.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'team_mo_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "We have a specific game-opening action package. We want to run plays we've prepared in the first four minutes before either team has made adjustments. Tonight it worked exactly as installed.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up', 'team_mo_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': 'We talk about starting with purpose. A strong start sets the tone defensively and offensively. Tonight the guys came out ready.', 'effect_tags': ['team_mo_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "It's a mindset thing. We talk about playing with urgency from the jump — not because the game is won or lost in the first few minutes, but because how you start says something about your intent.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up', 'team_mo_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "We prepare players for exactly this — specific opening looks that play into their strengths. When players start with confidence because they're getting shots they've practiced, the rest of the game builds from there.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up', 'team_mo_up']}]},
    {'id': 'first_blood_user_02', 'category': 'team_performance', 'subcategory': 'first_blood_user', 'tier': 2, 'requires_tracking': True, 'trigger': {'condition': 'first_blood', 'filters': {'user_scored_first_min': 5}}, 'weight': 1, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'Does a fast start change how you approach the rest of the game, or does the game plan stay the same regardless?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "The game plan stays consistent. A fast start validates preparation, but it doesn't change the scheme or the principles we're executing. We stay disciplined to the plan regardless of the score.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "Same standard throughout. Whether we're up five or down five after the first few minutes, the expectations don't change. We play to our level for forty minutes.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "The game plan stays the same. A fast start creates a little margin but you can't let it change your approach. Complacency after a fast start has killed plenty of games.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': 'I want players to play with freedom when we have early momentum. A fast start builds confidence and I want them to play within that confidence rather than tightening up to protect it.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'team_mo_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "We capitalize on the energy. A fast start creates collective momentum that feeds off itself. You don't change the plan but you do want to sustain the spirit that created the start.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up']}]},
    {'id': 'first_blood_user_03', 'category': 'team_performance', 'subcategory': 'first_blood_user', 'tier': 2, 'requires_tracking': True, 'trigger': {'condition': 'first_blood', 'filters': {'user_scored_first_min': 5}}, 'weight': 1, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'Good teams respond well to facing a deficit early. Were you surprised by how long it took them to get back into it?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "We disrupted their early rhythm, which disrupted their individual confidence. When you take a team's best players out of their normal flow early, they take longer to establish themselves. That's by design.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "We didn't let them. Our defense didn't give them easy opportunities to climb back. We made them earn every basket. That's what a fast start is supposed to do — extend the gap.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "We played well enough to keep the pressure on after the start. That's what matters — maintaining the advantage rather than letting it evaporate.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': 'We made specific adjustments to prevent their early offense from finding rhythm. We anticipated their response and had counters built in. That preparation window after a fast start is critical.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "We competed hard enough on defense to keep them off-rhythm. When the whole group is locked in and communicating, it's hard for any team to get comfortable. We had that collective defensive focus tonight.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up']}]},
    {'id': 'first_blood_user_04', 'category': 'team_performance', 'subcategory': 'first_blood_user', 'tier': 2, 'requires_tracking': True, 'trigger': {'condition': 'first_blood', 'filters': {'user_scored_first_min': 5}}, 'weight': 1, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'How much of a fast start is preparation versus the players simply being ready to compete?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "Preparation creates the readiness. You can't separate them. Players come out ready because they know exactly what they're running. The confidence to attack in the first possession comes from the work done before the game.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "The readiness comes from the culture. Players who are excited to compete for each other don't need a pep talk to come out fast. The preparation gives them the tools but the culture gives them the will.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "Standard preparation. This is what we practice. The readiness is built into the routine. You come in prepared, you execute what you've prepared, and a fast start is the result.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': 'Both play a role. Preparation creates the structure for a fast start, but the players have to bring the energy. Tonight they brought both.', 'effect_tags': ['red_herring']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Individual readiness is the real driver. A player who has prepared his craft, knows his spots, and trusts his preparation comes out aggressive. Tonight those players set the tone. That's individual preparation showing up as collective performance.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}]},
    {'id': 'first_blood_opponent_01', 'category': 'team_performance', 'subcategory': 'first_blood_opponent', 'tier': 2, 'requires_tracking': True, 'trigger': {'condition': 'first_blood', 'filters': {'opponent_scored_first_min': 5}}, 'weight': 1, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'Your team was slow out of the gate tonight. What does a slow start cost you?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "It costs you momentum and it costs you confidence in the first unit. You're spending energy trying to catch up instead of pressing your own agenda. We can't continue to do this.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'team_mo_down']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': 'It costs you the game plan advantage. When you give up early points, opponents gain confidence in their actions. They start believing their game plan works. We gave them that belief early and had to work twice as hard to take it back.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_down', 'team_mo_down']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "It costs you the early energy. You spend the first quarter reacting rather than dictating. That's not ideal, though tonight we were able to recover.", 'effect_tags': ['team_mo_down', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "It costs you the feeling of competing together from the start. When you're behind early, you can press and start playing as individuals. We have to find a way to get that collective readiness from the opening tip.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_down', 'fight_up', 'team_mo_down']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': 'It costs certain players their rhythm. Players who need to feel their way into a game create slow starts. I need to identify who those players are and address it — whether through preparation, matchups, or sequencing.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_down', 'discipline_up', 'team_mo_down']}]},
    {'id': 'first_blood_opponent_02', 'category': 'team_performance', 'subcategory': 'first_blood_opponent', 'tier': 2, 'requires_tracking': True, 'trigger': {'condition': 'first_blood', 'filters': {'opponent_scored_first_min': 5}}, 'weight': 1, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'Is slow starting a recurring pattern for this team, or was tonight an anomaly?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "It's a pattern we've identified. We're addressing it specifically in preparation — game-opening actions, first defensive possession rules, and timeout management in the first four minutes. Patterns have causes and those causes are correctable.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "It's a pattern and it will stop. I'm not going to accept slow starts as part of who we are. This program competes from the opening tip. End of discussion.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "We've had some spotty starts this season. It's something we're aware of and working on. There's no single fix — it requires attention to detail across multiple things.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_down', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Pattern. Certain players need more of a warm-up period before they're at competitive intensity. That's developmental work — building the mental muscle to be ready immediately rather than working into the game.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_down', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "We've had slow starts when the team's mindset isn't fully locked in before tip-off. That's a culture and preparation conversation that happens before the game, not during it. We're working on the pre-game routine.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_down', 'discipline_up']}]},
    {'id': 'first_blood_opponent_03', 'category': 'team_performance', 'subcategory': 'first_blood_opponent', 'tier': 2, 'requires_tracking': True, 'trigger': {'condition': 'first_blood', 'filters': {'opponent_scored_first_min': 5}}, 'weight': 1, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'What does the locker room look like after a slow start? How do you recalibrate without panicking?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "Direct. You name what's happening, you give them exactly what you need from them, and you send them back out. No excess emotion. Clarity and standard. That's what the locker room gets from me.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "Specific adjustments. What did they run? What did we give up? Here's the counter. You make it concrete and executable so they go back out with answers, not anxiety.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'team_mo_down']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "You keep it calm and focused. It's early. The game isn't over. You make the necessary adjustments and remind them they're capable of competing.", 'effect_tags': ['team_mo_down', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "You bring the energy back to collective purpose. You remind them who they are and who they're playing for. You can't chase points — you can only reconnect to what makes you good.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Individual check-ins. I need to know quickly who is ready to compete and who isn't. I make adjustments — subs, matchup changes, role clarifications — and I make them fast. Slow starts require quick decisions.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}]},
    {'id': 'first_blood_opponent_04', 'category': 'team_performance', 'subcategory': 'first_blood_opponent', 'tier': 2, 'requires_tracking': True, 'trigger': {'condition': 'first_blood', 'filters': {'opponent_scored_first_min': 5}}, 'weight': 1, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'What would it mean for this team to start games with the same energy they sometimes show in the second half?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': 'It would mean we become very hard to beat. The second half energy is who this team can be. The work is bringing that urgency and togetherness to the first possession of the game, not the twenty-first.', 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "It would mean we don't have to fight out of holes we created ourselves. Second half energy first half means forty minutes of full-effort basketball. That's our standard and we'll get there.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "It would make us significantly harder to beat. The games we've come back in this year show what this team is capable of. Bringing that from the start is the goal.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "It would compress the variance in our results significantly. Late-game execution is where our system shines. Applying that execution from tip-off rather than building to it — that's the next step for this program.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "It would mean individual players have made the mental jump to playing at full intensity from the opening possession. That's a professional attribute and it's exactly what we're working to develop. It would take this team to another level.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}]},
    {'id': 'lead_changes_high_01', 'category': 'team_performance', 'subcategory': 'lead_changes_high', 'tier': 2, 'requires_tracking': True, 'trigger': {'condition': 'lead_changes', 'filters': {'min_changes': 10}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'The lead changed hands many times tonight. What does a game like that demand from a coaching staff and a roster?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "Composure and scheme fidelity. In a back-and-forth game, the team that stays committed to its principles — rather than chasing the score emotionally — usually wins. It's a test of system discipline under prolonged pressure.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': 'Mental toughness. When the game goes back and forth, the team that holds its standard on every possession wins the one that matters most. Everything else is noise.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "Composure and focus. You can't let the lead changes affect your decision-making or your energy. Stay in the process and let the game come to you.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "Trust. When the lead keeps flipping, players who trust each other stay together. Players who don't start looking for someone to blame. Tonight we had the trust. That's why we competed all the way through.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': 'Individual consistency. In a game like tonight, the player who gives you the same thing on every possession — offensively and defensively — is the player you build around. It reveals the mentally stable players on your roster.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}]},
    {'id': 'lead_changes_high_02', 'category': 'team_performance', 'subcategory': 'lead_changes_high', 'tier': 2, 'requires_tracking': True, 'trigger': {'condition': 'lead_changes', 'filters': {'min_changes': 10}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'In a game that volatile, how do you manage your bench and your timeout strategy differently than a more controlled game?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "You conserve timeouts for scheme resets rather than momentum stops. In a volatile game, timeouts are your best tool for breaking opponent runs. You can't spend them all early and have nothing left when it matters most.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': 'Rotations stay tighter. In a game that close, you need your best players on the floor in crunch time. I limit the depth of rotation and extend the minutes of the players I trust most.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "You stay flexible. You're reacting to the game more than executing a preset rotation plan. Energy management and matchup awareness become more important.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "I watch the body language on the bench as much as on the floor. In a volatile game, bench energy is critical. I try to put players in when the energy is right — when they're ready to add to the collective rather than detract from it.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': 'Individual matchup management becomes primary. In a back-and-forth game, you identify the advantage matchups and exploit them. Timeouts go toward creating those opportunities rather than pure emotional management.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}]},
    {'id': 'lead_changes_high_03', 'category': 'team_performance', 'subcategory': 'lead_changes_high', 'tier': 2, 'requires_tracking': True, 'trigger': {'condition': 'lead_changes', 'filters': {'min_changes': 10}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'A game with that many lead changes suggests neither team could establish sustained control. Is that frustrating or is it what you want?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': 'Frustrating. I want to establish control and hold it. A game that volatile means neither team dominated a phase of the game. We have to be better at sustaining leads and maintaining defensive intensity when we have momentum.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "Neither. It tells me the systems were evenly matched. What determines the winner in those games is execution on the final possessions. That's where we need to be better.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "Both, honestly. You want to control games. But back-and-forth games test character and we competed well. There's value in both results.", 'effect_tags': ['red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "I love the fact that we competed in it — that we kept coming back when they went ahead. I don't love the fact that we couldn't hold leads when we had them. That's the next thing to develop.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "It tells me we have enough talent to compete with anyone but enough inconsistency to be beaten by anyone. The margin between those two things is individual development. That's motivating to me.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}]},
    {'id': 'lead_changes_high_04', 'category': 'team_performance', 'subcategory': 'lead_changes_high', 'tier': 2, 'requires_tracking': True, 'trigger': {'condition': 'lead_changes', 'filters': {'min_changes': 10}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'In a game that unpredictable, what separates the team that wins from the team that loses?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "Who wants it more for each other. In a game like tonight, the talent is essentially even. What tips it is the team that makes the next play for someone else rather than trying to be the hero. That's a culture answer.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "The harder team. In a game that close, the team that competes harder on the final five possessions wins. Talent doesn't decide those games — will does.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': 'Execution on the most important possessions. Both teams are going to make and miss plays. The team that makes the right play at the most important moment wins.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "Scheme clarity at the end. When the game is close, teams that know exactly what they're running and why are calmer and more decisive. Confusion loses games in overtime situations. Clarity wins them.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "The best individual player in a pressure moment. When it's that close, one player on one possession decides it. Developing players who can be that person — who rise rather than shrink in big moments — is what close games come down to.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}]},
    {'id': 'clutch_time_advantage_01', 'category': 'team_performance', 'subcategory': 'clutch_time_advantage', 'tier': 2, 'requires_tracking': True, 'trigger': {'condition': 'clutch_time_scoring', 'filters': {'user_outscored_q4_final_2min': True}}, 'weight': 3, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'Your team outscored the opponent in the final two minutes of the fourth quarter. Is being a clutch team something you build deliberately?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "Absolutely. We have a specific late-game execution package — plays, spacing, actions — that we practice in simulated pressure situations. When you've run a play in practice with the clock under two minutes a hundred times, you can run it in a game with the same calm.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up', 'team_mo_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "You build it by holding your standard in practice under difficult conditions. Clutch performance in games is a direct output of whether you've been competing at a high level when things are hard in practice. We have.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': 'You prepare for it and you put your best players in position to succeed. The rest is competition and execution. Tonight we executed.', 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "You build the relationships that hold under pressure. In those final two minutes, players are making decisions for each other or they're not. Tonight they were. That trust is what we've built all season.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "You identify which players rise in pressure situations and make sure they're on the floor in those moments. And you develop the others — work on the mental preparation, the breathing, the process — so the gap between your clutch players and non-clutch players narrows.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}]},
    {'id': 'clutch_time_advantage_02', 'category': 'team_performance', 'subcategory': 'clutch_time_advantage', 'tier': 2, 'requires_tracking': True, 'trigger': {'condition': 'clutch_time_scoring', 'filters': {'user_outscored_q4_final_2min': True}}, 'weight': 3, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'What do the final two minutes of a close game look like from the coaching side — how much is scheme and how much is player instinct?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': 'More scheme than people think. In the final two minutes, both teams are exhausted and emotions are high. The team that has specific answers — not general ideas — executes more cleanly. We invest heavily in late-game specificity.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "Mostly player instinct built on preparation. You call a play and trust your players to execute it. You can't over-coach in the moment. You prepare them, you set them up, and then you get out of the way.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': 'A mix of both. You have a plan, but you have to read the game and trust your players to make plays within it. The best late-game teams have both.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "More player instinct than fans realize. By the final two minutes, the coaching is mostly done. What you're watching is whether the relationships and the trust you've built hold under maximum pressure. Tonight they did.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "In the final two minutes, I'm thinking matchups and individual reads. Who has the best chance on this possession against this defender? I try to create the highest-percentage individual opportunity and trust that player to execute it.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}]},
    {'id': 'clutch_time_advantage_03', 'category': 'team_performance', 'subcategory': 'clutch_time_advantage', 'tier': 2, 'requires_tracking': True, 'trigger': {'condition': 'clutch_time_scoring', 'filters': {'user_outscored_q4_final_2min': True}}, 'weight': 3, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'Being able to outscore teams in crunch time is a meaningful competitive advantage. How sustainable is that?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "It's sustainable if the players performing in those moments keep developing. Clutch performance isn't random — it's a skill that grows with experience and preparation. These players are getting better at it every game.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "Very sustainable, because it's system-based. Our late-game actions aren't relying on one player making a hero play. They're designed to create advantages and they work consistently because the design is sound.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "It depends on execution. Crunch time performance can be variable. But we believe in our preparation and our players. We've shown we can compete in those moments.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "Sustainable for as long as we hold our standard. Clutch performance is a product of discipline and mental toughness built over a whole season. You don't lose that overnight — but you can erode it if you let the standard slip.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "As sustainable as the trust in that locker room. Teams that play for each other in big moments do it game after game because the culture that produces it doesn't disappear between games. We're building something real here.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'prestige_minor_up', 'fan_interest_up']}]},
    {'id': 'clutch_time_advantage_04', 'category': 'team_performance', 'subcategory': 'clutch_time_advantage', 'tier': 2, 'requires_tracking': True, 'trigger': {'condition': 'clutch_time_scoring', 'filters': {'user_outscored_q4_final_2min': True}}, 'weight': 3, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'Is there a player on this team you trust above all others in the final two minutes? What makes them that player?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "I trust this whole group in the final two minutes. That's not a diplomatic answer — it's the truth. When the culture is right, you have five players who want the ball and want to make the play for each other. That's more dangerous than one designated hero.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "I'll keep that between me and the locker room. What I'll say is that the players who earn trust in the final two minutes earn it through every other minute first. The standard is the same — they just hold it when others can't.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "We have players we put in position to succeed at the end of games. I don't want to single anyone out publicly — that creates pressure and expectations that can be counterproductive.", 'effect_tags': ['red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "There are players who execute the late-game scheme with exceptional precision. What makes them that player isn't heroism — it's the willingness to stay within the system when everything is on the line. That's rarer than raw talent.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "There are players on this team who have shown the mental makeup to perform in the final two minutes — specific technical skills, composure, good decision-making. I invest in developing that in the full roster, but yes — there are players I trust above others and they've earned that trust.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}]},
    {'id': 'high_scorer_01', 'category': 'player_performance', 'subcategory': 'high_scorer', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'player_pts', 'filters': {'min_pts': 25}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': 'high_scorer', 'text': '{player_name} had a big scoring night. What were you seeing from {player_name} that made {player_name} so hard to guard?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "{player_name} was getting to the right spots and making decisions within the skill set. When {player_name} plays within {player_name}'s game rather than forcing things, this is what's possible. That's development showing up.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': 'The system created the looks and {player_name} converted. We designed actions specifically around what {player_name} does best. When that alignment is there, good things happen.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "{player_name} was locked in tonight. {player_name} shot it well and made good decisions. That's what you hope for from your scorers.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "{player_name} executed the game plan. {player_name} took what the defense gave {player_name} and didn't deviate. That's all we ask.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "The team got {player_name} great looks. It's easy to score twenty-five when your teammates are making the right reads and finding you. That's a team effort as much as an individual one.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}]},
    {'id': 'high_scorer_02', 'category': 'player_performance', 'subcategory': 'high_scorer', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'player_pts', 'filters': {'min_pts': 25}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': 'high_scorer', 'text': 'Is a night like this what you expect from {player_name} on a regular basis?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': 'I expect {player_name} to hold the standard every night. The scoring is a product of that. When the standard is met, results like tonight follow.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "This is closer to {player_name}'s ceiling than {player_name}'s floor. The development arc says {player_name} should be here more nights than not. Tonight {player_name} proved the ceiling is real.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': 'We expect {player_name} to compete at a high level. Specific point totals vary, but this level of engagement and decision-making — yes, we expect that.', 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': 'When the matchup creates these opportunities and {player_name} executes at this level — yes. The system will continue to put {player_name} in position. Whether {player_name} continues to convert is an execution question.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': 'When {player_name} is playing for the team and not for the stat line, you see nights like this. I expect the attitude that led to this performance. The scoring takes care of itself from there.', 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_up']}]},
    {'id': 'high_scorer_03', 'category': 'player_performance', 'subcategory': 'high_scorer', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'player_pts', 'filters': {'min_pts': 25}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': 'high_scorer', 'text': "How much of {player_name}'s scoring night came from matchup advantage versus {player_name}'s own preparation and skill?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "We identified the matchup advantage in film and built the game plan around exploiting it. {player_name} recognized the reads and executed. That's preparation and skill in equal measure.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': 'Skill. The matchup gave {player_name} opportunities, but not every player converts those opportunities. {player_name} converted because of the work {player_name} has put in. The matchup was a door — {player_name} walked through it.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': 'Both play a role. The matchup was favorable but {player_name} still had to make shots and good decisions. Give {player_name} full credit.', 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': 'Preparation. Matchup advantages exist for every player every game. The players who capitalize are the ones who are ready. {player_name} was ready.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "The matchup gave {player_name} space, but the team's ball movement made it exploitable. I'd give equal credit to the teammates who kept finding {player_name} in the right spots.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_up']}]},
    {'id': 'high_scorer_04', 'category': 'player_performance', 'subcategory': 'high_scorer', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'player_pts', 'filters': {'min_pts': 25}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': 'high_scorer', 'text': 'What do you say to {player_name} after a night like this?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "Same thing I always say — find the mistakes and fix them. A big scoring night doesn't buy {player_name} a pass from the standard. That's respect, not criticism.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': 'I tell {player_name} what worked specifically and why. And I challenge {player_name} to identify what {player_name} would do differently. The best players learn from their best nights as much as their worst ones.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "Good job — now let's look at the film and find what we build on. Acknowledge it and move forward.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "I show {player_name} the two or three possessions where the system broke down even in a big scoring night. You don't want a player thinking a high point total means flawless execution. It never does.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "I make sure {player_name} understands how much {player_name}'s teammates contributed to that night. Then I acknowledge what {player_name} did. The humility and the confidence can coexist — that's what makes a great teammate.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_up']}]},
    {'id': 'top_rebounder_01', 'category': 'player_performance', 'subcategory': 'top_rebounder', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'player_reb', 'filters': {'min_reb': 12}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': 'top_rebounder', 'text': '{player_name} was a force on the glass tonight. What was {player_name} doing that created so many rebounding opportunities?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': 'Physicality and positioning. Rebounding is about wanting the ball more than the person next to you. {player_name} wanted it more tonight.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': '{player_name} followed our boxing-out principles on every possession and read the trajectory well. Rebounding is mostly technique — when the technique is right, the numbers follow.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': '{player_name} was relentless. {player_name} went after every ball and made it happen. That kind of effort on the glass changes games.', 'effect_tags': ['fight_up', 'prestige_minor_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Anticipation. {player_name} has been working on reading shot trajectory and timing {player_name}'s approach. Tonight that work showed up in the numbers.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': 'The whole team blocked out and {player_name} finished it. When everyone does their job on the glass, the best rebounder gets their opportunities. This was a collective effort that {player_name} capped.', 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_up']}]},
    {'id': 'top_rebounder_02', 'category': 'player_performance', 'subcategory': 'top_rebounder', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'player_reb', 'filters': {'min_reb': 12}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': 'top_rebounder', 'text': "Rebounding at that level is an underappreciated skill. How important is {player_name}'s glass work to how your team operates?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': 'Foundational. Rebounding is possession control and possession control is how this system functions. {player_name} dominating the glass means we get more possessions and they get fewer. That compounds over forty minutes.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "{player_name}'s glass work sets a tone for the whole team. When your best rebounder goes after every ball with that kind of intensity, it raises the standard for everyone else. The effort is contagious.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': 'Extremely important. Winning the rebounding battle almost always means winning the game. {player_name} is a big reason we compete on the glass at the level we do.', 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "It's non-negotiable for this program. Rebounding is effort and will. {player_name} brings that every night. It's the foundation of what we do.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Critical. And what makes {player_name} special is that the rebounding comes from {player_name}'s athleticism and {player_name}'s anticipation in equal measure. That combination is what we've been developing and tonight it was on full display.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}]},
    {'id': 'top_rebounder_03', 'category': 'player_performance', 'subcategory': 'top_rebounder', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'player_reb', 'filters': {'min_reb': 12}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': 'top_rebounder', 'text': 'Opponents will look to neutralize {player_name} on the glass next time. How do you adjust for that?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': 'We build counters into the box-out scheme. When they send extra bodies to neutralize {player_name}, that opens up second-chance opportunities for other players. The adjustment to neutralize one rebounder creates vulnerabilities elsewhere.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "You don't. {player_name} keeps competing at the same level regardless of what they do. The answer to extra attention is more effort, not scheme changes.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': 'We prepare for it and look for other rebounders to step up. When they focus on one player, someone else has to take advantage of the opportunity.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "We work on {player_name}'s reads specifically — how to adjust {player_name}'s approach when {player_name} is drawing extra attention. That's a specific skill and we'll develop it further.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "Other guys step up. When {player_name} draws extra attention, somebody else gets an opportunity on the glass. We talk about that as a team — the second rebounder's mindset is just as important as the first.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'discipline_up']}]},
    {'id': 'top_rebounder_04', 'category': 'player_performance', 'subcategory': 'top_rebounder', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'player_reb', 'filters': {'min_reb': 12}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': 'top_rebounder', 'text': 'What does {player_name} still need to develop to become even more dominant as a rebounder?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Outlet passing decision-making. {player_name} gets the ball — now the next play matters as much as the grab. We're developing that read so the rebound converts to points faster.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "Consistency on the defensive glass in transition. Offensive rebounding is there. The discipline to prioritize defensive rebounding positioning on every single trip — that's the next level.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'player_em_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "Positioning in the half-court. The athletic rebounding is already there. Reading the play before the shot goes up consistently — that's what separates good rebounders from elite ones.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "Physicality late in games. {player_name} is physical early. As fatigue sets in, the physicality has to stay at the same level. That's conditioning and mental toughness. We work on it.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'player_em_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "Leadership on the glass. {player_name} does it — now I want {player_name} to communicate that to teammates and elevate the whole group's rebounding intensity. That's the next level of {player_name}'s impact.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_up']}]},
    {'id': 'hot_shooter_01', 'category': 'player_performance', 'subcategory': 'hot_shooter', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'player_three_pt_made', 'filters': {'min_made': 5}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': 'hot_shooter', 'text': "{player_name} was on fire from three tonight. What were you seeing from {player_name}'s shot that was different?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Rhythm and confidence. When {player_name} gets into a rhythm early, the release is quicker and the footwork is cleaner. Tonight {player_name} found it from the first shot and rode it. That's a developed skill.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': 'The system generated high-quality catches for {player_name} — balanced feet, in-rhythm, off the movement we practice. Good-quality threes fall at a higher rate. Tonight the quality was consistently high.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': '{player_name} was in a zone tonight. When a shooter gets going like that, you feed {player_name} and get out of the way.', 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "Execution. {player_name} followed {player_name}'s shot routine and didn't deviate from {player_name}'s spots. Consistency of process produces consistent results.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': 'The ball found {player_name} in the right places because teammates made the right reads. Hot shooting nights come from the whole offense functioning — {player_name} finished what the team created.', 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_up']}]},
    {'id': 'hot_shooter_02', 'category': 'player_performance', 'subcategory': 'hot_shooter', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'player_three_pt_made', 'filters': {'min_made': 5}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': 'hot_shooter', 'text': 'When {player_name} is shooting the ball like that, how does it change how you run your offense?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': 'You run more actions to get {player_name} the ball in the same spots that have been working. The system has sequencing built in for when a shooter gets hot. You exploit it without abandoning the rest of what you do.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "You keep running the offense and let {player_name} shoot when the shots are there. You don't force it but you don't suppress it either. The game plan adjusts to reward what's working.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "You find more ways to get {player_name} open looks. You can't force a shooter's hot streak but you can maximize the number of opportunities {player_name} gets within the system.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': 'You make sure the whole team is trying to find {player_name}. A hot shooter needs teammates who want to feed {player_name} as much as {player_name} wants to shoot. Tonight that trust was mutual.', 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "You get {player_name} the ball in the spots where {player_name} is already in rhythm and let {player_name} read the defense. You don't over-prescribe — when a player is hot, you trust {player_name}'s instincts and get out of the way.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}]},
    {'id': 'hot_shooter_03', 'category': 'player_performance', 'subcategory': 'hot_shooter', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'player_three_pt_made', 'filters': {'min_made': 5}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': 'hot_shooter', 'text': "Has {player_name}'s three-point shooting been consistent all season or was this more of a breakout night?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "The capability has always been there. The consistency is what we've been developing. Tonight was a sign that the developmental work is turning capability into reliability. That's the goal.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': 'The work is there. What fluctuates is the execution in games. Tonight the execution matched the preparation. I want to see {player_name} replicate that process, not just the result.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "{player_name} has had good stretches. Tonight was {player_name}'s best. We expect more nights like this as the season goes on.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': 'The system has generated quality looks for {player_name} all season. The conversion rate fluctuates. Tonight the conversion matched the look quality. When those two things align, you get this.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "There have been games where {player_name} didn't get many attempts because the ball found other people. Tonight {player_name} got {player_name}'s looks and made them. That's what happens when everyone is involved.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_up']}]},
    {'id': 'hot_shooter_04', 'category': 'player_performance', 'subcategory': 'hot_shooter', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'player_three_pt_made', 'filters': {'min_made': 5}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': 'hot_shooter', 'text': 'Five threes in a game is a problem for opponents. How do you expect them to adjust defensively next time?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "They'll extend and try to take {player_name} off the catch. That creates driving lanes and kick-out opportunities for others. We'll have answers built in when they make that adjustment.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "They'll chase. When {player_name} makes five threes, opponents are going to send a lot more attention {player_name}'s way. {player_name} needs to be ready to use that attention — attack the close-out, find teammates.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'player_em_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "More ball pressure and tighter off-ball coverage. We'll adjust to find {player_name} in different ways when that happens.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "The next step in {player_name}'s development is using that defensive attention to create advantages for the offense. A shooter who can score off the dribble when defenders are running at them becomes nearly unguardable.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': '{player_name} will key on {player_name} and that opens things up for everyone else. We embrace that. When defenses collapse on one player, the team benefits. {player_name} understands that and will make the right play.', 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_up']}]},
    {'id': 'surprise_scorer_01', 'category': 'player_performance', 'subcategory': 'surprise_scorer', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'player_pts_vs_rating', 'filters': {'player_rt_max': 50, 'min_pts': 15}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': 'surprise_scorer', 'text': '{player_name} had a big offensive night — maybe not what people outside this program expected. Were you surprised?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Not at all. I see {player_name} every day. The development has been real. What you saw tonight isn't a surprise to anyone who's been in that gym — it's validation that the work is translating.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'prestige_minor_up', 'fan_interest_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "{player_name} was ready for this opportunity. {player_name}'s been doing the right things in practice, in the locker room, in preparation. When a player does everything right, eventually the game rewards that player. Tonight it did.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_up', 'fan_interest_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': 'Not surprised. {player_name} has been working hard and playing well in practice. We believed in what {player_name} could do. Tonight {player_name} showed everyone else.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'fan_interest_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "{player_name} met the standard tonight. That's all that produced this. When you hold the standard, the opportunities come and you convert them. Nothing surprising about it.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'player_em_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "The system created the opportunity and {player_name} was prepared to take it. We design roles based on what each player does best. Tonight {player_name}'s role aligned perfectly with what the game needed.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'player_em_up', 'fan_interest_up']}]},
    {'id': 'surprise_scorer_02', 'category': 'player_performance', 'subcategory': 'surprise_scorer', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'player_pts_vs_rating', 'filters': {'player_rt_max': 50, 'min_pts': 15}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': 'surprise_scorer', 'text': 'How do you build confidence in a player like {player_name} to perform at this level in a real game?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Individual investment. Honest feedback, specific skill work, and meaningful reps in practice situations that mirror game pressure. Confidence in games comes from competence built in practice. That's where we've been with {player_name}.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "The locker room believes in {player_name}. When your teammates believe in you before you've done it in a game, that belief becomes its own foundation. {player_name} knew this team expected {player_name} to compete. That matters.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': 'You give {player_name} real opportunities in practice and a defined role in games. Players who know their role and get real reps build the confidence to perform when their number is called.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': 'You hold {player_name} to the same standard as everyone else. When a player knows {player_name} is held to the same expectation regardless of experience level, {player_name} rises to meet it. {player_name} did that tonight.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'player_em_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': 'You put {player_name} in system reads {player_name} has mastered in practice. The confidence comes from executing something familiar under game conditions. We sequence the introduction carefully — tonight {player_name} was ready for the bigger role.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'player_em_up']}]},
    {'id': 'surprise_scorer_03', 'category': 'player_performance', 'subcategory': 'surprise_scorer', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'player_pts_vs_rating', 'filters': {'player_rt_max': 50, 'min_pts': 15}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': 'surprise_scorer', 'text': "Does a night like this change {player_name}'s role going forward?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': 'Roles are earned in practice, not awarded based on one game. Tonight is a very positive data point. What happens in practice tomorrow will tell me more about what {player_name} deserves going forward.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "It opens doors. I'll increase {player_name}'s opportunities in specific situations based on what {player_name} showed tonight. Development is about building on momentum like this. We'll build on it.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "We'll look at the film and evaluate. One great night doesn't guarantee a larger role but it certainly creates opportunity.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "{player_name}'s role in specific situations expands. The system adjusts to deploy players who have proven they can execute. {player_name} showed {player_name} can execute in this context. The system will reflect that.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'player_em_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "The team will trust {player_name} more in those situations now. Role expansion happens organically in a healthy culture — when a player proves {player_name} belongs, teammates start looking for {player_name}. That's already starting.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_up']}]},
    {'id': 'surprise_scorer_04', 'category': 'player_performance', 'subcategory': 'surprise_scorer', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'player_pts_vs_rating', 'filters': {'player_rt_max': 50, 'min_pts': 15}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': 'surprise_scorer', 'text': 'What does this say about the depth of this program that a player like {player_name} can step up and produce like this?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "It says the culture is working. When every player at every level of the roster is invested and prepared, you get performances like {player_name}'s. Depth isn't just talent — it's culture going all the way down the roster.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'prestige_minor_up', 'fan_interest_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': 'It says the standard applies to everyone. {player_name} held the standard and was rewarded with an opportunity. That message resonates across the entire roster.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "It says we have more players capable of contributing than opponents can prepare for. That's a significant advantage over a long season.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_up', 'fan_interest_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "It says the development pipeline is working. {player_name} didn't arrive ready for this — {player_name} was developed into it. That's repeatable. This program can do this with every player who commits to the process.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'prestige_minor_up', 'fan_interest_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "It says the system works for everyone on the roster, not just the stars. When a player like {player_name} can produce at this level within the scheme, opponents can't key on one or two players. That's a structural competitive advantage.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}]},
    {'id': 'surprise_rebounder_01', 'category': 'player_performance', 'subcategory': 'surprise_rebounder', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'player_reb_vs_rating', 'filters': {'player_rt_max': 50, 'min_reb': 12}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': 'surprise_rebounder', 'text': '{player_name} was a monster on the glass tonight — probably not what the other team prepared for. What made that happen?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': 'Will and technique in equal measure. {player_name} has been working specifically on rebounding positioning. Tonight the technique was sharp and the effort was elite. That combination produces exactly what you saw.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': '{player_name} competed harder than the person {player_name} was matched against. Rebounding is decided by effort and positioning, and {player_name} won both battles on every play.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'player_em_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': '{player_name} put in work and took advantage of the opportunity. When players are prepared and the matchup opens up, this is what can happen.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'fan_interest_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "The team's boxing out created the opportunities and {player_name} finished them. These things don't happen without collective effort — {player_name} was the beneficiary and the finisher of a team rebounding effort.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "We identified a rebounding matchup advantage in film and designed our box-out assignments around it. {player_name} executed the assignment at a high level. The result wasn't accidental.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'player_em_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}]},
    {'id': 'surprise_rebounder_02', 'category': 'player_performance', 'subcategory': 'surprise_rebounder', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'player_reb_vs_rating', 'filters': {'player_rt_max': 50, 'min_reb': 12}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': 'surprise_rebounder', 'text': "Is this a new dimension of {player_name}'s game or have you been seeing this in practice?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Practice. This isn't new — it's been building for weeks. What's new is the game stage and the result. {player_name} has been developing this in their skill work and tonight it translated to the scorebook.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "We see effort in practice every day. Tonight the effort showed up in the numbers. That's all this is.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "{player_name} has been working hard on the glass in practice. Tonight the work showed up. We believe it's a consistent part of {player_name}'s game now.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "We added specific rebounding assignments to {player_name}'s role in recent weeks based on matchup analysis. This is a designed expansion of {player_name}'s contribution, not an accident.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'player_em_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "The teammates have seen this in practice. They weren't surprised. {player_name} was happy for {player_name} because they know how hard {player_name} has worked for exactly this kind of night.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_up']}]},
    {'id': 'surprise_rebounder_03', 'category': 'player_performance', 'subcategory': 'surprise_rebounder', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'player_reb_vs_rating', 'filters': {'player_rt_max': 50, 'min_reb': 12}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': 'surprise_rebounder', 'text': 'How much does a performance like this change what opponents have to account for when they game-plan against you?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': 'It creates a new variable. When scouting reports underestimate a player and that player produces at this level, coaching staffs have to recalibrate. That complexity is a competitive advantage for us.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "They have to respect everyone on this roster now. When you don't know which player is going to hurt you, you can't key on one or two. {player_name} just added {player_name} to that threat list.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': 'It adds another player they have to account for. The more threats on your roster, the harder you are to defend. {player_name} just became a legitimate factor.', 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_up', 'fan_interest_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': 'It tells every opponent that everyone on this roster can hurt you on a given night. That kind of uncertainty is a product of the whole program working and everyone being invested.', 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "{player_name} is now a player scouts will flag. That's significant for {player_name}'s development — {player_name} has earned attention, and how {player_name} handles that attention will be the next chapter of {player_name}'s growth.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'prestige_minor_up', 'fan_interest_up']}]},
    {'id': 'surprise_rebounder_04', 'category': 'player_performance', 'subcategory': 'surprise_rebounder', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'player_reb_vs_rating', 'filters': {'player_rt_max': 50, 'min_reb': 12}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': 'surprise_rebounder', 'text': 'What would it mean for this program if {player_name} could replicate this kind of production consistently?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "It would mean the developmental model is working at a level that changes the program's ceiling. When lower-rated players develop into impact contributors, you build something that can't be disrupted by one or two players leaving.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'prestige_minor_up', 'fan_interest_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "It means the culture produces players the ratings didn't fully see. That's one of the most powerful things a program can build — the ability to develop players others overlook. {player_name} is showing what that looks like.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'prestige_minor_up', 'fan_interest_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': 'It would significantly deepen our roster. Players who provide value above what the ratings suggest are extremely valuable over a long season.', 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "It means we have a reliable piece in a critical role. That's what programs are built on — players who show up, do their job, and produce. {player_name} is showing {player_name} can be that.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "It means opponents can't simply ignore {player_name} in their scouting. When every player on your roster demands defensive attention, the system generates better looks everywhere. {player_name} becoming a consistent rebounder changes the math for the whole offense.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}]},
    {'id': 'game_winner_01', 'category': 'player_performance', 'subcategory': 'game_winner', 'tier': 2, 'requires_tracking': True, 'trigger': {'condition': 'game_winner_shot', 'filters': {}}, 'weight': 3, 'player_slot': 'game_winner', 'text': '{player_name} hit the shot that won the game. What goes through your mind in that moment?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': 'Pure pride. Not just because we won — because {player_name} had the courage to take that shot and the character to make it. That moment is the product of everything this team has built together.', 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_up', 'prestige_minor_up', 'fan_interest_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "Relief and respect. {player_name} took the shot I expected {player_name} to take and made it. That's what preparation and standard-setting produce in a moment like that.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "Everything — elation, relief, pride. Those are the moments you work all season for. I'm incredibly proud of {player_name} for delivering.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'prestige_minor_up', 'fan_interest_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "Validation. We designed the final possession around creating the best possible shot. {player_name} got to {player_name}'s spot, read the defense, and executed. That's the system and the player working together perfectly.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up', 'player_em_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Confirmation. I've seen {player_name} hit that shot a thousand times in practice. When it went in tonight, what I felt was — of course. {player_name} was ready. {player_name} has always been ready for exactly that moment.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'prestige_minor_up', 'fan_interest_up']}]},
    {'id': 'game_winner_02', 'category': 'player_performance', 'subcategory': 'game_winner', 'tier': 2, 'requires_tracking': True, 'trigger': {'condition': 'game_winner_shot', 'filters': {}}, 'weight': 3, 'player_slot': 'game_winner', 'text': 'You drew up the final play. Was {player_name} always the intended option, or did the defense dictate it?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': '{player_name} was the primary option. We identified the matchup advantage and designed the action to create that look specifically. The defense responded the way we anticipated and {player_name} made the shot.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "I'll keep the specifics of the play design between us and the locker room. What I'll say is that {player_name} was ready for the moment. The rest is game strategy.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': 'We had options. {player_name} was the primary read and the defense gave us exactly what we wanted. Credit to {player_name} for making the shot when it was there.', 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': '{player_name} earned that shot. We trust {player_name} in that moment because {player_name} has earned that trust every day in practice. The design and the trust — they work together.', 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "{player_name} was the primary option because that's {player_name}'s moment — the spot {player_name} has been developing for, the range, the footwork. We put the ball in the right hands. {player_name} did the rest.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}]},
    {'id': 'game_winner_03', 'category': 'player_performance', 'subcategory': 'game_winner', 'tier': 2, 'requires_tracking': True, 'trigger': {'condition': 'game_winner_shot', 'filters': {}}, 'weight': 3, 'player_slot': 'game_winner', 'text': "What does a moment like this do for {player_name}'s trajectory and {player_name}'s confidence going forward?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Moments like this permanently change a player's belief in themselves. {player_name} now has proof that {player_name} can deliver in the biggest moment. That changes how {player_name} approaches every game going forward.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'prestige_minor_up', 'fan_interest_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "It changes the whole team's belief in {player_name}. Everyone on this roster just saw {player_name} deliver when it mattered most. That trust doesn't fade. It builds.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': 'It gives {player_name} a reference point. Every player needs a moment they can go back to when things are hard. {player_name} has that now.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'prestige_minor_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "It confirms what I've always believed — that {player_name} has what it takes. Now {player_name} knows it too. That changes everything.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'player_em_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "It validates the preparation. {player_name} executed under maximum pressure. That's a skill and it's repeatable. {player_name} will approach every late-game situation differently because of tonight.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'player_em_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}]},
    {'id': 'game_winner_04', 'category': 'player_performance', 'subcategory': 'game_winner', 'tier': 2, 'requires_tracking': True, 'trigger': {'condition': 'game_winner_shot', 'filters': {}}, 'weight': 3, 'player_slot': 'game_winner', 'text': 'Players who hit shots like that — what separates them mentally from players who want to avoid the ball in that moment?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Preparation. Players who avoid pressure haven't done enough work to trust themselves in those moments. Players who want the ball have. {player_name} has put in the work. That's why {player_name} was ready.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "Character. Some players want to succeed. Others are afraid of failing. {player_name} is in the first group. You can't teach that but you can develop the preparation that makes it more likely to show up.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'player_em_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': 'Confidence built over time. It comes from preparation, from experience, from having been in difficult moments before and coming through them. {player_name} has been building toward this.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "They play for something bigger than themselves. When you're playing for your teammates in that moment, the fear of failure is replaced by the responsibility to compete. {player_name} plays for this team. That was clear tonight.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "Process. Players who avoid pressure are thinking about the outcome. Players who want the ball are thinking about their next action — their footwork, their release, the read. {player_name} was in process mode. That's coachable and we coach it.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'player_em_up']}]},
    {'id': 'confident_player_01', 'category': 'player_performance', 'subcategory': 'confident_player', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'player_em', 'filters': {'min_em': 80}}, 'weight': 1, 'player_slot': 'confident_player', 'text': "{player_name} seemed locked in from start to finish tonight. Is that the version of {player_name} you're seeing consistently right now?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Consistently in practice, increasingly in games. {player_name} has found a mental place that's producing great basketball. We're working to anchor that and make it {player_name}'s baseline, not a peak.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "When the team is right, {player_name} is right. There's a direct connection between the collective energy and {player_name}'s individual performance. Tonight both were there.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "{player_name} has been in a good place mentally and it's showing up on the court. We hope to see more of this going forward.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "{player_name} is holding the standard right now. That's what locked-in looks like. That's the expectation every night.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'player_em_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "The system is working well for {player_name} right now — {player_name} understands the reads, trusts the actions, and the results are building {player_name}'s confidence. That's the cycle we want for every player.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'player_em_up']}]},
    {'id': 'confident_player_02', 'category': 'player_performance', 'subcategory': 'confident_player', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'player_em', 'filters': {'min_em': 80}}, 'weight': 1, 'player_slot': 'confident_player', 'text': 'What does {player_name} do well that other players could learn from in terms of mental preparation?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': 'Process over outcome. {player_name} focuses on what {player_name} can control — preparation, reads, execution. The results are the product of that, not the focus. That mental framework is what every player should be developing.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': 'Consistency. {player_name} brings the same standard to practice Tuesday as to game day Saturday. The confidence in games is built from that consistency. Everyone on this roster can learn from that.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "{player_name} prepares well and trusts {player_name}'s preparation when the game comes. That's the most important mental habit in basketball and they've developed it.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "{player_name} plays without fear of teammates' judgment. When you're in a culture where mistakes are learning opportunities, you play freely. {player_name} has internalized that. Every player in this program benefits from the culture, but {player_name} uses it best right now.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "{player_name} knows the system so completely that {player_name}'s mental energy goes to reading the defense rather than remembering the action. System mastery creates mental freedom. That's a model for every player we develop.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'player_em_up']}]},
    {'id': 'confident_player_03', 'category': 'player_performance', 'subcategory': 'confident_player', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'player_em', 'filters': {'min_em': 80}}, 'weight': 1, 'player_slot': 'confident_player', 'text': 'How do you maintain this level of confidence for {player_name} over the rest of the season?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Honest feedback. Not just praise — specific feedback that helps {player_name} understand what's working and why. Confidence built on honest assessment is more durable than confidence built on compliments.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': 'Consistent role and clear expectations. Players stay confident when they know what success looks like for them. We keep that clarity steady for {player_name} regardless of what else changes around {player_name}.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'player_em_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "Protect the routine. What's working for {player_name} right now — preparation, role, usage — we protect that as much as possible. Confidence lives in consistency.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "The standard doesn't change regardless of how well {player_name} is playing. That consistency is actually what keeps the confidence real. When the bar moves up and down based on results, players get unstable. We keep the standard fixed.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "The locker room. {player_name} draws energy from this group. We make sure the environment stays one where {player_name} knows {player_name} is trusted and valued. That's the soil the confidence grows in.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_up']}]},
    {'id': 'confident_player_04', 'category': 'player_performance', 'subcategory': 'confident_player', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'player_em', 'filters': {'min_em': 80}}, 'weight': 1, 'player_slot': 'confident_player', 'text': 'When {player_name} is playing like this, does it change how you use {player_name} — more minutes, different situations?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "Trust is earned. When {player_name} holds the standard at this level, {player_name} earns {player_name}'s deployment. I don't chase hot streaks but I do reward sustained performance.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'player_em_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': 'I look for specific high-leverage situations to deploy {player_name} in. Confident players in the right matchups can have outsized impact. I want to maximize that window.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "Somewhat. You trust the player more and put {player_name} in situations to succeed. It's a natural response to performance.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "The system adjusts to deploy players where they're most effective. When {player_name} is performing at this level, specific actions become primary reads for {player_name}. The scheme reflects {player_name}'s current form.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'player_em_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "The team finds {player_name} more when {player_name} is playing like this — it happens organically. I don't have to engineer it. Players know who's locked in and want to get that player the ball.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_up']}]},
    {'id': 'dominant_star_01', 'category': 'player_performance', 'subcategory': 'dominant_star', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'player_pts_rating', 'filters': {'min_pts': 30, 'min_rt': 80}}, 'weight': 3, 'player_slot': 'dominant_star', 'text': '{player_name} was completely unstoppable tonight. Is this what you expected when you built this team around {player_name}?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "This is exactly what we built toward — creating a system and a culture that maximizes {player_name}'s impact. When a player of that quality is operating at {player_name}'s ceiling with the right support around {player_name}, this is the result.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'prestige_major_up', 'fan_interest_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': 'Yes. When {player_name} holds the standard and the game plan is executed, this is what happens. {player_name} is capable of this every night. The expectation is that {player_name} delivers it.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_major_up', 'fan_interest_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "This is {player_name} playing at {player_name}'s best. We want to see this consistently. Tonight {player_name} showed what's possible when everything clicks.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_major_up', 'fan_interest_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': 'This is why we design the system the way we do — to create the maximum number of high-quality opportunities for our best players. {player_name} converting at this rate when those opportunities are there is exactly what we planned for.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_major_up', 'fan_interest_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': 'This is {player_name} playing free. When {player_name} trusts teammates to do their jobs, when {player_name} is not carrying the whole offense alone — this is what you get. The team enabled this and {player_name} delivered it.', 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_up', 'prestige_major_up']}]},
    {'id': 'dominant_star_02', 'category': 'player_performance', 'subcategory': 'dominant_star', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'player_pts_rating', 'filters': {'min_pts': 30, 'min_rt': 80}}, 'weight': 3, 'player_slot': 'dominant_star', 'text': "Thirty-plus points from {player_name} — at what point are opposing coaches thinking about changing what they're doing defensively?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': 'Early. And every adjustment they make opens something else in the system. We prepare {player_name} for the double-teams, the traps, and the defensive changes. The goal is to make the adjustments hurt them more than they help.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_major_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "Let them adjust. {player_name} can handle whatever opponents throw at {player_name}. And when they commit extra resources to {player_name}, the rest of the team takes advantage. We're comfortable playing against any defensive scheme.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_major_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "By the second quarter, they're thinking about it. Every team that faces {player_name} in that kind of form has to make a decision. We prepare for all of them.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_major_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "They can send as much at {player_name} as they want — this team has the players and the trust to make them pay for it. {player_name} playing well makes everyone's job easier and more dangerous simultaneously.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'prestige_major_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': '{player_name} is thinking about it immediately. And the pressure of being that threat is something {player_name} has worked to handle. {player_name} is better now at reading the extra attention and using it — not just scoring through it.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'prestige_major_up']}]},
    {'id': 'dominant_star_03', 'category': 'player_performance', 'subcategory': 'dominant_star', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'player_pts_rating', 'filters': {'min_pts': 30, 'min_rt': 80}}, 'weight': 3, 'player_slot': 'dominant_star', 'text': 'How do you keep {player_name} motivated and hungry when {player_name} has nights like this — when it all looks easy?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': 'You raise the bar immediately. You show {player_name} what {player_name} could have done better even in a great game. Not to diminish the performance — but to remind {player_name} that greatness is a journey, not a destination.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "The standard doesn't change based on the result. {player_name} knows that. A thirty-point night still goes on the film and the film still has mistakes. That keeps the focus sharp.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': 'You let {player_name} enjoy it and come back with the same approach the next day. The best players are self-motivated. {player_name} is one of those players.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "You point {player_name} toward the next challenge together. {player_name} isn't playing to have thirty-point games — {player_name} is playing to help this team win something. That purpose is more sustaining than any individual result.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "You identify the plays {player_name} didn't execute within the system. Even in a dominant performance, there are moments where a player went away from the scheme. You show those. Excellence within structure is the standard — not just excellence.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'player_em_up']}]},
    {'id': 'dominant_star_04', 'category': 'player_performance', 'subcategory': 'dominant_star', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'player_pts_rating', 'filters': {'min_pts': 30, 'min_rt': 80}}, 'weight': 3, 'player_slot': 'dominant_star', 'text': 'When {player_name} is in a game like that, does any part of you want to just let {player_name} keep going regardless of the rotation plan?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': 'No. The plan is the plan. And {player_name} knows that. Burning {player_name} for thirty-five minutes tonight hurts us two games from now. The long view wins.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "You adjust the rotation timing, not the rotation logic. If {player_name} is rolling and we have strategic reasons to keep {player_name} in, we do. But you don't abandon game management — you refine it in real time.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'player_em_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "Of course there's a temptation. But player health and long-term program interests outweigh the individual performance. We manage that balance every game.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "Sometimes. But {player_name} would be the first to tell you that the team's health over the season matters more than any single performance. {player_name} understands the long game as well as anyone in that locker room.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "In high-stakes games, yes — I extend the minutes. But I also know that protecting {player_name}'s body and {player_name}'s mental freshness is how you keep this level of performance accessible all season. One game isn't worth the season.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}]},
    {'id': 'struggling_star_01', 'category': 'player_performance', 'subcategory': 'struggling_star', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'player_pts_rating', 'filters': {'max_pts': 6, 'min_pts': 1, 'min_rt': 80}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': 'struggling_star', 'text': "{player_name} had a tough offensive night. What were you seeing from {player_name} that wasn't working?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "{player_name} was pressing. When {player_name} doesn't get early looks, there's a tendency to reach for shots rather than stay patient within the system. We'll look at the possessions where {player_name} deviated and address those specifically.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_down', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "The defense took away {player_name}'s primary actions and we were slow to find counters. Part of that is on the scheme and part is on {player_name} finding secondary reads. Both need to improve.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'player_em_down']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "{player_name} faced tough coverage and didn't find a rhythm. {player_name} has nights like this — the key is how {player_name} responds and how the team responds around {player_name}.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_down', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "{player_name} didn't compete at {player_name}'s level. Whether that's focus, effort, or execution — {player_name} knows the standard and knows {player_name} didn't meet it tonight.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'player_em_down']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "Some nights the ball doesn't go your way. What I was watching was how {player_name} competed on the other end and how {player_name} supported teammates. That tells you more about character than the box score does.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_down']}]},
    {'id': 'struggling_star_02', 'category': 'player_performance', 'subcategory': 'struggling_star', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'player_pts_rating', 'filters': {'max_pts': 6, 'min_pts': 1, 'min_rt': 80}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': 'struggling_star', 'text': "When your best player struggles, how does that affect the team's approach and your offensive game plan mid-game?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': 'You run more actions for other players to take pressure off {player_name} while keeping {player_name} involved without forcing. You look for easy opportunities — second-chance touches, open cuts — to get {player_name} a look {player_name} can make.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'team_chemistry_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "You keep running the offense. {player_name} is going to have difficult nights. The standard is that the team doesn't change what it does — it competes regardless of who's hot and who isn't.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "You find ways to involve other players more while looking for easy opportunities to get {player_name} back into the game. You don't abandon your best player but you don't force it either.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': 'The team picks {player_name} up. Other players accept larger roles, make plays, and communicate — they give {player_name} room to breathe. Tonight we could have done that better as a collective.', 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "You find the action that gets {player_name} to the line or to an easy mid-range look — something within {player_name}'s skill set that doesn't require {player_name}'s best rhythm. You get {player_name} on the board and rebuild from there.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}]},
    {'id': 'struggling_star_03', 'category': 'player_performance', 'subcategory': 'struggling_star', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'player_pts_rating', 'filters': {'max_pts': 6, 'min_pts': 1, 'min_rt': 80}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': 'struggling_star', 'text': 'Is this more of a one-game anomaly for {player_name}, or does it reflect something you need to address going forward?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "I won't know until I look at the film. If the shots were good shots that didn't fall, it's variance. If the decision-making was off, it's something we address. {player_name} deserves an honest evaluation either way.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "We'll look at the film and let that tell us. {player_name} has a track record. One bad night doesn't change that track record — but it also doesn't get a free pass. We address it the same way we address everything.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "One game in isolation is hard to read. We'll look at the context — the coverage, the shot selection, the decision-making — and get a clearer picture before drawing conclusions.", 'effect_tags': ['red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': 'The film will tell us whether the scheme created the right opportunities and {player_name} missed them, or whether the scheme failed to create enough. Both have different solutions.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'player_em_down']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "I'm going to have a private conversation with {player_name} before I draw any public conclusions. What's happening with a player goes beyond the box score. I want to understand the full picture first.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_up']}]},
    {'id': 'struggling_star_04', 'category': 'player_performance', 'subcategory': 'struggling_star', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'player_pts_rating', 'filters': {'max_pts': 6, 'min_pts': 1, 'min_rt': 80}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': 'struggling_star', 'text': 'Despite the scoring struggles, are there other ways {player_name} contributed tonight?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "Absolutely. I watched {player_name} compete on defense, communicate, and support teammates even when the offensive game wasn't there. That's character. The scoring will come back — this team needs that fight more than the points.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "{player_name} competed on the defensive end. That's the minimum standard in this program regardless of what's happening offensively. {player_name} held that. It doesn't offset the offensive performance but it's noted.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "Yes. Defense, communication, effort — there were positive contributions. But we need {player_name} on both ends and we'll work to get back to that.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "I look at the non-scoring impact specifically — screens, spacing, defensive effort, assists. {player_name} contributed in some of those areas. That's what I'll acknowledge while we work on the scoring game together.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "{player_name} maintained defensive assignments and spacing responsibilities even when the offensive results weren't there. That system discipline in a difficult night is actually something to acknowledge.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'player_em_up']}]},
    {'id': 'zero_star_01', 'category': 'player_performance', 'subcategory': 'zero_star', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'player_pts_rating', 'filters': {'pts': 0, 'min_rt': 80}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': 'zero_star', 'text': '{player_name} was held scoreless tonight. How do you account for that?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "I can't account for it in a way that's acceptable. {player_name} is one of our best players. Zero points is a failure of execution and possibly a failure of will. We'll get to the bottom of it.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'player_em_down', 'prestige_minor_down']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "The opponent took away every action we ran for {player_name}. Their defense was exceptional in that matchup and we couldn't generate a clean look all game. That's a schematic challenge we'll address before the next time we see a similar scheme.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'player_em_down', 'prestige_minor_down']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "It happens. The defense keyed on {player_name} and we didn't find enough counters. We'll look at the film and find better answers.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_down', 'prestige_minor_down', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "I'll talk to {player_name} privately before I offer any public assessment. A scoreless night for a player of {player_name}'s caliber says something — I want to understand what before I say anything else.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_down']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "I look at the shot attempts first. If {player_name} was getting looks and missing, that's one conversation. If {player_name} wasn't getting looks, that's a different conversation about shot creation and assertiveness. The film will tell me which one we're having.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_down', 'discipline_up']}]},
    {'id': 'zero_star_02', 'category': 'player_performance', 'subcategory': 'zero_star', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'player_pts_rating', 'filters': {'pts': 0, 'min_rt': 80}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': 'zero_star', 'text': "Does {player_name} need to show more assertiveness in creating {player_name}'s own shot, or is this a systemic issue?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Both need to be examined. {player_name} needs to assert {player_name}'s individual shot creation within the flow of the offense. And the scheme needs to create more options when the primary actions are being taken away. We'll address both.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "Assertiveness. {player_name} is good enough to create {player_name}'s own shot. Tonight {player_name} didn't. That's not a scheme problem — that's a will and decision-making problem. It will change.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'player_em_down']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "Some of both. We need better system answers for when the defense keys on {player_name}, and {player_name} needs to find ways to get involved even when the primary actions aren't available.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'player_em_down', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "The system failed to generate enough looks. We'll adjust the scheme specifically to make {player_name} harder to completely eliminate. That's a preparation failure on our part that we will correct.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'player_em_down', 'prestige_minor_down']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "I want to understand {player_name}'s mental state first. Sometimes a scoreless night is about what's happening inside the player more than what the defense did. The conversation happens privately and honestly.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_up']}]},
    {'id': 'zero_star_03', 'category': 'player_performance', 'subcategory': 'zero_star', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'player_pts_rating', 'filters': {'pts': 0, 'min_rt': 80}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': 'zero_star', 'text': 'How do you get {player_name} right mentally and physically heading into the next game?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': 'Film, then individual time on the court. We identify exactly what the defense took away and we practice the counters specifically. {player_name} leaves the next day of practice knowing {player_name} has specific answers. Confidence is rebuilt through preparation.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "{player_name} knows the standard. {player_name} knows {player_name} didn't meet it. You go back to work. The best response to a bad performance is the next performance. We prepare and we compete.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'player_em_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "You give {player_name} the film, you have an honest conversation, and you set clear goals for the next game. Then you let {player_name} do {player_name}'s preparation and trust that {player_name} will respond.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "You make sure {player_name} feels supported, not abandoned. One bad night shouldn't fracture a player's sense of belonging in this program. Then you prepare them specifically and give them the opportunity to respond. I believe they will.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "Specific scheme preparation. {player_name} gets a clear picture of what was taken away and exactly how we're going to attack it next time. Clarity is confidence for players who play within a system.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'player_em_up']}]},
    {'id': 'zero_star_04', 'category': 'player_performance', 'subcategory': 'zero_star', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'player_pts_rating', 'filters': {'pts': 0, 'min_rt': 80}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': 'zero_star', 'text': "How much of a factor was this in the game's outcome — did {player_name}'s scoreless night cost you?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "Significantly. We need {player_name} to produce. When {player_name} doesn't, the entire offensive structure is under more pressure. That pressure showed tonight.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_down', 'player_em_down']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "It created an imbalance the scheme couldn't fully correct. When your primary option produces nothing, the system can compensate to a point — tonight it wasn't enough.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "It was a factor. You can't have your best offensive player score nothing and not feel that impact. We found some answers but not enough.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_down', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "The team competed without the scoring contribution we usually get from {player_name}. That's a credit to everyone else. But yes — we're harder to beat when {player_name} is producing.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "It changed the offensive burden distribution. Other players were asked to do more and some rose to it and some didn't. That information is valuable. But ultimately — yes, we need {player_name} on the board.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_down', 'discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}]},
    {'id': 'foul_out_01', 'category': 'player_performance', 'subcategory': 'foul_out', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'player_fouls', 'filters': {'min_fouls': 5}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': 'foul_out', 'text': '{player_name} fouled out tonight. What was happening with the foul trouble?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "Poor decision-making. Whether it's technique or judgment, fouling out is preventable in most cases. {player_name} knows the standard — you compete physically without handing the opponent free points. We'll address it.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'player_em_down']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "{player_name}'s body positioning was poor on several possessions. When you're late to defensive coverage, you either give up a basket or you foul. {player_name} was too often in a position where fouling was the lesser of two evils. That's correctable.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'player_em_down']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "A combination of being in tough defensive matchups and some poor fouling decisions. We'll look at the film and figure out what was avoidable.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_down', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "{player_name} was competing hard — sometimes too hard without the discipline to match. The intensity is there. The technique needs to catch up. We'll work on that balance.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_down', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "There were two or three specific situations where {player_name} made reactive fouls rather than positioning fouls. That's a footwork and preparation issue. We'll run them through those exact situations in practice.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}]},
    {'id': 'foul_out_02', 'category': 'player_performance', 'subcategory': 'foul_out', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'player_fouls', 'filters': {'min_fouls': 5}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': 'foul_out', 'text': 'How did losing {player_name} to fouls affect how you managed the rest of the game?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': 'It forced specific scheme adjustments — different defensive assignments, modified rotations. We have contingency plans for these situations. Tonight we needed them earlier than expected.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "You manage it. The next player steps up. Foul trouble is part of basketball and this program prepares for it. Nobody in that locker room gets to feel like we can't compete without one player.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "You adjust the rotation and look for the next man to fill the role. It's not ideal but it's a situation every team faces.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_down', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "Other players stepped up to fill the gap. That's what this team does. Nobody used it as an excuse. We competed with what we had.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "I had to ask other players to accept roles and responsibilities they weren't prepared for. That's valuable development data — we found out who could handle the expanded role and who needs more preparation for those situations.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}]},
    {'id': 'foul_out_03', 'category': 'player_performance', 'subcategory': 'foul_out', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'player_fouls', 'filters': {'min_fouls': 5}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': 'foul_out', 'text': 'Is fouling out something {player_name} has struggled with before, or was tonight unusual?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "It's been an issue at certain points this season. We've worked on it. Tonight it resurfaced and we'll have to go back to that specific work. Some habits take longer to break than others. This one has to be broken.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_down', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "It's happened before. And every time it happens, the standard is the same — it's unacceptable. If {player_name} fouled out, {player_name} failed at something controllable. We fix it.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "It's happened occasionally. Tonight the matchup created more opportunities for foul trouble. We'll look at the film and evaluate what was systemic versus situational.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_down', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "Foul trouble has shown up for {player_name} against physical opponents. That's a pattern we need to address — specifically when the defense is guarding them aggressively, how does {player_name} respond without fouling.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'player_em_down']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "More than I'd like. We've talked about it. I think the competitiveness in {player_name} sometimes tips into reactive aggression. We're working on channeling that intensity constructively.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}]},
    {'id': 'foul_out_04', 'category': 'player_performance', 'subcategory': 'foul_out', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'player_fouls', 'filters': {'min_fouls': 5}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': 'foul_out', 'text': "What's the message to {player_name} after tonight?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "That we needed {player_name} and {player_name} wasn't there because of choices {player_name} made. That's the message. Not personal — but direct. The team needs {player_name} on the floor and that has to take priority over individual defensive aggression.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "That the intensity is there and we don't want to lose it — we want to direct it. The energy that creates foul trouble is the same energy that makes {player_name} special. We're going to develop the technique to keep both.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "Learn from it and come back better. The foul trouble hurt us tonight. That's the honest assessment. We fix it and move forward.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': 'That the team needs {player_name} available. When you foul out, your teammates lose a player they count on. That collective responsibility — staying on the floor for each other — is part of what we build here.', 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "We'll go through specific film sequences and build a personal rule set for {player_name} — situations where retreat is smarter than contest. Making it a concrete decision tree rather than an abstract standard.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'player_em_up']}]},
    {'id': 'frustrated_player_01', 'category': 'player_performance', 'subcategory': 'frustrated_player', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'player_em', 'filters': {'max_em': 20}}, 'weight': 1, 'player_slot': 'frustrated_player', 'text': '{player_name} seemed to be in a tough spot mentally tonight. What were you seeing?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "{player_name} was fighting {player_name}'s own performance instead of competing through it. When a player loses confidence, {player_name} starts trying to force results. That creates a cycle we need to break. I'll sit with {player_name} and get to the root of what's going on.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "Something wasn't right for {player_name} tonight — I saw it early. My job is to figure out what that is and address it. These things often have nothing to do with basketball. The support system around {player_name} starts with this program.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "{player_name} struggled to find a rhythm and it affected {player_name}'s confidence. These nights happen. How {player_name} responds tomorrow will tell us more than what we saw tonight.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_down', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "{player_name} needs to learn to compete through adversity. Basketball is hard and every player faces stretches where nothing goes right. The standard is that you compete at the same level regardless. {player_name} didn't meet that tonight.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'player_em_down']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "The reads weren't there for {player_name}. When a player loses decisiveness within the scheme, body language changes. We'll rebuild the decisiveness through specific reps and get {player_name} back to playing freely.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'player_em_up']}]},
    {'id': 'frustrated_player_02', 'category': 'player_performance', 'subcategory': 'frustrated_player', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'player_em', 'filters': {'max_em': 20}}, 'weight': 1, 'player_slot': 'frustrated_player', 'text': "How do you support a player like {player_name} when {player_name} is in a difficult stretch without it coming across as managing {player_name}'s emotions?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Direct, honest, private conversation. Not motivational speeches — specific observations about what I'm seeing and specific things we can work on. Players who feel respected enough to receive honest feedback respond better than those who are managed.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "You let the team carry {player_name}. The best thing a program can do for a struggling player is surround {player_name} with teammates who believe in {player_name} and compete for {player_name}. That's not managing emotions — it's culture doing its job.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "You give {player_name} space and opportunity. Over-coaching a player who's struggling can make it worse. Clear expectations, meaningful reps, and space to work through it.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "The standard. You don't soften the standard because someone is struggling — you hold it consistently. That consistency is actually what struggling players need. It tells {player_name} the bar doesn't move based on how {player_name} feels.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "You simplify {player_name}'s role. When a player is struggling, you reduce the decision complexity and let {player_name} succeed at something specific before building back up. Confidence comes from competence and competence starts with small wins.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'player_em_up']}]},
    {'id': 'frustrated_player_03', 'category': 'player_performance', 'subcategory': 'frustrated_player', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'player_em', 'filters': {'max_em': 20}}, 'weight': 1, 'player_slot': 'frustrated_player', 'text': "Does {player_name}'s mood on a night like this affect the team's overall energy?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "Honest answer — yes. When a player's body language is down, it can pull at the edges of the collective energy. A strong culture absorbs it but doesn't ignore it. We'll take care of {player_name} and take care of the group.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_down', 'player_em_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "It shouldn't and in a mature program it doesn't. Every player's job is to compete at the same level regardless of how they feel personally. That standard applies to {player_name} as much as to everyone else.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "It can. That's why we address it quickly and privately. You don't let individual frustration become a team problem if you can prevent it.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_down', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "It can bleed into the team's performance if we're not careful. My job is to identify it early and address it at the individual level so it doesn't become a group issue. Tonight I saw it coming and we managed it.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "The system is designed so that individual emotional states don't derail the group. But players are human and connection matters. We'll support {player_name} and protect the team's energy simultaneously.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'team_chemistry_up']}]},
    {'id': 'frustrated_player_04', 'category': 'player_performance', 'subcategory': 'frustrated_player', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'player_em', 'filters': {'max_em': 20}}, 'weight': 1, 'player_slot': 'frustrated_player', 'text': 'What do you expect from {player_name} in the next game?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "The standard. Same as always. How {player_name} felt tonight is irrelevant to what's expected next game. {player_name} knows what the bar is and I expect {player_name} to clear it.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'player_em_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "A response. Not a perfect game — a response. I want to see {player_name} compete with focus and confidence. The result will take care of itself. The mental reset is what I'm watching for.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "I expect {player_name} to come in ready to compete and to leave tonight behind. One hard game doesn't define {player_name} and we won't let it.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "I expect this team to rally around {player_name} and I expect {player_name} to come back ready to play for this team. That reciprocity is what makes a group special. We'll see it next game.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "A focused, decisive performance within the scheme. When {player_name} trusts the system and stops trying to force individual results, {player_name} plays {player_name}'s best basketball. That's what I'm preparing them for.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'player_em_up']}]},
    {'id': 'foul_trouble_01', 'category': 'player_performance', 'subcategory': 'foul_trouble', 'tier': 2, 'requires_tracking': True, 'trigger': {'condition': 'early_foul_trouble', 'filters': {'fouls_by_halftime_min': 3}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': 'foul_trouble', 'text': '{player_name} picked up foul trouble early tonight and it limited their impact. How do you manage that situation?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': 'You sit {player_name} early, protect {player_name} from the second foul until halftime, and manage {player_name} back into the game in the second half. The goal is to have {player_name} available for the fourth quarter. The scheme has to adjust in the meantime.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "You make a decision early and you hold it. I'm not going to let {player_name} foul out trying to win the first half. {player_name} sits, the next player steps up, and we compete with what we have.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "You protect them in foul trouble and get them back when the matchup and the game situation call for it. It's an art form — managing foul trouble is part of coaching.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "You lean on the team. When {player_name} can't be fully deployed, other players have to step into larger roles. Tonight that challenge was met — which is a credit to the depth and the culture of this program.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': 'I keep {player_name} in specific situations where the foul risk is lowest — not guarding ball-handlers in transition, no contested closeouts. You limit the risk while maintaining their offensive impact as long as possible.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}]},
    {'id': 'foul_trouble_02', 'category': 'player_performance', 'subcategory': 'foul_trouble', 'tier': 2, 'requires_tracking': True, 'trigger': {'condition': 'early_foul_trouble', 'filters': {'fouls_by_halftime_min': 3}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': 'foul_trouble', 'text': 'Were the fouls {player_name} picked up tonight preventable or were they just in tough situations?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Most were preventable. Foul trouble is usually a technique issue — wrong body positioning, reaching instead of moving feet. We'll look at each foul specifically and build the footwork corrections into individual practice.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': 'Preventable. The first foul is sometimes a tough situation. The second, third — those are choices. {player_name} needs to make better choices in those moments.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "A mix. Some were unavoidable competitive fouls. Others were preventable with better positioning. We'll sort through the film and identify which is which.", 'effect_tags': ['red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "At least two were scheme-related — {player_name} was put in a position to foul by the defensive assignment. We'll adjust the scheme so {player_name} is not being asked to cover situations that invite foul trouble.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': 'Partially. There were moments where the competitive intensity that makes {player_name} great crossed into reactive fouling. The intensity stays — the technique around it has to improve.', 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}]},
    {'id': 'foul_trouble_03', 'category': 'player_performance', 'subcategory': 'foul_trouble', 'tier': 2, 'requires_tracking': True, 'trigger': {'condition': 'early_foul_trouble', 'filters': {'fouls_by_halftime_min': 3}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': 'foul_trouble', 'text': 'Does your program have a protocol for when a key player gets into early foul trouble — specific rotations, role shifts?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "Yes. Every player in this program knows who their backup is and what changes when they come in. Foul trouble isn't a surprise — it's a scenario we prepare for. Tonight the protocol was executed.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "The next player plays. That's the protocol. Every player in this program is expected to be ready when their name is called. Tonight that standard held.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': 'You manage it in real time based on the game situation. There are general guidelines but every foul trouble situation is different. You adapt.', 'effect_tags': ['red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "The whole team knows the adjustments — it's not a coaching secret. When {player_name} is limited, specific teammates know their roles expand. That shared understanding is part of what makes us a team.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': 'We have specific players developed for exactly this role. Part of individual development is knowing how to expand in specific situations. Tonight those players got that call and responded well.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}]},
    {'id': 'foul_trouble_04', 'category': 'player_performance', 'subcategory': 'foul_trouble', 'tier': 2, 'requires_tracking': True, 'trigger': {'condition': 'early_foul_trouble', 'filters': {'fouls_by_halftime_min': 3}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': 'foul_trouble', 'text': 'What does {player_name} need to work on specifically to avoid this kind of foul trouble in the future?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Footwork on the catch — that's where most of the fouls originated. We'll drill specific defensive slides and closeout technique until the correct movement is automatic. When technique becomes habit, fouls drop.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "Discipline. The fouls tonight were about aggression exceeding judgment. {player_name} needs to compete just as hard with better restraint. That's a mental skill that we develop through repetition.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "Body positioning. Better positioning means you don't have to reach. When you reach, you foul. We'll work on the footwork and the approach angles.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "Reading the offensive player's intent earlier. By the time {player_name} reacted, it was already a foul situation. You need to read the drive one step earlier to position your body without fouling.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'player_em_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': 'Composure in defensive pressure situations. {player_name} competes at maximum intensity, which is exactly what we want. The next layer is channeling that intensity into better footwork and positioning rather than reactive contact.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'team_chemistry_up', 'discipline_up']}]},
    {'id': 'benched_star_01', 'category': 'player_performance', 'subcategory': 'benched_star', 'tier': 2, 'requires_tracking': True, 'trigger': {'condition': 'limited_minutes_high_rt', 'filters': {'max_minutes': 20, 'min_rt': 75}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': 'benched_star', 'text': '{player_name} had limited minutes tonight. Can you explain the decision?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': 'Playing time in this program is earned every day. {player_name} knows the expectations. Anything beyond that is handled internally.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "There are things going on with {player_name} that we're managing. The decision to limit {player_name}'s minutes was made with {player_name}'s development and the team's interests in mind. I'd rather not get into the specifics publicly.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "Game management and matchup decisions. It's something we evaluated in real time and made the call we thought was best for the team tonight.", 'effect_tags': ['red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "There are things happening behind the scenes that I'm not going to discuss publicly. What I will say is that {player_name} is part of this program and we'll work through it together.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "The matchup and game situation didn't create the ideal deployment conditions for {player_name} tonight. We'll adjust and you'll see a different picture going forward.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}]},
    {'id': 'benched_star_02', 'category': 'player_performance', 'subcategory': 'benched_star', 'tier': 2, 'requires_tracking': True, 'trigger': {'condition': 'limited_minutes_high_rt', 'filters': {'max_minutes': 20, 'min_rt': 75}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': 'benched_star', 'text': "Does limiting {player_name}'s minutes send a message to the rest of the roster?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': 'It sends the same message every decision in this program sends — the standard applies equally to everyone regardless of your rating or your history. Nobody is above the standard.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Every roster decision is a communication. What I hope this communicates is that we make decisions based on what's right for the player and the program, not on reputation or prior performance.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "It says that decisions are made for the team. Everyone understands that. It's part of how a program operates.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "What it communicates to this locker room is that we take care of our own. The decision about {player_name} was made with their best interests and the team's in mind. The team understands that.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': 'It communicates that the system works best when everyone executes their role correctly, and that deployment decisions are based on that execution — not on name recognition.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}]},
    {'id': 'benched_star_03', 'category': 'player_performance', 'subcategory': 'benched_star', 'tier': 2, 'requires_tracking': True, 'trigger': {'condition': 'limited_minutes_high_rt', 'filters': {'max_minutes': 20, 'min_rt': 75}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': 'benched_star', 'text': "How do you maintain {player_name}'s engagement and buy-in when {player_name}'s role is being reduced?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Honest, ongoing individual conversation. {player_name} knows exactly what the situation is, what I need from {player_name}, and what the path back to full deployment looks like. Clarity is respect. I'm not going to leave {player_name} guessing.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "{player_name} competes the same whether {player_name} plays forty minutes or four. That's the expectation. How {player_name} responds in practice and on the bench says everything about {player_name}'s character.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': 'You keep {player_name} involved in practice, communicate clearly, and give {player_name} a path back. Players respond to honesty and to feeling like they still have a future in the program.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "The team keeps {player_name} engaged. When the culture is right, a player in a reduced role still feels valued — because the team treats {player_name} that way. That's not something I have to manufacture. It's already there.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "I give {player_name} specific system work and specific goals in practice. {player_name} knows {player_name}'s value to the scheme and what {player_name} is working toward. Structure is its own form of engagement.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'player_em_up']}]},
    {'id': 'benched_star_04', 'category': 'player_performance', 'subcategory': 'benched_star', 'tier': 2, 'requires_tracking': True, 'trigger': {'condition': 'limited_minutes_high_rt', 'filters': {'max_minutes': 20, 'min_rt': 75}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': 'benched_star', 'text': 'How long do you expect this situation with {player_name} to last?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': 'As long as it takes. When {player_name} meets the standard consistently, their role reflects that. Not before.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "We're working through it and I expect improvement. I'm not going to put a timeline on it publicly — that's between me and {player_name}. But I'm optimistic about the direction.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "We'll take it day by day. The situation will resolve itself when the circumstances change — and they will change.", 'effect_tags': ['red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "I'm not going to put a public timeline on a situation that involves a person. What I'll say is that this program takes care of its players and we'll work through this together.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "We have specific benchmarks. When {player_name} meets those benchmarks consistently, the role expands. I've been transparent with them about what those benchmarks are.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'player_em_up']}]},
    {'id': 'bench_outperformer_01', 'category': 'player_performance', 'subcategory': 'bench_outperformer', 'tier': 2, 'requires_tracking': True, 'trigger': {'condition': 'bench_outscores_starter', 'filters': {}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': 'bench_outperformer', 'text': '{player_name} came off the bench and outproduced some of your starters tonight. Does that change anything going forward?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "It means {player_name} is putting pressure on the starters in front of them. That's how this program works. You earn your spot every day. Tonight {player_name} made a statement.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'player_em_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "It opens a conversation. {player_name} showed {player_name} is ready for more. I'll evaluate the matchups, the minutes, the development arc — and we'll make decisions based on what's best for the team and for {player_name}'s growth.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "It's a positive problem to have. {player_name} played well and put {player_name} in the conversation for more minutes. That's how rosters evolve.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "It means the whole roster is competitive and developing. When reserve players push starters, everyone gets better. That's exactly the kind of program we're trying to build.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "It means the system works at every level of the roster. {player_name} produced because {player_name} understood the scheme and executed it. That's the goal — a system that makes every player effective when they're on the floor.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'player_em_up']}]},
    {'id': 'bench_outperformer_02', 'category': 'player_performance', 'subcategory': 'bench_outperformer', 'tier': 2, 'requires_tracking': True, 'trigger': {'condition': 'bench_outscores_starter', 'filters': {}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': 'bench_outperformer', 'text': 'How do you handle the internal dynamic when {player_name} outperforms the players ahead of {player_name} in the rotation?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': 'You handle it by holding the standard equally. Starters who are outperformed by their backups face the same expectations everyone faces. The rotation reflects production and standard, not tenure.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "Honestly and directly with all parties. The starter knows we saw it, {player_name} knows we saw it, and the team knows it. In a culture of honesty, you don't pretend it didn't happen — you use it to push everyone forward.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "Professionally. Competition for minutes is healthy. You acknowledge performance, you maintain relationships, and you make decisions based on what's best for the team.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Individual conversations with both players. The starter gets honest feedback about what needs to improve. {player_name} gets clear guidance on what they did well and what they need to maintain. You don't avoid it — you use it.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "The system handles a lot of it. When everyone understands that deployment is based on execution and matchup fit, a reserve outperforming a starter isn't a crisis — it's the system functioning correctly.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'player_em_up']}]},
    {'id': 'bench_outperformer_03', 'category': 'player_performance', 'subcategory': 'bench_outperformer', 'tier': 2, 'requires_tracking': True, 'trigger': {'condition': 'bench_outscores_starter', 'filters': {}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': 'bench_outperformer', 'text': 'What did {player_name} do specifically tonight that made {player_name} so effective?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': '{player_name} made the right reads within the scheme at a high rate. No forced plays, no deviations — just execution. When a player is tuned in to the scheme at that level, that player is going to produce.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'player_em_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "{player_name} played with confidence and stayed within {player_name}'s strengths. {player_name} didn't try to do too much — {player_name} did exactly what {player_name} does best and did it decisively. That's individual preparation paying off.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "{player_name} came in ready, took advantage of {player_name}'s opportunities, and made the most of {player_name}'s minutes. That's everything you can ask from a reserve player.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "{player_name} held the standard. Everything {player_name} did tonight came from meeting the standard in practice consistently. That's where tonight was built.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'player_em_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': '{player_name} played free. {player_name} came in without pressure and without hesitation, which often happens when a player is playing for the team rather than for a stat line. That freedom produced the performance.', 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_up']}]},
    {'id': 'bench_outperformer_04', 'category': 'player_performance', 'subcategory': 'bench_outperformer', 'tier': 2, 'requires_tracking': True, 'trigger': {'condition': 'bench_outscores_starter', 'filters': {}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': 'bench_outperformer', 'text': 'Nights like this for {player_name} — how do you make sure {player_name} stays hungry rather than becoming satisfied with the performance?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "The standard doesn't celebrate good nights — it builds on them. Tomorrow {player_name} comes back with the same expectations. The bar is always the next performance, not the last one.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "You raise the challenge immediately. Acknowledge the performance, then point toward the next level. The best players aren't satisfied by production — they're curious about what they can still unlock.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': 'You let {player_name} feel the success briefly and then redirect to the next challenge. Hunger comes from clear goals. You celebrate and then point forward.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': 'The locker room keeps everyone grounded. In a team-first culture, individual performances are appreciated but quickly channeled back into what the group is chasing. {player_name} knows this team has bigger goals than any one night.', 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "You show {player_name} the film immediately. You find the plays where {player_name} was even better than the box score shows and the plays where the system broke down. Excellence within the scheme is the standard — not just production. There's always more to chase.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'player_em_up']}]},
    {'id': 'ft_struggles_01', 'category': 'player_performance', 'subcategory': 'ft_struggles', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'player_ft', 'filters': {'max_ft_pct': 25, 'min_ft_attempts': 8}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': 'ft_struggles', 'text': '{player_name} struggled significantly at the free throw line tonight. Is this a recurring issue or was tonight unusual?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "It's been an area of focus. Free throw shooting is a skill and it's developable — we work on it specifically. Tonight the work didn't show up in the results. We'll go back to the fundamentals and identify what broke down mechanically.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_down', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "We practice free throws daily. There's no excuse for that performance at the line. {player_name} knows it and we'll address it directly starting tomorrow.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'player_em_down']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "It's been something we've been working on. Tonight it came at the worst time. We'll continue the development work and trust the process.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_down', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "Free throw shooting under pressure is a specific skill distinct from practice free throws. The mechanics are the same but the mental state is different. We'll add pressure components to {player_name}'s free throw routine.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'player_em_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "The team rallied around {player_name} at the line tonight. The support was there. The performance wasn't. That's a technique and confidence issue and we'll support {player_name} through developing both.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_up']}]},
    {'id': 'ft_struggles_02', 'category': 'player_performance', 'subcategory': 'ft_struggles', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'player_ft', 'filters': {'max_ft_pct': 25, 'min_ft_attempts': 8}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': 'ft_struggles', 'text': "When a player is that poor at the line, opponents will intentionally foul {player_name}. How do you counter the 'Hack-a' strategy?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "You adjust {player_name}'s deployment in late-game fouling situations — sub {player_name} out in the final two minutes when the foul strategy is most likely. And you accelerate the development work so it stops being a viable tactic against this team.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'player_em_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "You fix the problem. The real counter is {player_name} making {player_name}'s free throws. Everything else is symptom management. We fix the root cause.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'player_em_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "You manage {player_name}'s minutes in situations where that strategy is viable and you work intensely on the free throw mechanics. Both together.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'player_em_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Specific free throw pressure training. We replicate the game situation in practice — noise, crowd simulation, fatigue — until the mechanics are bulletproof under pressure. That's the only real solution.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': 'The team supports {player_name} through it. And {player_name} has to trust that the team believes in {player_name} at the line. The mental part of free throw shooting is huge — when a player knows the team is with {player_name}, the mechanics often follow.', 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_up']}]},
    {'id': 'ft_struggles_03', 'category': 'player_performance', 'subcategory': 'ft_struggles', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'player_ft', 'filters': {'max_ft_pct': 25, 'min_ft_attempts': 8}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': 'ft_struggles', 'text': 'How many points did the free throw struggles cost you tonight, and how significant was that gap?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "It was a significant margin. In a close game, free throw execution is often the determining factor. We need to close that gap — both in {player_name}'s development and in our late-game deployment decisions.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "Enough to matter. And the players know it. Free throws are the one area where effort and focus should guarantee results. When they don't, it's a focus problem and it costs us.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': 'More than we could afford in a game this close. Free throw shooting is an area we have to be better in and we will be.', 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_down', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': 'The gap was significant. And beyond the points themselves, the missed free throws affected the rhythm of our offense and the confidence of {player_name} on the possessions that followed. The ripple effect is real.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_down', 'discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "It was a difficult situation for {player_name} and the team felt it. But the team didn't abandon {player_name} — they competed harder to compensate. That's character. Now we have to help {player_name} fix the problem so we don't keep asking for that kind of collective compensation.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}]},
    {'id': 'ft_struggles_04', 'category': 'player_performance', 'subcategory': 'ft_struggles', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'player_ft', 'filters': {'max_ft_pct': 25, 'min_ft_attempts': 8}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': 'ft_struggles', 'text': "What's your message to {player_name} after a night like this at the free throw line?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': 'That we need {player_name} to be a liability-free player and right now this is a liability. Not to embarrass {player_name} — to be honest about what this program needs from {player_name} and what {player_name} owes teammates.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "That free throw shooting is the most developable skill in basketball and we're going to develop it. We'll identify the specific mechanical breakdown and we'll fix it. This is temporary. The work starts tomorrow.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "Shake it off, go back to basics, and come in ready to work on it. One difficult night at the line doesn't define you — your response to it does.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "That this team believes in {player_name} and will be with {player_name} while {player_name} works through it. But I'll also be honest that we need this to get better — because {player_name} deserves to be in the game in crucial moments, not subbed out because of this.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "We show the film together — specifically what changed mechanically between practice and game pressure. Then we build a specific free throw routine that reduces variance under pressure. It's an engineering problem and we treat it that way.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'player_em_up']}]},
    {'id': 'lockdown_defender_01', 'category': 'player_performance', 'subcategory': 'lockdown_defender', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'player_def_pct', 'filters': {'min_def_pct': 80, 'min_defa': 5}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': 'lockdown_defender', 'text': '{player_name} was exceptional defensively tonight. What was {player_name} doing that made {player_name} so difficult to score against?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "Effort and footwork in equal measure. {player_name} competed on every possession defensively. There's no mystery to it — you move your feet, you stay in front of your player, and you force the matchup into bad decisions.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Anticipation. {player_name} has been studying {player_name}'s matchup and it showed — {player_name} was a step ahead on reads. That IQ component is what separates good defenders from elite ones and {player_name} demonstrated it tonight.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "{player_name} was locked in defensively. {player_name} stayed in front of {player_name}'s assignment and made life difficult. That's what you want from your defensive stopper.", 'effect_tags': ['fight_up', 'prestige_minor_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "Perfect assignment execution. The defensive scheme gave {player_name} clear principles and {player_name} applied them precisely. Body positioning, help reads, contest angle — all by the book. That's coachability showing up in the performance.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "{player_name} competed for teammates tonight. The best defenders don't do it for the stat — they do it because they take personally the idea of someone scoring against their team. You can see that in {player_name}'s eyes when {player_name} is locked in like that.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_up', 'fight_up']}]},
    {'id': 'lockdown_defender_02', 'category': 'player_performance', 'subcategory': 'lockdown_defender', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'player_def_pct', 'filters': {'min_def_pct': 80, 'min_defa': 5}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': 'lockdown_defender', 'text': "How much of {player_name}'s defensive ability is natural and how much is developed?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': 'Eighty percent developed. The athleticism is natural. The technique, the film study, the positioning — those are earned. {player_name} has invested heavily in the craft of defending and tonight that investment showed.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "More developed than people assume. Defense is effort and discipline. You build those in practice. {player_name} competes in practice the same way {player_name} does in games. That's where the ability comes from.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': 'Both. The athleticism gives them potential. The work {player_name} has put in has developed that potential into what you see. You need both.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': 'The movement skills are natural but the system application is entirely developed. Knowing when to help, how to navigate screens, where to force the ball — those are taught. {player_name} has internalized the defensive scheme as well as anyone in this program.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'player_em_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "The will to defend is something you either have or you develop through culture. {player_name} came in with some of it and this program built more. The competitive pride on the defensive end — that's who {player_name} is, and a lot of it came from being surrounded by people who care about the same things.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_up']}]},
    {'id': 'lockdown_defender_03', 'category': 'player_performance', 'subcategory': 'lockdown_defender', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'player_def_pct', 'filters': {'min_def_pct': 80, 'min_defa': 5}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': 'lockdown_defender', 'text': "Does being known as the team's defensive stopper create any limitations for {player_name}'s offensive development?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "It can, if we let it. We're intentional about developing {player_name}'s offensive game alongside {player_name}'s defensive identity. The best players in the game are impactful on both ends. That's the standard we hold for {player_name}.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "We design {player_name}'s offensive role to complement their defensive one. {player_name} doesn't have to carry the offense — {player_name} has to be reliable within {player_name}'s specific actions. That focus creates confidence, not limitation.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'player_em_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "We try to avoid that. Every player in this program is expected to contribute on both ends. {player_name}'s defensive identity shouldn't limit their offensive development and we work to prevent it.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': 'Not in this program. The standard applies on both ends. {player_name} is expected to compete offensively at the same level {player_name} competes defensively. There are no defensive specialists who get a pass on offense.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "The team celebrates {player_name}'s offensive contributions as much as the defensive ones. When your teammates celebrate what you do on offense, it reinforces that growth. {player_name} has support on both ends of the floor.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_up']}]},
    {'id': 'lockdown_defender_04', 'category': 'player_performance', 'subcategory': 'lockdown_defender', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'player_def_pct', 'filters': {'min_def_pct': 80, 'min_defa': 5}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': 'lockdown_defender', 'text': "Defensive performances like {player_name}'s don't show up in the box score the way scoring does. How do you make sure that contribution is recognized?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "In this locker room, defense is celebrated loudly. Every stop, every lockdown possession — the team acknowledges it. That recognition doesn't come from me alone — it comes from the whole group. {player_name} knows exactly how valued this contribution is.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': 'I recognize it directly in front of the team. Publicly. Defense wins games and this program celebrates it as much as any scorer. Every player in that locker room knows that tonight {player_name} won us possessions.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'player_em_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "You call it out specifically in team meetings and in public. Defensive contributions are real and they deserve recognition. We make sure players who excel on that end know it's seen.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Film sessions. We stop the film on {player_name}'s best defensive possessions and we talk about the reads, the technique, the execution. When players see their defensive work analyzed and praised with the same rigor as offensive plays, they understand the value.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "The defensive metrics we track internally tell the story the box score doesn't. I share those with {player_name} specifically so they understand exactly how impactful their work was. Numbers that matter — not just points.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'player_em_up']}]},
    {'id': 'defensive_liability_01', 'category': 'player_performance', 'subcategory': 'defensive_liability', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'player_def_pct', 'filters': {'max_def_pct': 20, 'min_defa': 5}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': 'defensive_liability', 'text': '{player_name} had a very difficult night defensively. What was going wrong on that end?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "{player_name} didn't compete on defense. Whether it's focus, effort, or fatigue — the result is the same. We gave up too many points on {player_name}'s assignments and that is not acceptable in this program.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'player_em_down', 'prestige_minor_down']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "Positioning. {player_name} was consistently out of {player_name}'s defensive assignment — late closeouts, wrong help positioning. That's a scheme execution issue and it's correctable. But it has to be corrected.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'player_em_down', 'prestige_minor_down']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "A combination of things — tough matchup, some technique breakdowns, and an opponent who was simply making shots. We'll look at the film honestly.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_down', 'prestige_minor_down', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "I want to understand what was happening with {player_name} before I make a public assessment. The defensive breakdowns were real. The causes aren't always what they appear. I'll have that conversation privately first.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_down']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Specific technique breakdowns — I identified three or four recurring situations where {player_name} made the same wrong decision. Those situations will be replicated in practice and we'll drill the correct response until it's automatic.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}]},
    {'id': 'defensive_liability_02', 'category': 'player_performance', 'subcategory': 'defensive_liability', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'player_def_pct', 'filters': {'max_def_pct': 20, 'min_defa': 5}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': 'defensive_liability', 'text': 'When one player is being targeted defensively the way {player_name} was tonight, do you make rotational adjustments or do you ask {player_name} to work through it?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "You make schematic adjustments — add help earlier, change the defensive assignment, reduce exposure to the most difficult matchup. You protect {player_name} while {player_name} develops. You don't abandon them.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'player_em_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': 'You work through it. Taking {player_name} off the floor when {player_name} is being targeted teaches {player_name} nothing. You trust the scheme, you give them the tools to compete, and you expect them to hold the standard.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': 'Both. You make some adjustments to limit the damage and you give {player_name} a chance to compete through it. It depends on the score and the situation.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "You lean on the team. When {player_name} is being targeted, the defense becomes more collective — more communication, more help, more support. You don't isolate {player_name} and you don't hide {player_name}. You rally around them.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Targeted adjustments. You modify {player_name}'s specific defensive assignments to reduce exposure to {player_name}'s biggest weakness while you develop that weakness in practice. It's tactical and developmental simultaneously.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}]},
    {'id': 'defensive_liability_03', 'category': 'player_performance', 'subcategory': 'defensive_liability', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'player_def_pct', 'filters': {'max_def_pct': 20, 'min_defa': 5}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': 'defensive_liability', 'text': "Is {player_name}'s defensive development something that's improving over the course of the season, or is it a persistent challenge?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Improving but not fast enough. We've been doing specific defensive skill work with {player_name} all season. The improvement is real but the gap between what they're giving us and what we need is still too large. We'll increase the intensity of that work.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "It's been inconsistent and tonight was a step backward. The standard is clear and {player_name} knows what it is. {player_name} has to decide to meet it consistently. That decision hasn't been made consistently yet.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "There's been some improvement. But we need more. It's an ongoing area of focus and tonight showed us there's still significant work to do.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_down', 'prestige_minor_down', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "The scheme execution has improved. The mental consistency hasn't. When {player_name} is focused, the defensive principles work. When {player_name} is not, you see nights like tonight. We're addressing the consistency issue.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'player_em_down']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "There's development happening but nights like tonight show there's a long way to go. I believe in {player_name}'s ability to improve. I also believe the competitive pride needed to defend at a high level every night has to come from inside them — not just from coaching.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}]},
    {'id': 'defensive_liability_04', 'category': 'player_performance', 'subcategory': 'defensive_liability', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'player_def_pct', 'filters': {'max_def_pct': 20, 'min_defa': 5}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': 'defensive_liability', 'text': "How significant an issue is {player_name}'s defensive limitations for this team's ceiling?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "Significant. This program's ceiling is determined by our defensive standard. Any player who operates below that standard is a ceiling constraint. We address that directly with {player_name}.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "It's a real constraint and I won't pretend otherwise. What I believe is that {player_name} has the ability to close this gap. The question is development timeline versus what the team needs right now. We're managing that tension deliberately.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "It's an area that limits how we can use {player_name} in certain matchups. We design around it where we can and we develop it where we can. It's a real consideration.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_down', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "We build the defensive scheme around compensating for individual limitations. It creates complexity but it's manageable. Long-term, {player_name} developing as a defender raises the team's ceiling significantly. That development is a priority.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "It's something the team compensates for collectively — and that takes its toll over forty minutes. Sustainable programs don't rely on others to cover defensive gaps indefinitely. {player_name} knows this and I believe they'll respond.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_down', 'player_em_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}]},
    {'id': 'opponent_star_held_01', 'category': 'player_performance', 'subcategory': 'opponent_star_held', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'opponent_star_pts', 'filters': {'max_pts': 6, 'opponent_highest_rt': True}}, 'weight': 3, 'player_slot': 'lockdown_defender', 'text': 'You held their best player to almost nothing tonight. How much of the game plan was centered around that?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "Significant. We built the defensive game plan around taking away their primary weapon. When a team's best player doesn't score, the rest of the offense becomes predictable. We took away the threat and made them rely on players they don't typically rely on.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': 'We prepared specifically for their best player and we delivered. That preparation and execution is a significant competitive achievement. Holding an elite player to almost nothing requires perfect focus for forty minutes.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': 'It was a priority. Neutralizing their best offensive threat was central to our defensive approach. The players executed it extremely well.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "The whole team was involved in taking them away. When you hold an elite player to almost nothing, it's rarely one person's achievement — it's five guys communicating, helping, and competing together. Tonight this group did that at a very high level.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': 'Our primary defender was specifically prepared for this matchup — their tendencies, their favorite actions, their responses to various coverages. That individual preparation made the defensive game plan functional rather than theoretical.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}]},
    {'id': 'opponent_star_held_02', 'category': 'player_performance', 'subcategory': 'opponent_star_held', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'opponent_star_pts', 'filters': {'max_pts': 6, 'opponent_highest_rt': True}}, 'weight': 3, 'player_slot': 'lockdown_defender', 'text': "When you take away an opponent's best player that completely, what does it do to the rest of their team?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "It forces their system into secondary options. Most offenses are built around their best player drawing attention. When that player is held, the others have to create out of structure they're not fully prepared to execute. You see the offense break down.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "It breaks them psychologically. When your best player can't get a bucket, everyone else starts pressing. You see rushed decisions, forced shots, poor execution. Holding their best player tonight broke their whole team's confidence.", 'effect_tags': ['fight_up', 'discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "It shifts the burden to players who aren't usually primary options. That creates discomfort and usually worse decision-making. You take away the top of the food chain and the whole ecosystem suffers.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "It fractures the confidence of the whole group. When the player everyone looks to can't get comfortable, it ripples through the team. Our collective defensive focus tonight created individual discomfort that spread into team discomfort for them.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Secondary players face pressure they aren't used to. The defensive matchup on their best player transfers psychological pressure to players lower in the rotation. Our preparation was specifically designed to create that cascading effect.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}]},
    {'id': 'opponent_star_held_03', 'category': 'player_performance', 'subcategory': 'opponent_star_held', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'opponent_star_pts', 'filters': {'max_pts': 6, 'opponent_highest_rt': True}}, 'weight': 3, 'player_slot': 'lockdown_defender', 'text': 'Credit to {player_name} for the defensive assignment tonight. What specifically made {player_name} so effective in that matchup?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': '{player_name} had done significant film work on this matchup before tonight. {player_name} knew the tendencies, the preferred actions, the tells. That preparation meant {player_name} was a step ahead on almost every possession. Knowledge is the foundation of great individual defense.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "{player_name} competed for this team tonight with everything {player_name} had. The film work, the preparation, the forty minutes of intensity — all of it was for us, not for individual recognition. That's what makes {player_name} special.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "{player_name} was locked in, moved {player_name}'s feet well, and made the right help decisions. {player_name} had a great defensive game. Full credit to {player_name}.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'prestige_minor_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "{player_name} competed at the standard for forty minutes. {player_name} didn't take a possession off. When you defend for forty minutes at that level, this is the result. That's what I expect and tonight {player_name} delivered.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'player_em_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "{player_name} applied the defensive scheme at a level of precision we don't always see. Every coverage principle executed correctly in the right situation. That kind of system adherence under pressure is rare and extremely valuable.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'player_em_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}]},
    {'id': 'opponent_star_held_04', 'category': 'player_performance', 'subcategory': 'opponent_star_held', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'opponent_star_pts', 'filters': {'max_pts': 6, 'opponent_highest_rt': True}}, 'weight': 3, 'player_slot': 'lockdown_defender', 'text': 'Is this a blueprint for how you approach elite offensive players going forward?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "It's a proven execution of principles that apply against any elite player. The specific actions change based on the player, but the preparation model — deep film study, specific coverage principles, collective help structure — that's repeatable.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "The blueprint is always the same — prepare specifically, compete physically, hold the standard for forty minutes. Tonight proved the blueprint works when executed correctly. We'll execute it the same way going forward.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "Every elite player is different. Tonight's approach worked for this specific matchup. The principles are transferable but the specifics have to be rebuilt for each new challenge.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "The blueprint is collective will. When this team decides together to take something away from an opponent, they're capable of doing exactly what they did tonight. That's not a one-time achievement — it's who this group can be.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': 'For {player_name} specifically — yes. {player_name} has a proven model now for how to prepare for and execute an elite defensive assignment. That experience builds their library. Each elite matchup they study becomes another tool.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}]},
    {'id': 'team_defense_dominant_01', 'category': 'player_performance', 'subcategory': 'team_defense_dominant', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'team_def_pct', 'filters': {'min_def_pct': 70, 'min_defa': 15}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': "Your team's defensive numbers were exceptional tonight. What created that level of collective defensive performance?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "They defended for each other. When every player on the floor is competing to protect the player next to them, you get performances like tonight. That's not talent — that's trust.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "Collective scheme execution at an extremely high level. Every player in the right position, correct help rotations, tight closeouts, good contest angles. When the scheme is executed that precisely, you're going to see elite defensive numbers.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': 'Focus and effort for forty minutes. This team defended at a high level from start to finish and it showed in the numbers.', 'effect_tags': ['fight_up', 'prestige_minor_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "The standard was met. This is what this defense looks like when everyone holds the standard on every possession. It's not a surprise — it's the product of what we build every day in practice.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': 'Individual accountability on every possession. Each player took their assignment personally. When you multiply that individual ownership by five for forty minutes, you get what we saw tonight.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}]},
    {'id': 'team_defense_dominant_02', 'category': 'player_performance', 'subcategory': 'team_defense_dominant', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'team_def_pct', 'filters': {'min_def_pct': 70, 'min_defa': 15}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'Is this level of defensive performance sustainable, or does it require a specific game plan or opponent?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': 'The principles are sustainable. The specific execution level varies, but the scheme is designed for this outcome every night. Tonight we achieved it. The goal is to raise the floor closer to this ceiling.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': 'The standard is the standard regardless of opponent. Tonight we met it. I expect it again next game. Whether we achieve it is entirely up to the focus and effort of this group.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "Some opponents make it harder than others. But the level of focus and execution tonight — that's something this team can bring to any game. They've shown us what's possible.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "It's sustainable when the culture is right. The collective intensity tonight came from a shared commitment. As long as that commitment is present, we're capable of this. Building and maintaining that commitment is what we do every day.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Individual players can sustain their contribution. Collective peaks require everyone being individually dialed in simultaneously. Tonight that alignment was there. Developing each player's individual defensive consistency is how you make these nights more frequent.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}]},
    {'id': 'team_defense_dominant_03', 'category': 'player_performance', 'subcategory': 'team_defense_dominant', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'team_def_pct', 'filters': {'min_def_pct': 70, 'min_defa': 15}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'Defense-first teams have a certain identity. Is that how you see this program?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "Absolutely. In this program, defense is the foundation. It's not about offense first or defense first — it's about the standard on both ends. But if you push me to choose, I'll build a program around defense and let the offense follow. Tonight is why.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "We have a competitor's identity. Defense reflects that more than anything else — it requires will, sacrifice, and collective commitment every single possession. Tonight this team showed that identity at its best.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "We want to be a complete team. But when we're at our best defensively, it enables everything else. Tonight was a good example of what's possible when the defense sets the tone.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "The system prioritizes defensive stops as the engine of the offense. That philosophy shapes everything from practice structure to lineup decisions. It's not just an identity — it's a design choice and tonight it paid off.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': 'Defense is where individual development shows up most measurably. Offensive contributions vary by matchup, but defensive contribution is a constant reflection of preparation and commitment. I invest heavily in that development and tonight the investment produced this result.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}]},
    {'id': 'team_defense_dominant_04', 'category': 'player_performance', 'subcategory': 'team_defense_dominant', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'team_def_pct', 'filters': {'min_def_pct': 70, 'min_defa': 15}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': "What does a defensive performance like this do for a team's confidence heading into the rest of the season?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "It gives every individual player a reference point for their defensive ceiling. When players see proof of what they're capable of defensively, the next time the standard is demanded they know they can meet it. That belief is real and it compounds.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "It confirms the standard is achievable. Every player in that locker room now knows what holding the standard for forty minutes looks like. That's the expectation from here on. No excuses.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': 'It builds belief. When a team performs at this level defensively, they know they can win any game. That confidence is valuable and we have to protect it.', 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_up', 'team_mo_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "It builds shared identity. When a team defends together at this level, it bonds them. There's a shared experience of collective excellence that's hard to create any other way. This team has that now.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'prestige_minor_up', 'fan_interest_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "It validates the system. Every player who's committed to the defensive scheme now has proof that full commitment produces elite outcomes. That proof makes the next commitment easier and the next defensive performance more likely.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up', 'team_mo_up']}]},
    {'id': 'prestige_new_high_01', 'category': 'program_context', 'subcategory': 'prestige_new_high', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'prestige_new_high', 'filters': {}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'This program is at its highest prestige point right now. What does that mean to you?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "It means the players who've been here, who bought into this from the beginning — they're getting to see what they built. That matters more to me than any ranking or number. This belongs to them.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'prestige_major_up', 'fan_interest_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "It means the work is paying off. Not cause for celebration — cause for more work. Programs that peak and stop pushing don't stay at their peak. We keep building.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_major_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "It's a meaningful milestone. The program is in a better place than it's ever been. Now the challenge is sustaining it and building further from here.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_major_up', 'fan_interest_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "It means the system is producing at its designed level. Every structural decision we've made — recruiting philosophy, development model, scheme — is reflected in that number. It validates the approach.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_major_up', 'fan_interest_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': 'It means individual players are reaching their potential at a higher rate than ever before. Program prestige is the sum of individual excellence. This number tells me the development model is working.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'prestige_major_up', 'fan_interest_up']}]},
    {'id': 'prestige_new_high_02', 'category': 'program_context', 'subcategory': 'prestige_new_high', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'prestige_new_high', 'filters': {}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': "Reaching a new prestige high — does that change recruiting conversations or the program's ability to attract talent?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "It helps. Recruits want to be part of something rising. But we recruit on culture and development first. The prestige validates what we tell recruits — it doesn't replace what we tell them.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_major_up', 'fan_interest_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': 'It opens doors. Recruits who may not have considered us are now paying attention. That increases the pool we can draw from. What we do with that pool depends on the quality of our pitch and our development model.', 'effect_tags': ['prestige_major_up', 'fan_interest_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': 'Significantly. Prestige matters in recruiting. Players want to play for programs that are going somewhere. Right now this program clearly is.', 'effect_tags': ['prestige_major_up', 'fan_interest_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "The culture was always the best recruiting pitch. This makes it easier for recruits to believe the culture we're describing. You can see it in the results — and that's a powerful thing to point to.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'prestige_major_up', 'fan_interest_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "It validates our development claims. When we tell recruits we'll make them better — this is the proof. Players want to be developed and they want to know it's real. The prestige supports that narrative.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'prestige_major_up', 'fan_interest_up']}]},
    {'id': 'prestige_new_high_03', 'category': 'program_context', 'subcategory': 'prestige_new_high', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'prestige_new_high', 'filters': {}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': "What's the next milestone from here? What does continued growth look like for this program?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "Sustained consistency. Reaching a new prestige high is meaningful. Staying there and building further is the real test of whether the system is sound. The next milestone isn't a number — it's durability.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_major_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "The next level of competition. We should be playing in bigger games against better teams. That's what continued growth looks like. Not the prestige score itself — the caliber of competition that prestige attracts.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_major_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': 'Winning at the highest level of the conference and making a deep tournament run. The prestige is a means to that end, not the end itself.', 'effect_tags': ['prestige_major_up', 'fan_interest_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "Building something that lasts beyond the current players and staff. Real program growth is when the next generation of players arrives and the standard is already set for them. That's what we're building toward.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'prestige_major_up', 'fan_interest_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': 'More players reaching their individual ceilings. The prestige follows from that. As long as we keep developing players at the highest level, the program metrics will reflect it.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'prestige_major_up']}]},
    {'id': 'prestige_new_high_04', 'category': 'program_context', 'subcategory': 'prestige_new_high', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'prestige_new_high', 'filters': {}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'Who deserves the most credit for getting this program to this point?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': 'The players. Every player who walked into that gym and chose to compete for something bigger than themselves — they built this. The coaches create the conditions. The players create the program.', 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_up', 'prestige_major_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "Everyone who held the standard. Players, coaches, staff — the people who refused to accept less than what this program is capable of. That's a collective achievement.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_major_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "It's a team effort across the entire program. Players, coaches, staff, the support structure around this program — everyone has contributed.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_major_up', 'fan_interest_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "The players who trusted the system before they saw results. It's easy to trust a process that's already working. The players who committed when the proof wasn't there yet — they built the foundation.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_major_up', 'fan_interest_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Every player who committed to their individual development. Program prestige is built player by player. Each one who got better, who reached a new level — they're the program.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'prestige_major_up']}]},
    {'id': 'prestige_decline_01', 'category': 'program_context', 'subcategory': 'prestige_decline', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'prestige_drop_streak', 'filters': {'min_weeks': 3}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': "The program's prestige has been declining over the past few weeks. What's driving that and what's the response?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "Results. Prestige follows performance and performance hasn't been at the standard. The response is the same as always — get back to work, hold the standard, and let the results fix the number.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_major_down']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "A combination of our own results and the competitive landscape shifting. We've identified the execution gaps that are costing us. There's a plan in place and I'm confident we'll reverse this.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_major_down']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "Results have not been where they need to be. We're addressing that directly. Programs go through periods like this — the ones that survive them do so by focusing on what they can control.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_major_down', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "We've had a rough stretch and it shows up in every metric. The response is to reconnect as a group — to remember why we're here and who we're doing this for. The prestige will follow when we're playing the right way again.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_major_down']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Individual performances have declined and it's showing program-wide. We're doing specific development work to address the drop in execution quality. The prestige is a lagging indicator — fix the individual performance first.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up', 'prestige_major_down']}]},
    {'id': 'prestige_decline_02', 'category': 'program_context', 'subcategory': 'prestige_decline', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'prestige_drop_streak', 'filters': {'min_weeks': 3}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'A sustained prestige decline affects recruiting, fan interest, everything. How urgent is turning this around?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "Extremely urgent. This program has a standard and right now we're not meeting it. The urgency isn't about the prestige number — it's about getting back to who we are. That happens now.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_major_down']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "Urgent but manageable. Programs go through downturns. What matters is how they respond. I'm confident this group has the character to respond correctly. The urgency is real but so is my belief in this team.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_major_down']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "Very urgent. We're aware of the downstream effects and we're working to address this quickly. There are clear things we need to do better and we're doing them.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_major_down', 'fan_interest_down', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "The system identifies the corrections needed. I'm not panicking but I am moving with intention. Three weeks of decline tells you there's a structural issue, not just variance. We're fixing the structure.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_major_down']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Very. The players feel it too — their individual confidence is tied to the program's momentum. Breaking the decline isn't just about metrics — it's about getting individuals back to competing at their level. That's the priority.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up', 'prestige_major_down']}]},
    {'id': 'prestige_decline_03', 'category': 'program_context', 'subcategory': 'prestige_decline', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'prestige_drop_streak', 'filters': {'min_weeks': 3}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': "Is the prestige decline a reflection of this team's talent level or an execution problem that can be fixed?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Execution. The talent on this roster is real. The gap between the talent and the results is a development and mental focus issue, not a ceiling issue. We're closing that gap specifically and deliberately.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up', 'prestige_major_down']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "Execution. I've seen this team compete. The talent is there. The standard hasn't been met consistently. That's correctable and we're correcting it.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_major_down']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "Primarily execution. The talent is sufficient to compete at a higher level than we've shown recently. Getting back to consistent execution is the path out of this.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_major_down', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "Execution at the system level. The personnel can run the system — they've done it. The consistency of that execution has dropped. That's a focus and preparation issue, not a talent ceiling.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_major_down']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "Collective focus. When this group is locked in together, the results follow. We've lost some of that collective urgency. Rebuilding it isn't about talent — it's about culture, and culture is something we can control.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_major_down']}]},
    {'id': 'prestige_decline_04', 'category': 'program_context', 'subcategory': 'prestige_decline', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'prestige_drop_streak', 'filters': {'min_weeks': 3}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'What does this program need to show to start rebuilding confidence — internally and externally?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "Wins. That's what rebuilds confidence internally and externally. Not speeches, not meetings — wins that come from the standard being met. We start there.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': 'Competitive effort with each other. Internally, the players need to see each other fight. That reconnection is what produces the results that rebuild external confidence. The inside job comes first.', 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "Consistent competitive effort and some results to show for it. Both internally and externally, the program needs to demonstrate it can compete at a high level again. We're working toward that.", 'effect_tags': ['fight_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': 'System execution. When the scheme is being run correctly, the results improve. Internally, players trust the system when it produces results. Externally, programs that execute consistently are respected regardless of recent record.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_major_down']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Individual players taking ownership. When I see each player accept personal responsibility for the program's current state and compete differently as a result — that's when the turnaround starts. It begins individually.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}]},
    {'id': 'entered_top_25_01', 'category': 'program_context', 'subcategory': 'entered_top_25', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'entered_top_25_first_time', 'filters': {}}, 'weight': 3, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'This program is in the top 25 for the first time. What does that moment mean?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "It means the players who were here when nobody was paying attention — when this program was building in the dark — they get to see what that belief built. It's for them. All of it.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'prestige_major_up', 'fan_interest_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "It means the work is visible now. What we've been building was always this — the ranking just confirms it for people who weren't watching. We keep working the same way.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_major_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "It's a significant milestone for this program and everyone associated with it. We're proud of it. Now we have to show we belong here.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_major_up', 'fan_interest_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "It's confirmation that the system can produce at a nationally relevant level. The design was always built for this. The players have executed it at the level it requires. That's the meaning.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_major_up', 'fan_interest_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "It's validation for every player who chose this program and committed to their development here. The ranking is a reflection of individual excellence multiplied across the roster. They earned this.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'prestige_major_up', 'fan_interest_up']}]},
    {'id': 'entered_top_25_02', 'category': 'program_context', 'subcategory': 'entered_top_25', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'entered_top_25_first_time', 'filters': {}}, 'weight': 3, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'Being ranked changes how opponents prepare for you and how players see this program. How do you manage that shift?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "The same way you manage everything — with the standard. The ranking changes nothing about what we expect from ourselves. If anything, the standard gets harder to meet because everyone is now preparing specifically for us. That's a challenge I welcome.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_major_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': 'Opponents will have more film on us. Our scheme will face more targeted preparation. That requires us to have more answers, more counters, more depth within the system. The ranking raises the bar on our preparation.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_major_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "You keep the focus internal. The ranking is external validation — the preparation and the standard are internal. You don't let the outside noise change the inside work.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_major_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "You lean on the identity. When a team knows who they are — deeply, collectively — the noise around the ranking doesn't penetrate. We've built something with roots. A ranking doesn't shake roots.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'discipline_up', 'prestige_major_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': 'You address it individually. Each player responds differently to the pressure of a ranking. Some need to be reminded to stay humble, some need to be reminded they deserve this. The management is personal.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}]},
    {'id': 'entered_top_25_03', 'category': 'program_context', 'subcategory': 'entered_top_25', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'entered_top_25_first_time', 'filters': {}}, 'weight': 3, 'player_slot': None, 'text': "For recruits watching, what message does this program's top-25 ranking send?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': 'That this is a place where players get better and the results follow. Every recruit wants to see development translate to national recognition. This ranking is proof that it does — at this program, right now.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'prestige_major_up', 'fan_interest_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "That this community shows up and supports something real. That the culture here is not just words — it produces results. Any recruit who's looking for a program that's building something genuine should be watching us right now.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'prestige_major_up', 'fan_interest_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': 'That this is a program on the rise. Recruits want to be part of something with momentum. Right now this program has it.', 'effect_tags': ['prestige_major_up', 'fan_interest_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "That if you come here and hold the standard, you'll compete for something significant. The ranking is proof. It wasn't handed to us. We built it. Recruits who want to build something should take notice.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_major_up', 'fan_interest_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "That the system works. A recruit can look at this program and see that players who commit to the scheme compete at a nationally relevant level. That's a concrete promise. The ranking makes it visible.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_major_up', 'fan_interest_up']}]},
    {'id': 'entered_top_25_04', 'category': 'program_context', 'subcategory': 'entered_top_25', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'entered_top_25_first_time', 'filters': {}}, 'weight': 3, 'player_slot': None, 'text': "Once you're in the top 25, staying there becomes the new challenge. How do you build that sustainability?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "The same way you got here — the standard. Programs fall out of the top 25 when they let the ranking do the motivating. We don't. The standard motivates us. The ranking is just feedback.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_major_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "By continuing to evolve the system. Programs that stay ranked are programs that don't let opponents solve them completely. You keep adding answers, keep deepening the system, keep making yourself harder to prepare for.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_major_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "Consistent execution over a long stretch. Getting there is one thing — staying there is about depth, preparation, and resisting complacency. We'll address all three.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_major_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "Culture. Programs that sustain rankings have cultures that don't let one week's result — good or bad — define the whole. We build that every day. That's what keeps a program in the conversation long-term.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'prestige_major_up', 'fan_interest_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': 'By continuing to develop every player on the roster. When the program keeps producing at an individual level, the collective metrics follow. The ranking is sustainable as long as the development pipeline is working.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'prestige_major_up']}]},
    {'id': 'fell_out_top_25_01', 'category': 'program_context', 'subcategory': 'fell_out_top_25', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'fell_out_top_25', 'filters': {}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'The program has dropped out of the rankings. How do you process that publicly and privately?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "Publicly — we acknowledge it and move forward. Privately — I'm direct with the team. The ranking reflects the standard we held and the standard wasn't high enough. That changes immediately.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_major_down']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "Publicly, I protect this group. The ranking is a number and numbers change. Privately, we're honest about what got us here and what we owe each other going forward. We fell together — we'll get back together.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_major_down']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "Honestly. We acknowledge the decline, we're clear about what needs to improve, and we focus on the work. Rankings come and go. How we respond to falling out is what defines us.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_major_down', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "Analytically. The drop tells us exactly where the execution gaps are — what we gave up that we shouldn't have, where the scheme broke down. The ranking is data. We use it.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_major_down']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Directly with each player individually. The ranking fell because individual performances declined. That's where the conversation has to happen — one by one, honestly, with a clear path forward.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up', 'prestige_major_down']}]},
    {'id': 'fell_out_top_25_02', 'category': 'program_context', 'subcategory': 'fell_out_top_25', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'fell_out_top_25', 'filters': {}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'Does falling out of the rankings create a motivational opportunity, or is it purely a setback?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "Both, and I'll use both. Publicly it's a setback — I don't spin it otherwise. Privately, in that locker room, we talk about what it costs to get back. Hunger is a powerful motivator and this will create hunger.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_major_down']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "In the right culture, it's an opportunity. This group has something to prove together now. The teams I've seen respond best to adversity are the ones with deep enough trust to be honest with each other and compete their way back.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_major_down']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "There's motivation in adversity. We've been here before — used setbacks as fuel. I expect this group to respond the same way.", 'effect_tags': ['fight_up', 'prestige_major_down', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "It's primarily a data point and secondarily a motivational tool. The data tells us what to fix. The motivation is a byproduct of fixing it. I don't lead with emotion — I lead with the plan.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_major_down']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "For certain players, absolutely a motivational opportunity. External validation matters to some players more than others. For those players, this will light a fire. I know which ones and I'll have those conversations directly.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_major_down']}]},
    {'id': 'fell_out_top_25_03', 'category': 'program_context', 'subcategory': 'fell_out_top_25', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'fell_out_top_25', 'filters': {}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': "What's the message to the fan base when the program drops out of the rankings?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "Stay with us. This program is built on something real — not a ranking, not a hot stretch. Real programs go through this. Our fans have seen what we're capable of. We'll get back there. We need them in that building.", 'effect_tags': ['fan_interest_down', 'team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "That we hear them, we share the frustration, and we're going to fix it. Not with words — with results. That's what this program does.", 'effect_tags': ['fan_interest_down', 'discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "We acknowledge where we are, we thank them for their patience and support, and we commit to getting back. That's the honest message.", 'effect_tags': ['fan_interest_down', 'prestige_major_down', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "Trust the system. We've built something that works. This is a correction, not a collapse. The fans who understand what we're building will stay patient. The results will bring everyone else back.", 'effect_tags': ['fan_interest_down', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Come watch these players fight their way back. What you see in the next several games will tell you more about this program's character than the ranking ever could. I believe in these players to respond.", 'effect_tags': ['fan_interest_down', 'player_em_up', 'fight_up']}]},
    {'id': 'fell_out_top_25_04', 'category': 'program_context', 'subcategory': 'fell_out_top_25', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'fell_out_top_25', 'filters': {}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': "What's the realistic timeline for getting back into the rankings?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "That's determined by performance, not timelines. We hold the standard, we win the right games, and the ranking follows. I don't set external timelines — I set internal standards. Meet those and the timeline takes care of itself.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "I don't put a timeline on it. The focus is on getting back to playing the right way. When this team plays the right way consistently, the results follow and the rankings follow that. You don't chase rankings — you chase the work.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "Rankings move week to week. A strong stretch of games can move the needle quickly. I'm not going to speculate publicly — I'll let the results do that.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_major_down', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': 'The system gives me a clear view of what has to improve and by how much to reverse this. When those corrections are made and sustained — and I believe they will be — the ranking will reflect it. My estimate is several weeks of quality execution.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_major_down']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': 'As soon as individual players recommit to the performance level this program requires. That commitment can happen immediately. The ranking is a lagging indicator — the individual turnaround can be immediate.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}]},
    {'id': 'chemistry_high_01', 'category': 'program_context', 'subcategory': 'chemistry_high', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'team_chemistry', 'filters': {'min_chemistry': 20}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': "There's a sense that this team is really clicking together right now. What's driving that cohesion?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "The relationships are real. When players genuinely care about each other — not just as teammates but as people — the basketball reflects it. You can't manufacture what this group has right now. It's been built over time.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'prestige_minor_up', 'fan_interest_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "Shared standards. When everyone in a locker room holds each other to the same expectation and trusts that the person next to them is doing the same, that's chemistry. It's accountability made visible.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "Results and shared experience. Teams come together through competition and through going through things together. This group has had both this season and it's showing.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'prestige_minor_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': 'System mastery creating confidence. When players trust the scheme completely, they trust each other within it. That trust reduces friction and increases communication. The chemistry is partly a byproduct of everyone knowing their role deeply.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'team_chemistry_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Individual players operating at their best and recognizing that their teammates are too. When every player trusts the person next to them because they've seen that person grow — that's a different kind of chemistry. It's earned.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'team_chemistry_up']}]},
    {'id': 'chemistry_high_02', 'category': 'program_context', 'subcategory': 'chemistry_high', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'team_chemistry', 'filters': {'min_chemistry': 20}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'High team chemistry is rare. How do you protect it rather than take it for granted?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "You keep doing the things that built it. Team dinners, honest conversations, practices where people compete for each other. Chemistry isn't a state — it's a practice. You maintain it by practicing it every day.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': 'You hold the standard. Chemistry fractures when accountability disappears — when winning becomes an excuse for softness. I keep the standard exactly where it is regardless of how well things are going.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'team_chemistry_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': 'Communication and honesty. Chemistry erodes when issues go unaddressed. You protect it by staying direct with each other even when things are going well.', 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'discipline_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': 'By maintaining the conditions that created it — clear roles, consistent preparation, fair deployment decisions. Chemistry follows from structure. Protect the structure and the chemistry follows.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'team_chemistry_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Individual investment in each player's experience. Chemistry stays high when every player feels seen and valued. I keep that individual connection active even when the collective is flourishing.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'team_chemistry_up']}]},
    {'id': 'chemistry_high_03', 'category': 'program_context', 'subcategory': 'chemistry_high', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'team_chemistry', 'filters': {'min_chemistry': 20}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'How much does chemistry translate directly to wins versus other factors?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "Chemistry reduces execution friction. Teams that communicate well and trust each other make fewer mental errors and recover from mistakes faster. It doesn't score points but it makes the scheme more efficient. The translation to wins is real.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'team_chemistry_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': 'Significantly in close games. When the game is tight and everything is on the line, the team that trusts each other executes better under pressure. Chemistry is a competitive advantage that shows up when it matters most.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'team_chemistry_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "It's a multiplier on talent. High chemistry teams maximize what they have. Low chemistry teams underperform their talent. For this group, it's been a real competitive advantage.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'prestige_minor_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "I believe chemistry is foundational to everything. The technical elements — scheme, preparation, matchups — matter. But teams that play for each other find ways to win that talented but fractured teams don't.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': 'High chemistry makes every individual better. When players trust their teammates to cover for them, they play more freely. Playing freely produces better individual performance. So chemistry raises individual ceilings — and that translates directly to wins.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'team_chemistry_up']}]},
    {'id': 'chemistry_high_04', 'category': 'program_context', 'subcategory': 'chemistry_high', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'team_chemistry', 'filters': {'min_chemistry': 20}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': "Is there a player or group of players who's been the heartbeat of this team's chemistry?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "I'll keep the specifics in the locker room. What I'll say is that the players who hold the standard when it's hard to hold it — those are the chemistry leaders. This team has those players.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'team_chemistry_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': 'There are players who give this team its character — who set the tone in how they treat each other every day. I see it in practice more than in games. Those players are the heartbeat and they know how important they are.', 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "The chemistry is collective. There are leaders, yes, but it takes every player buying in. I'm proud of this whole group for what they've built.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': 'Players who execute their roles with complete buy-in create chemistry by example. When others see that commitment, they match it. The chemistry leaders in this program are the ones who lead through execution.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'team_chemistry_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': 'There are individuals who make every player around them better — not by being the best player, but by being the most invested. Those players are the chemistry glue and they deserve significant credit for what this team has built.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'team_chemistry_up']}]},
    {'id': 'chemistry_low_01', 'category': 'program_context', 'subcategory': 'chemistry_low', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'team_chemistry', 'filters': {'max_chemistry': 10}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': "There's been some reporting about tension within this program. What's the current state of things in the locker room?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': 'Every program has internal friction. What separates programs is how they address it. We address it directly, with standards, and without drama. Everything else stays in the locker room.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'team_chemistry_down']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "We're going through something difficult together right now. I'm not going to pretend otherwise. The important thing is that we're addressing it as a group — openly, honestly, and with the shared goal of getting this right.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "Every team faces challenges. How you work through them defines you. We're working through ours. I'll leave the specifics internal.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_down', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "When a system isn't functioning cohesively, you identify where the breakdowns are and fix them structurally. We've done that evaluation and we're making adjustments. I'm not concerned about what's being reported externally.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'team_chemistry_down']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "I'm having individual conversations with every player in this program. The cohesion issues start individually and they're resolved individually. The group will follow once the individual situations are addressed.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'team_chemistry_down']}]},
    {'id': 'chemistry_low_02', 'category': 'program_context', 'subcategory': 'chemistry_low', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'team_chemistry', 'filters': {'max_chemistry': 10}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': "Low team chemistry is one of the harder coaching challenges. What's the path to rebuilding it?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "Shared adversity and shared honesty. Teams rebuild chemistry when they go through something hard together and choose to pull toward each other rather than apart. We're in that moment. I'm trying to lead them toward each other.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': 'Standards and results. Teams that are losing and fractured find each other again when winning creates a reason to. I create the conditions for winning — the chemistry follows from accountability and results.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'team_chemistry_down']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "Communication and time. You address the issues directly, you rebuild trust through shared experiences, and you give it time to develop. There's no shortcut.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "You clarify roles and reduce ambiguity. Most chemistry problems have structural roots — players who don't know their role feel insecure, and insecurity breeds friction. Clarity is the first step.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'team_chemistry_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Individual investment. You build chemistry by making each player feel valued and seen. When every player knows their individual contribution matters, the collective improves. I'm investing intensely in each person right now.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'team_chemistry_up']}]},
    {'id': 'chemistry_low_03', 'category': 'program_context', 'subcategory': 'chemistry_low', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'team_chemistry', 'filters': {'max_chemistry': 10}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': "Is this a leadership problem within the roster, or something that's come from the coaching staff?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "Everything starts with the coaching staff. If this program has a chemistry problem, it starts with whether I've created the right conditions. I take full accountability for that and I'm addressing it directly.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'team_chemistry_down']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "It's collective. Culture problems are always collective — they don't have a single source. What matters now is that the solution is also collective. I'm doing my part and I'm asking the players to do theirs.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "I'm not going to assign blame publicly. We're working through it internally and that's where the accountability will be addressed.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_down', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "Chemistry fractures when the system isn't providing enough clarity and structure. That's a staff responsibility. We've identified specific structural adjustments that will help and we're implementing them.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'team_chemistry_down']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Both have to answer for their part. I'll answer for mine directly with the staff. I'm asking the players to answer for theirs — individually, in private conversations with me. This doesn't get fixed with public assignments of blame.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}]},
    {'id': 'chemistry_low_04', 'category': 'program_context', 'subcategory': 'chemistry_low', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'team_chemistry', 'filters': {'max_chemistry': 10}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'How long can a program compete effectively with chemistry this low?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "Not long at a high level. The standard eventually requires cohesion. You can compete on talent alone for a stretch, but the ceiling drops fast. We're addressing this now because the alternative is unacceptable.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'team_chemistry_down']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "Not as long as we need to compete for what this program is chasing. Chemistry isn't optional — it's the engine. We need it and we're building it back. This is the most urgent thing on my plate right now.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "It's a real constraint. Low chemistry creates execution problems that compound over a season. We can't sustain our goals without improving this. It's a priority.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_down', 'prestige_minor_down', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "The system can compensate for some chemistry loss through structure and clarity. But there's a floor — below it, even the best scheme can't function. We're working to stay above that floor and rebuild.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'team_chemistry_down']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Individuals can carry a fractured team for a while. But it costs those individuals, and eventually it costs the program. Sustainable competition requires collective belief. We have to rebuild that before it costs us what we're working toward.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'team_chemistry_down', 'fight_up']}]},
    {'id': 'above_500_first_time_01', 'category': 'program_context', 'subcategory': 'above_500_first_time', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'above_500_first_time_season', 'filters': {}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': "You're above .500 for the first time this season. What does that milestone mean for this group?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "It means the fight was worth it. This team has been through a difficult stretch and they kept competing for each other. Getting above .500 is validation that the belief wasn't misplaced. I'm really proud of these guys.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "It's a baseline. In this program, winning more than you lose is a minimum standard. Getting here took too long. Now we hold it and build further.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "It's an important psychological marker. Being above .500 changes how the team thinks about itself and what's possible. We needed to get here and now we need to stay here.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_up', 'team_mo_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "The system is now producing more wins than losses — that's what this number reflects. The next step is understanding what's been producing the wins and doubling down on that execution.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': 'Individual players seeing their development translate to team results. That connection — between personal growth and collective outcome — is one of the most important things a developing player can experience.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'prestige_minor_up', 'team_mo_up']}]},
    {'id': 'above_500_first_time_02', 'category': 'program_context', 'subcategory': 'above_500_first_time', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'above_500_first_time_season', 'filters': {}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'It took a while to get here. What was the hardest part of staying the course when things were difficult?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "Maintaining the standard when results weren't there. It's easy to hold the standard when you're winning. Holding it through the difficult stretch — that's where this team's character was built and proven.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "Keeping the players believing in each other. When results don't come, doubt creeps in. The hardest part was protecting the faith this group has in one another. We did it and this is what it built.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "Keeping everyone focused on the process rather than the record. When you're below .500, the temptation is to fixate on the number. We stayed focused on what we could control and trusted the results would follow.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "Trust in the system during the losing stretch. Players questioned the scheme when results weren't there. Maintaining scheme commitment during adversity is always the hardest thing to sustain. Tonight that commitment paid off.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Keeping individual players from losing faith in their own development. When the team is struggling, individuals internalize it. The hardest part was maintaining each player's belief in their own growth when the collective results weren't reflecting it.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'fight_up']}]},
    {'id': 'above_500_first_time_03', 'category': 'program_context', 'subcategory': 'above_500_first_time', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'above_500_first_time_season', 'filters': {}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': "Now that you're here, what's the target for the rest of the season?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "The next game. We don't set seasonal targets from here. You hold the standard, you win the next game, and you keep building. The season takes care of itself.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "To finish the season playing our best basketball and competing together at the highest level we're capable of. Whatever the record reflects from that effort — we'll accept it. I want the process to be right.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "Finishing strong and putting ourselves in the best possible position for the postseason. We've gotten to a good place — now we stay here and build toward something more.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': 'Continued execution improvement and finishing with a record that earns us the seeding we deserve. The system is working — the goal is consistency through the end of the schedule.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': 'Every player hitting their stride individually before the postseason. The record will be what it is. I want every player to be performing at their best when the games matter most.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}]},
    {'id': 'above_500_first_time_04', 'category': 'program_context', 'subcategory': 'above_500_first_time', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'above_500_first_time_season', 'filters': {}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'This team fought through adversity to get here. What does that journey say about who this group is?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "It says they have genuine character. Character isn't proven by winning when everything is going right — it's proven by competing when nothing is going right. This team proved theirs. I couldn't be more proud.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "It says they're hard. Getting to .500 through adversity is harder than getting there on a run. This team fought for every win and that tells you something about what they're built for.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "It says they're resilient and competitive. Those are qualities that matter when the games get bigger. This stretch gave us information about who this team is under pressure.", 'effect_tags': ['fight_up', 'prestige_minor_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "It says the system has depth. You only find out whether a scheme holds under adversity when you face real adversity. This team and this scheme proved they hold. That's significant going forward.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "It says these players grow through difficulty. That's the single most important attribute in a developing player. The players who got better when things were hard this season will be the ones who carry us when it matters most.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'prestige_minor_up', 'fan_interest_up']}]},
    {'id': 'below_500_01', 'category': 'program_context', 'subcategory': 'below_500', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'fell_below_500', 'filters': {}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': "You're below .500. How honest are you being with yourself and this program about where things stand?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "Completely honest. This program is below the standard. That's unacceptable and it won't be the final word on this season. But I won't pretend it's acceptable either. We address it directly and we fix it.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "Fully honest with the team and with myself. We've had a meeting about it. The honesty is painful but it's necessary. Programs that pretend things are fine when they're not don't fix things. We're being real with each other.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "Very honest. The record is what it is. We're working to change it. I'm not going to sugarcoat where we are — but I also believe in this group's ability to respond.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_down', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "The film doesn't allow for self-deception. We know exactly where the execution is failing and what it's costing us. The honesty is already there — now the question is whether the corrections are fast enough.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "I'm having the hardest conversations I've had all season with individual players. Full honesty, no cushioning. They deserve that and the program needs it. We can't fix what we won't acknowledge.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}]},
    {'id': 'below_500_02', 'category': 'program_context', 'subcategory': 'below_500', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'fell_below_500', 'filters': {}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'What needs to fundamentally change for this program to get back above .500?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': 'The standard has to be held every single day. Not selectively — every day. When that happens, performance improves and results follow. The problem is the standard is being held inconsistently. That ends now.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "The players have to recommit to each other. When we're playing for each other — not for the stat line, not for individual recognition — we're hard to beat. We've lost that and we need to get it back.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "Execution in the areas where we're consistently breaking down. We know what they are. Fixing them isn't a mystery — it requires commitment and repetition. We're working on both.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "Two or three specific scheme execution areas that have been costing us games. They're identifiable and correctable. When those are fixed, our margin in close games improves and the record follows.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': 'Key players have to rediscover their individual form. The collective record reflects the sum of individual performances. When two or three players get back to competing at their level, the team record responds.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}]},
    {'id': 'below_500_03', 'category': 'program_context', 'subcategory': 'below_500', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'fell_below_500', 'filters': {}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'Is there a risk that being below .500 at this point in the season has done lasting damage to the program?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "Only if we let it. Programs aren't defined by their worst stretch — they're defined by how they respond to it. The damage is real and temporary. The response is what lasts.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "Reputationally — yes, there's short-term damage. But programs built on genuine culture bounce back. What we've built here is real. The record is a temporary reflection of a difficult stretch, not a permanent statement about who we are.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "There's recruiting and confidence damage that takes time to undo. We're aware of it. The answer is sustained quality performance that changes the narrative over the coming weeks.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_down', 'fan_interest_down', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "The system is sound. When the system is sound and the execution returns, programs recover quickly. I'm not concerned about lasting damage — I'm focused on accelerating the execution recovery.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "The players' individual confidence is the most fragile thing right now. If we don't reverse this soon, some players' development trajectories could be affected. That's the priority — protecting their belief in themselves while we fight back.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}]},
    {'id': 'below_500_04', 'category': 'program_context', 'subcategory': 'below_500', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'fell_below_500', 'filters': {}}, 'weight': 2, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'What do you need to see from this team before you believe the turnaround is real?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Individual players competing at their level for consecutive games — not just one good night. I need to see the performance sustained. One game is momentum. Three games is a trend. That's what I'm waiting for.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "The standard held for thirty consecutive minutes of any one game. Not a full game — thirty minutes of real standard. That's the first sign. Then we build from there.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': 'Consistent effort and execution for a stretch of games. Not a single great performance — a pattern. Patterns are what build programs, not single games.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "Players competing for each other again. When I see five guys on that floor playing like they need each other — not just playing well individually — that's when I'll believe the turnaround is real.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "Three consecutive games where the specific execution failures we've identified are corrected. Not perfect games — but games where those specific areas show real improvement. That's the proof I need that the adjustments are taking hold.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_down']}]},
    {'id': 'season_opener_01', 'category': 'season_phase', 'subcategory': 'season_opener', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'first_game_of_season', 'filters': {}}, 'weight': 3, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'First game of the season. What was the most important thing you wanted to see from this team tonight?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "Standard execution from the opening tip. I don't care about the opponent in the first game — I care whether this team plays at their level. Tonight told me what our baseline is. Now we build from it.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': 'Whether the work of the offseason translated. Practices and scrimmages are one thing — real competition is another. I wanted to see this team play for each other in a real game. What I saw gave me confidence about this group.', 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "Competitive effort and baseline execution. The first game isn't about being perfect — it's about establishing what this team is and starting to build from that foundation.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "System execution. We've spent the entire offseason installing scheme. The first game tells you how much transferred from practice to game speed. What I saw was — partly — encouraging. There are things to build on and things to fix.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Each player in a real game situation doing what they've developed in the offseason. The first game is data — who's ready, who needs more development, who surprised me. Tonight gave me a lot of that information.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}]},
    {'id': 'season_opener_02', 'category': 'season_phase', 'subcategory': 'season_opener', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'first_game_of_season', 'filters': {}}, 'weight': 3, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'What did the offseason teach this program and how much of that showed up tonight?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "We expanded the scheme significantly and added depth to our counters. Enough of it showed up tonight to validate the offseason work. There are elements that need more game reps before they're fully reliable. That's expected.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': 'The offseason taught this team what the standard looks like at the next level. How much showed up tonight depends on your definition of enough. Mine is higher than what I saw. We keep working.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "We worked on specific things over the offseason and some of them showed up tonight. There's always a translation period between practice and game execution. We'll get there.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': 'The offseason built relationships. New players got integrated, returning players deepened their bonds. That showed up in communication and trust tonight in ways that are harder to measure than box score stats.', 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': 'Individual players developed specific skills this offseason and several of them showed up in real game situations tonight for the first time. That translation is never complete after game one, but the foundation is there.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}]},
    {'id': 'season_opener_03', 'category': 'season_phase', 'subcategory': 'season_opener', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'first_game_of_season', 'filters': {}}, 'weight': 3, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'What are your goals for this program this season?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': 'Win. Be competitive at the highest level of this conference. Get into the postseason and compete there. I set concrete goals and I expect this team to meet them. Tonight is the first step.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "To build something these players will look back on when they're thirty-five and feel proud of. Championships matter — but the way you built them matters more. I want this to be a team people talk about for who they were, not just what they accomplished.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'prestige_minor_up', 'fan_interest_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': 'Compete for a conference title and put ourselves in the postseason conversation. Those are the metrics. Beyond that, we want to continue developing the program in the right direction.', 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_up', 'fan_interest_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': 'Reach full system command by mid-season and be playing our best basketball when the conference schedule tightens. The scheme is capable of competing at the highest level. The goal is having the players executing it there.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': 'Every player on this roster reaching a new personal ceiling. The wins follow from that. I want to look back at the end of this season and see a team that got better individually — and a team that won as a result.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'prestige_minor_up', 'fan_interest_up']}]},
    {'id': 'season_opener_04', 'category': 'season_phase', 'subcategory': 'season_opener', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'first_game_of_season', 'filters': {}}, 'weight': 3, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'Who on this roster are you most curious about as the season unfolds?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "I'll keep specific names between me and the locker room. What I'll say is that there are players on this roster who have developed significantly in the offseason and I'm genuinely curious how they respond to game-speed pressure at this level. Tonight was just the first chapter.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "The players who've been here the longest. I know what they're capable of. Now I want to see whether the work of the offseason produced growth or maintenance. The standard is higher this year and that test starts now.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "Every player — honestly. First games tell you things about readiness and temperament that practices can't. I'm learning things about this roster tonight that will shape how I coach this team all season.", 'effect_tags': ['red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "I'm curious about how the newcomers integrate as the season gets harder. When things get difficult — when there's adversity in the room — who are these players? That's what I'm watching for all season.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "The players in new roles. We've made some deployment changes based on how the system evolved. Whether those changes produce the results we projected is one of the more interesting questions this season will answer.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}]},
    {'id': 'season_finale_01', 'category': 'season_phase', 'subcategory': 'season_finale', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'last_regular_season_game', 'filters': {}}, 'weight': 3, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'Last regular season game. What does this team look like compared to where they started?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': 'Significantly more developed, individually and collectively. The gap between who this team was in game one and who they are tonight is visible and real. That growth is what this program is built to produce.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "Harder. This team is harder than they were in October. That's the most important development over a season — the standards held, the work was done, and the team became harder to beat. The record reflects that.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "More experienced and more cohesive. A full season of competition does things to a team that practice can't. This group has been through real things together and it shows.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_up', 'team_chemistry_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "The system command is at a completely different level. Game one, we were installing. Tonight, we're executing. That's the journey of a season within a system — and this team has taken it as far as this point in the year as I've ever seen.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': 'Closer. The relationships in this locker room tonight are deeper than they were in October. You go through a season together — the wins, the losses, the tough moments — and it either brings you together or pulls you apart. This group chose together.', 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'prestige_minor_up', 'fan_interest_up']}]},
    {'id': 'season_finale_02', 'category': 'season_phase', 'subcategory': 'season_finale', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'last_regular_season_game', 'filters': {}}, 'weight': 3, 'player_slot': None, 'text': "As the regular season ends, what's the honest assessment of where this program stands?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': 'Building. The gap between what this program is and what I believe it can become is still significant. The record is what it is. The standard for next season is already higher than it was for this one.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': 'System-capable at a competitive level. The scheme is fully installed and battle-tested. The foundation for what this program can do over the next several years is in place. The next step is recruiting to the system at a higher level.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': 'In a better place than the start of the season. We improved in the areas we targeted and there are clear things to work on in the offseason. This program is on the right trajectory.', 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "The culture is real. That's the honest assessment that matters most to me. When the culture is real, everything else is buildable. This season built on it and next season will build further.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'prestige_minor_up', 'fan_interest_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "More developed than the year before. Individual growth has been real and measurable. That's the foundation. What this program becomes depends on whether we keep developing players at this rate and accelerate it.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}]},
    {'id': 'season_finale_03', 'category': 'season_phase', 'subcategory': 'season_finale', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'last_regular_season_game', 'filters': {}}, 'weight': 3, 'player_slot': None, 'text': "What do you want to take into the postseason from what you've built this year?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "The standard. Everything we've built this year comes down to whether we hold the standard when it matters most. The postseason is that test. I want to take in a team that holds it under maximum pressure.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "The trust. This group has earned something together this season that will matter in the postseason. When the game is on the line and everything is harder than practice, the trust you've built is the only thing you can count on.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "Momentum and confidence. The way we've been playing down the stretch — that's who we want to be in the postseason. We want to carry that energy into what comes next.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_up', 'team_mo_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "Full system command. We're as sharp as we've been all year right now. The goal is to walk into the postseason executing at this level and be able to sustain it against increasingly difficult opponents.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Players playing at the peak of their individual development. The postseason comes down to who's performing at their best when it counts. I want every player on this roster going in with full confidence in their game.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}]},
    {'id': 'season_finale_04', 'category': 'season_phase', 'subcategory': 'season_finale', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'last_regular_season_game', 'filters': {}}, 'weight': 3, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'Any players whose growth this season has exceeded your expectations?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "I'll keep names out of it publicly — nobody needs that kind of comparison. What I'll say is that at least two players on this roster are performing at a level I wasn't certain they'd reach this year. Their development has been genuinely exciting to watch.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "Several. Players who held the standard even when it would have been easier not to — those players grew. You don't always see it in the stats. You see it in what they do when nobody is watching.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'player_em_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "This has been a good development year for several players. I don't want to single anyone out — this team wins and grows together. But yes, I've been pleasantly surprised by the development curve this season.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "The players who surprised me most aren't the ones who got better at basketball — it's the ones who grew as people and as leaders. That growth is what sustains programs through time. I saw more of it this year than I expected.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "Several players whose system execution advanced faster than projected. When a player internalizes the scheme at a rate that surprises even me, it creates possibilities I hadn't planned for. That happened with a few guys this year.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'player_em_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}]},
    {'id': 'must_win_seeding_01', 'category': 'season_phase', 'subcategory': 'must_win_seeding', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'must_win_seeding', 'filters': {}}, 'weight': 3, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'Tonight had seeding implications. How do you prepare a team for a game with that kind of weight attached?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "You don't. You prepare them for the game. If the preparation is right, the weight takes care of itself. I don't want my players playing not to lose — I want them playing to compete. Those require different preparation.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "You focus the week on execution rather than outcome. Players who are thinking about what the win means aren't thinking about the next possession. You eliminate the outcome from the preparation and replace it with the process.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': 'You acknowledge the stakes and then you redirect to what we can control. Seeding matters — we told the team that. Then we focused on preparation and execution, which is all any team can do.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "You frame it as an opportunity, not a pressure point. This team earned the chance to play for better seeding. That's something to be excited about, not afraid of. I want them playing free, not scared.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': 'Individual conversations about what each player needs mentally to perform in a high-stakes environment. Some players elevate under pressure, some tighten. You address both with specific preparation tools.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}]},
    {'id': 'must_win_seeding_02', 'category': 'season_phase', 'subcategory': 'must_win_seeding', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'must_win_seeding', 'filters': {}}, 'weight': 3, 'player_slot': None, 'text': "How much does seeding actually matter to a team's tournament success in your view?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "Seeding matters because path matters. A better seed means a better draw. I'm not going to pretend otherwise. We want the best seed we can earn because we intend to go as far as this program can go.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': 'Practically — it changes the path. A higher seed means theoretically easier early opponents, which means more energy for the games that really matter. We want every advantage the schedule can give us.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "Seeding creates context but doesn't determine outcomes. Any team can lose early with a high seed or go on a run with a lower one. We focus on being as sharp as possible when we get there.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "Less than people think, honestly. Cultures beat seeds. The teams that go deep in tournaments are the teams with genuine trust and competitive will. We're working to be that team, not just a high-seeded one.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "It matters to the extent that it puts individual players in better matchup situations early. When your best players face opponents they're equipped to handle, confidence builds. You want that going into tournament play.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}]},
    {'id': 'must_win_seeding_03', 'category': 'season_phase', 'subcategory': 'must_win_seeding', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'must_win_seeding', 'filters': {}}, 'weight': 3, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'When the stakes are this high, do you see a different version of your team, or are they the same as always?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "The same. That's the point. You build a program so that the stakes don't change the standard. If we need a different team to show up in big games, we haven't built it right. Tonight I saw the team we've been building all year.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': 'Actually — they can be better. When players feel the weight of something that matters, the genuinely competitive ones rise. This team has those players. High stakes sometimes produce the best version of a good team.', 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': 'Mostly the same, with some natural elevation. High stakes sharpen focus in most players. The execution tonight reflected a team that understood the moment and competed accordingly.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "They execute the scheme the same — that's the design. The system provides stability in high-stakes environments because players have concrete assignments regardless of the scoreboard or the significance of the game.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': 'The difference is individual. Some players elevate in high-stakes moments — their instincts sharpen, their decision-making improves. Those are the players I want on the floor in the final minutes of games like tonight.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}]},
    {'id': 'must_win_seeding_04', 'category': 'season_phase', 'subcategory': 'must_win_seeding', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'must_win_seeding', 'filters': {}}, 'weight': 3, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'What message goes to the team heading into the postseason after tonight?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': 'That we earned our spot and now we have to justify it. The postseason is the standard raised as high as it gets. Every expectation we hold in practice and in the regular season now gets tested by the best competition. Be ready.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "That everything we've built this year was for this. The relationships, the trust, the growth — it all comes with us into the postseason. We don't leave anything behind. We go in as who we are and we compete.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "We've earned this and we're ready. Stay with the process, compete hard, and let the preparation we've done all season do its job. One game at a time.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "The system is at its sharpest. We know what we do. We go into the postseason with full command of the scheme. Every opponent we face is going to see us executing at the highest level of the year. That's the message.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': 'That each player has something to prove — not to anyone else, but to themselves. The postseason is where development becomes achievement. This is what the individual work was for. Be ready to show it.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}]},
    {'id': 'clinched_seed_01', 'category': 'season_phase', 'subcategory': 'clinched_seed', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'clinched_conference_seed', 'filters': {}}, 'weight': 3, 'player_slot': None, 'text': "You've clinched your conference tournament seed. What does securing that position mean for this program?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "It means the work earned a position. Not a given, not an accident — earned. Now the job is to justify the seed in the tournament. We've secured where we start. How far we go is still to be determined.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': 'It means this team built something real over the course of the season. A conference seed reflects a full season of competing together. These players deserved to clinch it and they can feel that — they earned every win in that record.', 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'prestige_minor_up', 'fan_interest_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "It's a significant achievement and a meaningful milestone. We've given ourselves a solid position heading into the postseason. Now we focus on being ready to compete when the tournament begins.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_up', 'fan_interest_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "It validates the season's execution. The seed is the most objective measure of how the system performed against conference competition. We've earned something real and now we take that execution into the tournament.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "It reflects the individual development of this entire roster over a full season. A tournament seed is a team achievement — but it's built from individual performances accumulated game by game. This team's players got better and it shows.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'prestige_minor_up', 'fan_interest_up']}]},
    {'id': 'clinched_seed_02', 'category': 'season_phase', 'subcategory': 'clinched_seed', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'clinched_conference_seed', 'filters': {}}, 'weight': 3, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'Now that the seed is secured, how do you manage the remaining regular season games?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "The standard doesn't change. I won't play meaningless basketball in the name of rest management. We compete every game and we prepare to compete every game. The seed is secured — the standard is not.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "You use the remaining games to experiment with elements you want to have available in the tournament. You might try different lineup combinations or introduce counters you've been holding. These games become strategic preparation.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "You balance competition and preparation. You want to stay sharp, get meaningful reps, and protect players from unnecessary injury risk. It's a management exercise as much as a coaching one.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "These are opportunities for the whole roster to compete. Players who've contributed all season deserve these games as much as the starters. We use them to deepen this group's shared experience before the tournament.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': 'Each remaining game is an individual development opportunity. I give players specific assignments and specific challenges rather than just playing to win. The tournament is what matters — these games serve that goal.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}]},
    {'id': 'clinched_seed_03', 'category': 'season_phase', 'subcategory': 'clinched_seed', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'clinched_conference_seed', 'filters': {}}, 'weight': 3, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'What do you know about your first tournament opponent and how does that shape your preparation?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "We're already building the scouting report. The tournament preparation begins now — scheme adjustments, specific actions to target, defensive assignments. We use every day we have.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "We scout everyone regardless of seed or reputation. Every opponent in this tournament can beat us if we're not prepared. We prepare with the same intensity for every matchup.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "We start building the film package now. The sooner we can get our players familiar with the opponent, the more comfortable they'll be when the game starts.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': 'We prepare together. The film sessions are collective — every player understands the opponent, not just the starters. In tournament basketball, contributions can come from anywhere. Everyone needs to be ready.', 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "We match our players' individual strengths against their specific defensive vulnerabilities. Matchup advantages in tournament games are how lower seeds upset higher ones. We're building a plan around the advantages we have.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}]},
    {'id': 'clinched_seed_04', 'category': 'season_phase', 'subcategory': 'clinched_seed', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'clinched_conference_seed', 'filters': {}}, 'weight': 3, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'What does this program need to do to make a real run in this tournament?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "Play for each other without reservation. Tournament basketball is the moment where all the trust and relationships either matter or they don't. Teams that go deep in tournaments are teams that genuinely compete for each other when everything is on the line.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_major_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "Hold the standard for five consecutive days of competition at maximum intensity. That's what a tournament run requires. We've held it for individual games. Now we have to hold it for a gauntlet. That tests everything.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'prestige_major_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': 'Execute consistently, stay healthy, and compete in the close games. Tournament runs require all three. We have the ability. Whether we put it together at the right time is what the tournament will tell us.', 'effect_tags': ['prestige_major_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': 'Execute the scheme with complete precision against elite competition. Tournament opponents will be better prepared for us than regular season opponents. Our system is deep enough to compete — but the execution level has to rise to match the challenge.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_major_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Individual players performing at their highest level simultaneously. Tournament runs don't happen because of game plans — they happen because three or four players peak at exactly the right moment. My job is to have every player ready for that moment.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'prestige_major_up', 'fan_interest_up']}]},
    {'id': 'vanilla_01', 'category': 'vanilla', 'subcategory': 'vanilla', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'always', 'filters': {}}, 'weight': 1, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'Coach, how do you evaluate where this team is?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "Honestly. There are things we do well and things that aren't at the standard. We know the difference and we're working on the gap. That's where we are.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "We evaluate against the system's benchmarks — execution rate, shot quality, defensive adherence. By those measures, we're further along in some areas than others. The film is pretty honest about where we stand.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "Developing. There are good things happening and things to improve. That's probably true of every team at every point in the season.", 'effect_tags': ['red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': 'I evaluate this team by who they are in the locker room as much as what they do on the court. By that measure — I feel good. The basketball reflects who they are and who they are is pretty good.', 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Player by player. The team's trajectory is the sum of individual trajectories. Most of them are moving in the right direction. A few have specific things to address. That's where we are.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up']}]},
    {'id': 'vanilla_02', 'category': 'vanilla', 'subcategory': 'vanilla', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'always', 'filters': {}}, 'weight': 1, 'player_slot': None, 'text': "What's the biggest area of improvement you're still looking for from this group?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "Consistency. This team is capable of performing at a high level — they prove it in stretches. Sustaining that level for forty minutes, every game, is what separates good teams from great ones. We're not there yet.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "Playing for each other in the difficult moments. When things are going well, this team plays great together. When it gets hard — when the crowd is against us or we're down — that's where I want to see more collective response.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': 'Late-game execution. You can compete well for most of forty minutes and still let things slip in the final possessions — closing that gap is the next level for this group.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "Half-court offense command. We're solid in transition but our half-court execution still has too much variance. When the scheme is running cleanly, we're hard to guard. When it breaks down, we're too predictable.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Shot creation off the dribble for two or three specific players. The development work is happening but I need to see it translate more consistently in live game situations. That's the next unlock for this roster.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}]},
    {'id': 'vanilla_03', 'category': 'vanilla', 'subcategory': 'vanilla', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'always', 'filters': {}}, 'weight': 1, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'How do you keep the team focused through the grind of a long season?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "Structure. The routine doesn't change whether the result was comfortable or the game came down to the wire. Consistent preparation creates consistent focus. When players know exactly what to expect every day, the grind becomes manageable.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "Standards. When you hold the standard regardless of the record or the moment in the season, focus is a natural byproduct. You don't need to motivate players who know exactly what's expected of them.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "Honesty about where we are and where we're going. Players stay focused when they understand the purpose behind the work. We try to keep that purpose clear throughout the season.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "Each other. The best thing about a long season is that it deepens relationships. Players who genuinely care about the people they're competing with find motivation in that. You don't need external motivation when the internal motivation is real.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Individual goals. Every player in this program has specific things they're working toward. When you have personal development targets that you're making progress on, the daily work has meaning regardless of the record.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}]},
    {'id': 'vanilla_04', 'category': 'vanilla', 'subcategory': 'vanilla', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'always', 'filters': {}}, 'weight': 1, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'What does preparation look like for this program in a typical game week?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "Day one is film — our own performance first, then the opponent. Day two is scheme installation against their specific actions. Day three is execution emphasis. Game day is mental preparation and trust. The structure doesn't vary much because consistency of preparation produces consistency of performance.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "Hard practices Monday and Tuesday, specific opponent preparation Wednesday, sharpen and rest Thursday. Game day is about executing what we've prepared. The week is the same every week. That predictability is intentional.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': 'Film, practice, and mental preparation. We try to give players a clear picture of the opponent and clear goals for what we want to do. Then we trust the preparation when the game comes.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "We build in time that's not about basketball. Team meals, film sessions that feel more like conversations than lectures, moments where the players just spend time together. The basketball preparation is important. So is building the relationships that make the basketball better.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': 'Individual skill work is built into every day. Before we even get to team preparation, every player has a personal development block. Their individual game gets better every week regardless of what the opponent forces us to install.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}]},
    {'id': 'vanilla_05', 'category': 'vanilla', 'subcategory': 'vanilla', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'always', 'filters': {}}, 'weight': 1, 'player_slot': None, 'text': "What's your coaching philosophy in a sentence or two?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': 'Hold the standard. Every day, every player, every possession. When you do that consistently, everything else — wins, development, culture — follows.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': 'Build a system that makes every player better and every opponent uncomfortable. When the scheme is right and the players trust it, the game becomes simple. I try to create that simplicity.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "Compete every day and take care of each other. The wins come from the competition and the longevity comes from the care. That's as simple as I can make it.", 'effect_tags': ['red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "Build people first, players second. When you invest in who these young men are becoming, the basketball reflects that investment. You can't separate the person from the player and I don't try to.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': 'Every player deserves to find out what their ceiling is. My job is to create the conditions where that ceiling gets discovered and exceeded. Everything else — wins, culture, program growth — follows from developing players at the highest possible level.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up']}]},
    {'id': 'vanilla_06', 'category': 'vanilla', 'subcategory': 'vanilla', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'always', 'filters': {}}, 'weight': 1, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'How much attention do you pay to what other programs in your conference are doing?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "Enough to know our opponents. Not enough to let it shape what we do. This program doesn't build its identity around what everyone else is doing. We build it around our own standard.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': 'Significant attention. Conference scouting shapes our scheme evolution — what actions are being run, what defenses are being deployed, where the trends are going. You have to know the landscape to design a system that beats it.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "Enough to stay informed. You want to know what's working in your conference and what you'll face. But you can't coach other teams' programs — you can only coach your own.", 'effect_tags': ['red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "Less than people might expect. I'm more concerned with what we're building here than what anyone else is building. The programs I admire most are the ones that know exactly who they are. I'm trying to build that.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': 'Primarily from a development standpoint — what are other programs producing and how are their players being developed? That informs recruiting conversations and our own developmental model. The competitive piece is secondary.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up']}]},
    {'id': 'vanilla_07', 'category': 'vanilla', 'subcategory': 'vanilla', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'always', 'filters': {}}, 'weight': 1, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'How do you define a successful season for this program?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "We compete at the highest level we're capable of every single game. If we do that, the wins take care of themselves. A season where we held the standard — that's a successful season.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "Reaching full system command by the back half of the schedule and competing in the postseason. The program metrics follow from that. If we're executing the scheme at the level it's designed for by February, we're having a successful season.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "Improvement, competitiveness, and a postseason opportunity. Those three things, in that order. The specifics of where we finish matter less than the direction we're moving.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': 'When the players who were here look back on this year with pride — not just for what they accomplished but for who they were and how they treated each other. I want this to be a season they talk about for the right reasons.', 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': 'Every player on this roster finishing the season better than they started it — measurably, verifiably better. If every player takes a step forward individually, the collective results reflect that and the season is a success by any measure.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'prestige_minor_up']}]},
    {'id': 'vanilla_08', 'category': 'vanilla', 'subcategory': 'vanilla', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'always', 'filters': {}}, 'weight': 1, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'What do you enjoy most about coaching at this level?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "The competition. When two prepared teams meet on a floor and the best one wins — there's nothing like it. The stakes are real at this level and I thrive on that.", 'effect_tags': ['fight_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': 'The chess match. At this level, every opponent has a plan and you have to outprepare and outscheme them. The tactical challenge is constant and endlessly interesting. I love solving the problem.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "Watching players grow. The basketball is the vehicle. What I enjoy most is seeing a young person become better at something they care deeply about. That happens at this level in a way you can't manufacture.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "The relationships. I'll be honest with you — twenty years from now, I won't remember most individual scores. But I'll remember the people. The relationships I build in these locker rooms are what make this job worth it.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "The moment a player exceeds their own expectations. When a player does something they didn't believe they could do — and you can see it in their face — that's the reason I coach. Nothing competes with that.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'red_herring']}]},
    {'id': 'vanilla_09', 'category': 'vanilla', 'subcategory': 'vanilla', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'always', 'filters': {}}, 'weight': 1, 'player_slot': None, 'text': "What's the biggest misconception people have about what coaching this program actually involves?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "That it's primarily about the game. The game is maybe twenty percent of it. The rest is standards, accountability, preparation, and doing that work every single day without exception. People see the game. They don't see what builds it.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "That schemes come from inspiration. The system is built through thousands of hours of film, research, and iteration. There's nothing romantic about it — it's engineering. Most people underestimate how technical the preparation actually is.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "That it's glamorous. Most of it is early mornings, late nights, and a lot of problem-solving that never makes the highlights. The visible part is a fraction of the actual job.", 'effect_tags': ['red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "That the locker room takes care of itself. Culture is active and intentional work. The best locker rooms I've been part of didn't happen organically — they were built deliberately, conversation by conversation, decision by decision.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "That development happens in games. Games reveal development — they don't create it. The real work happens in individual sessions, in the weight room, in film study. People see the production. They don't see the thousands of hours that made it possible.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'red_herring']}]},
    {'id': 'vanilla_10', 'category': 'vanilla', 'subcategory': 'vanilla', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'always', 'filters': {}}, 'weight': 1, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'How important is home court advantage to this program?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': 'Significant but not decisive. The best teams protect home court by playing to their standard, not by depending on the crowd. We want to make this building a problem for opponents — but that comes from execution, not atmosphere alone.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "It matters enormously to our players. When this community shows up and is loud and behind us — our guys feed off that energy in a real way. Fan support isn't just noise. It's fuel. We try to honor it by competing every minute they're there.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fan_interest_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "Real but not something you can rely on. You want home court advantage and you want to use it. But good teams win on the road too. We try to build a program that competes wherever we're playing.", 'effect_tags': ['fan_interest_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': 'It affects opponent preparation — they see a different defensive atmosphere and a more vocal crowd. From a scheme standpoint, we try to build actions that are harder to execute in noise. The home court advantage should factor into how you design plays.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fan_interest_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "For some players it's enormous and for others it barely registers. Part of individual development is learning to perform at the same level regardless of environment. The home crowd is an advantage. Being able to play without it is a skill.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'fan_interest_up']}]},
    {'id': 'vanilla_11', 'category': 'vanilla', 'subcategory': 'vanilla', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'always', 'filters': {}}, 'weight': 1, 'player_slot': None, 'text': "What's your approach to game-day preparation — what does your routine look like?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "It doesn't vary. Same schedule, same sequence, same expectations. I've coached long enough to know that routine is the enemy of anxiety. When everything is predictable before the game, players can focus completely on competing.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "Film in the morning — focused specifically on the opponent's tendencies in game situations. Walkthrough at shootaround to make the assignments physical and not just mental. Then you trust the preparation and let the players play.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': 'Light preparation in the morning, mental focus in the afternoon, and then letting players settle into their individual routines. Coaches who over-prepare players on game day tend to overthink them. You want them ready, not loaded.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': 'I focus on where the group is — individually and collectively. Game-day preparation is partly physical, partly technical, and mostly about making sure every player takes the floor in the right frame of mind.', 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': 'Individual check-ins are the most important part of my game-day. I want to know where each player is mentally before tip-off. The players who need a conversation get one. The ones who need space get space. You learn which is which over a season.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}]},
    {'id': 'vanilla_12', 'category': 'vanilla', 'subcategory': 'vanilla', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'always', 'filters': {}}, 'weight': 1, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'How do you handle disagreements with your players about role or playing time?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "Directly. Playing time reflects performance and standard. If a player disagrees, we sit down and go through the film together. The film doesn't argue back. When the reasoning is clear and consistent, most disagreements resolve themselves.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "With honesty and specificity. I tell every player exactly what I see and exactly what they need to do to earn more. No vague answers, no false promises. Players who know specifically what they're working toward handle role discussions much better than players who are guessing.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "You listen first. Sometimes the player sees something I haven't. After listening, you share your perspective honestly. Disagreements are part of coaching. The goal is that both people walk away with clarity.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "Through relationship. When a player trusts that you're in their corner — that your decisions come from wanting what's best for them — the disagreement conversation is very different than when that trust isn't there. I invest in the relationship before those conversations happen.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "By tying the role to the scheme's requirements. When a player understands that the system needs specific things from specific people, the role feels less personal. It's not about who I like — it's about what the scheme requires. That framing takes a lot of the emotion out of it.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'player_em_up']}]},
    {'id': 'vanilla_13', 'category': 'vanilla', 'subcategory': 'vanilla', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'always', 'filters': {}}, 'weight': 1, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'What do you look for in the opponents you face — is there a style that gives this team the most trouble?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "Teams with multiple scheme answers — opponents who can adjust at halftime and show you something different. That's the hardest thing to prepare for. You can't install a counter for every possibility, so you have to trust your principles when they adjust.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "Physical teams that match our intensity. The tactical stuff we can prepare for. When you face a team that matches you physically and competes just as hard, that's where you find out what your program is really made of.", 'effect_tags': ['fight_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "Every team presents different challenges. I'd rather not tip our hand about specific styles. What I'd say is that the best opponents are usually the ones who are best prepared. Preparation beats style every time.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "Teams with genuine trust and chemistry are the hardest to beat. You can scheme against talent. You can't fully scheme against five players who genuinely play for each other. That kind of team finds ways to win that you can't anticipate.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Teams with multiple individual threats. When every player on the floor can score, you can't key on one person. That spreads your individual defenders thin and creates problems across the whole roster. It's the matchup that demands the most from our individual development.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}]},
    {'id': 'vanilla_14', 'category': 'vanilla', 'subcategory': 'vanilla', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'always', 'filters': {}}, 'weight': 1, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'How do you think about the relationship between this program and the fan community?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "It's a real relationship, not a transactional one. This community has invested in this program emotionally and we have a responsibility to that investment. I want the fans to feel like they're part of what we're building — because they are.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fan_interest_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "The fans deserve a program that competes at the highest level every night. That's what we owe them — not speeches, not promises, not feel-good moments. Results from hard work. When we deliver that, the relationship takes care of itself.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fan_interest_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': 'Important. Fan support matters to our players and to the energy in our building. We want to give people a reason to show up and we want to honor their presence when they do.', 'effect_tags': ['fan_interest_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': 'The fan base grows when the program produces consistently. Consistency — in results, in approach, in how we represent this institution — builds the kind of following that sustains a program. I think about that relationship in the long term.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fan_interest_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Our players draw energy from the fan base and the fan base invests in watching our players develop. When those two things are working together — when fans are following a player's journey and the player knows it — something special happens.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'fan_interest_up']}]},
    {'id': 'vanilla_15', 'category': 'vanilla', 'subcategory': 'vanilla', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'always', 'filters': {}}, 'weight': 1, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'Is there anything about how this team is perceived externally that you feel is inaccurate?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': 'The perception that results define who we are. External perception is a lagging indicator. The people who watch us play see a snapshot. What this program is — the standard, the work, the character — is built in between the snapshots.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "That we're defined by our record. The people in our locker room know what this program is about and what we're building. Some weeks the record reflects it, some weeks it doesn't. The record is not the program.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "There's always some gap between perception and reality. I try not to worry about it too much — results tend to correct perception over time. We focus on the work and let the results do the talking.", 'effect_tags': ['red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "That we're one-dimensional. The scheme gets labeled sometimes based on what opponents have seen us do most. What they haven't seen is the depth and the counters we haven't needed to use yet. The full picture is more interesting than the label.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "That our players are interchangeable. Every player in this program is being developed as an individual with specific strengths and specific growth areas. We're not a system that produces generic outputs. We develop people.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'red_herring']}]},
    {'id': 'vanilla_16', 'category': 'vanilla', 'subcategory': 'vanilla', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'always', 'filters': {}}, 'weight': 1, 'player_slot': None, 'text': "What does this program's identity look like on defense?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "Hard and consistent. We contest every shot, we compete for every rebound, and we make it unpleasant to play against us. That's not a scheme — it's an attitude. You build that in practice every single day.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': 'Structured and adaptive. We have a base defense with specific principles, and we build opponent-specific adjustments on top of that. The identity is the principles — read the ball, stop dribble penetration, contest without fouling. Everything else builds from there.', 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "Committed. We want to be a team that defends for forty minutes at a high level. We're better at it some nights than others, but the commitment to it is non-negotiable.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "Collective. The best defensive teams protect each other — they cover for each other's mistakes and they compete harder when a teammate gets beat. That collective defensive identity is something we build through culture, not just through scheme.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Individual ownership. Every player is responsible for their defensive assignment and held accountable for it on film. When players take personal ownership of their defensive performance, the collective defense is dramatically better. That's the identity we build.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}]},
    {'id': 'vanilla_17', 'category': 'vanilla', 'subcategory': 'vanilla', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'always', 'filters': {}}, 'weight': 1, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'How do you approach the mental health and wellbeing of your players?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': "With genuine care. Basketball is what we do together — it's not who these young men are. When a player is struggling with something beyond basketball, this program supports them. That support is not conditional on their performance. It's unconditional.", 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "As a development priority. Mental health directly affects performance — focus, decision-making, resilience under pressure. We've invested in resources and built conversations about mental wellbeing into how we operate. A player who is healthy mentally develops faster.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "Seriously. We have resources available and we try to create an environment where players feel comfortable using them. The pressure these athletes are under is real and we don't minimize it.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "The same way I approach everything — with standards and honest conversations. The standard in this program is that you ask for help when you need it. That's not weakness. It's intelligence. I model that myself.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'player_em_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "Structurally. We build check-ins into the weekly routine, we have support staff available, and we monitor for signs that a player needs more than what basketball can provide. It's part of how the program is designed to function.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'player_em_up']}]},
    {'id': 'vanilla_18', 'category': 'vanilla', 'subcategory': 'vanilla', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'always', 'filters': {}}, 'weight': 1, 'player_slot': None, 'text': "What separates the coaches you've learned the most from?", 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "Relentlessness of standard. The coaches who shaped me never accepted less than what they believed was possible — from their players, from their staff, from themselves. That relentlessness is something I've tried to build into everything I do.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "Intellectual curiosity. The best coaches I learned from were constantly studying — film, other sports, organizational theory. They never stopped trying to understand the game better. That curiosity is something I've tried to carry.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': 'The ability to connect with different kinds of players. The coaches who had the biggest impact on me could reach every type of person. That versatility — knowing when to push and when to support — is the hardest thing to develop.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': 'How they made people feel. The coaches who shaped me most were the ones whose players would run through a wall for them — not out of fear but out of genuine belief that the coach was in their corner. That relationship quality is what I study most.', 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "The belief they had in players before the players had it in themselves. The coaches who influenced me most saw things in people that hadn't been revealed yet. That ability — to see potential and to call it out — is the most powerful thing a coach can do.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'red_herring']}]},
    {'id': 'vanilla_19', 'category': 'vanilla', 'subcategory': 'vanilla', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'always', 'filters': {}}, 'weight': 1, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'What role does film study play in how this program prepares?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "Central. Everything starts on film. Our own execution first — every game, every possession, graded against the system's principles. Then the opponent. The film room is where the game is actually coached. What happens on the floor is the execution of what was built in that room.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "Essential and non-negotiable. Players who don't study film don't understand what I'm asking from them. The film is the most honest conversation a coach and player can have. You can't argue with what you see on the screen.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "Significant. We use film to prepare for opponents and to evaluate our own performance. Players who engage seriously with film tend to develop faster. It's one of the best tools we have.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': 'We try to make film sessions collaborative rather than lectures. When players are studying film together and arriving at conclusions together, the buy-in is dramatically higher than when a coach tells them what they did wrong. That collaborative approach is part of the culture.', 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'discipline_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': 'Individual film sessions are as important as team sessions. Every player gets personal film time — their specific possessions, their specific development areas. That individual attention is where the real growth happens. Team film sets the context. Individual film drives the development.', 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'discipline_up']}]},
    {'id': 'vanilla_20', 'category': 'vanilla', 'subcategory': 'vanilla', 'tier': 1, 'requires_tracking': False, 'trigger': {'condition': 'always', 'filters': {}}, 'weight': 1, 'player_slot': None, 'text': 'What would you want this program to be known for, ultimately?', 'answers': [{'letter': 'A', 'archetype': 'authoritarian', 'text': "Hardness. I want this program to be known as the program that was always prepared, always competitive, and never beaten because it wasn't ready. That reputation takes years to build and it's what I'm working toward every day.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'fight_up', 'fan_interest_up']}, {'letter': 'B', 'archetype': 'systems_coach', 'text': "Consistency of execution. Programs that execute their scheme at a high level over a long period of time become benchmarks for the sport. That's the legacy I'm trying to build — a system that produces results you can count on.", 'effect_tags': ['discipline_up', 'prestige_minor_up', 'fan_interest_up']}, {'letter': 'C', 'archetype': 'neutral', 'text': "Competitiveness and integrity. A program that competed at a high level and did it the right way. That combination is rarer than it should be. I'd be proud of that legacy.", 'effect_tags': ['prestige_minor_up', 'fan_interest_up', 'red_herring']}, {'letter': 'D', 'archetype': 'culture_builder', 'text': 'The people it produced. Not the wins — the people. I want players who came through this program to be better people because they were here. Better teammates, better leaders, better human beings. The basketball is the vehicle. The people are the point.', 'effect_tags': ['team_chemistry_up', 'player_em_up', 'fan_interest_up']}, {'letter': 'E', 'archetype': 'player_maximizer', 'text': "Development. I want this program to be known as the place where players became who they were capable of becoming. Where talent walked in as potential and walked out as achievement. That's the program I'm trying to build and that's the legacy I'm after.", 'effect_tags': ['player_em_up', 'prestige_minor_up', 'fan_interest_up']}]},

]
